window.CHINTHE_KB={"groups":[{"id":"wrestling_mat","name":"Wrestling: Mat Work & Rides","anchor":"referee_position","desc":"Breakdowns, rides, turns and escapes from the bottom — folkstyle and freestyle par terre.","after":"standing","include":["mat_return"]},{"id":"judo_ground","name":"Judo: Pins & Ne-Waza","anchor":"osaekomi_rules","desc":"Hold-downs, turnovers and collar chokes — judo's groundwork and its bridge to BJJ.","after":"judo","include":["kesa_gatame","judo_bjj_bridge"]},{"id":"gi_guard","name":"Gi Guards & Grips","anchor":"spider_guard","desc":"Guards built on sleeves, collars and lapels — spider, lasso, De La Riva and the lapel games.","after":"open","include":[]},{"id":"striking","name":"MMA: Striking","anchor":"fighting_stance","desc":"Stance, punches, kicks, knees, elbows and the defence that keeps you safe getting to the clinch.","after":"concepts","include":[]},{"id":"mma","name":"MMA: Cage & Ground","anchor":"cage_clinch","desc":"Wrestling against the fence, getting up, ground-and-pound posture and submissions with strikes in play.","after":"striking","include":["underhooks_pummel","whizzer","technical_standup","double_leg","rnc","guillotine","arm_triangle","kimura","back_control"]},{"id":"transitions","name":"Back Takes & Transitions","anchor":"arm_drag_back","desc":"The movements between positions: back takes, rolls, drags and getting up.","after":"back","include":["wrestle_up","body_triangle"]},{"id":"muay_thai","name":"Muay Thai: Art of Eight Limbs","anchor":"muay_thai_stance","desc":"Fists, elbows, knees and shins — the Thai stance, clinch, kicks and the way fights are scored.","after":"mma","include":["teep","leg_kick","body_kick","head_kick","thai_clinch","straight_knee","flying_knee","horizontal_elbow","spinning_back_elbow","checking_kicks","jab","cross","hook_punch","uppercut","blocking_covering"]},{"id":"lethwei","name":"Lethwei: Burmese Boxing","anchor":"lethwei_rules","desc":"Myanmar's bare-knuckle art of nine limbs: fists, elbows, knees, feet and the head.","after":"muay_thai","include":["teep","leg_kick","body_kick","thai_clinch","straight_knee","horizontal_elbow","checking_kicks","jab","cross","hook_punch","uppercut"]}],"entries":[{"id":"stance_motion","cat":"concept","name":"Stance & Motion","tagline":"Every takedown and every defence starts here. A bad stance loses before the first tie.","tags":["Wrestling","Foundation","Standing"],"objective":"Stay low enough to shoot and defend, balanced enough to move in any direction, with your hands in front of your hips.","mechanics":"Feet about shoulder width or slightly wider, lead foot slightly forward in a staggered stance or level in a square stance. Knees bent, hips down, back straight, head up and in front of your knees. Elbows tight to the ribs, hands in front — they are your first line of defence. Move with short steps; never cross your feet or bring them together. Circle away from their power side and change levels with your legs, not by bending at the waist.","defense":"A good opponent tests your stance with snaps and ties: if your head drops below your hips they snap you down, if you stand tall they shoot under you.","mistake":"Bending at the waist to get low. Your head drops, your hips go back, and you are already in a front headlock.","drill":"Stance-motion shadow drill: 3 × 1 minute. Partner points a direction, you move there in stance, then level-change on a clap. Keep your head above your knees the whole time.","groups":["standing","concepts"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Wrestling Stance"],"rel":["wrestling_shot","hand_fighting","sprawl"]}},{"id":"collar_tie","cat":"position","name":"Collar Tie","tagline":"The most common tie in wrestling: it controls their head, and where the head goes the body follows.","tags":["Clinch","Tie-Up","Snap Down"],"objective":"Use the collar tie to move their head, break their posture and create reactions you can attack — snap downs, duck unders and shots.","mechanics":"Cup the back of the neck with your palm, elbow pointing down and in front of their chest so it doubles as a frame. Your other hand controls their opposite elbow or wrist. Pull the head down and toward you in short, sharp movements; when they pull back up, go with it into a shot. Keep your own head tight to theirs to stop them returning the tie. The inside elbow position on their chest stops them squaring up.","defense":"They post on your chest, pummel inside to win their own tie, or lift the elbow and duck under. Strong opponents simply hold posture and wait for you to overcommit.","mistake":"Hanging on the tie with a straight arm. You give them a lever to drag or duck, and you lose the elbow frame that protects your legs.","drill":"Collar-tie snap-and-react: partner holds posture; snap 3 times, on the third they come up and you shoot. 3 × 10 reps each side.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Head Tie","Collar-and-Elbow"],"rel":["snap_down","duck_under","hand_fighting","russian_tie"]}},{"id":"russian_tie","cat":"position","name":"Russian Tie","tagline":"Two of your arms on one of theirs. They can't fight it with one hand, and every leg is open behind it.","tags":["Clinch","Tie-Up","Two-on-One"],"objective":"Isolate one arm with both of yours, pin it to your chest, and use the angle to shoot high crotch, single leg or go behind.","mechanics":"Grab their wrist with your same-side hand. Your other arm goes over the top of their upper arm and your hand grips just above their elbow, hugging the arm to your chest. Drop your hip into their side and lean your weight onto the arm so they carry you. From here, step to their back side for a go-behind, drop under the arm to their near leg for a high crotch or single, or drag the arm across for the back.","defense":"They turn into you and punch their free hand across to break the grip, or they circle away and lift the trapped elbow. Good wrestlers counter by attacking your exposed legs with their free side.","mistake":"Standing square while holding the tie. Without your hip in their side and your weight on the arm, it is just a grip and they strip it.","drill":"Russian tie entries: from a neutral wrist grip, win the tie, then hit the go-behind, the high crotch and the drag in sequence. 3 × 5 of each.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Two-on-One","Arm Drag Tie"],"rel":["arm_drag_standing","high_crotch","snatch_single","arm_drag_back"]}},{"id":"underhooks_pummel","cat":"position","name":"Underhooks & Pummelling","tagline":"In the clinch, the inside arm wins. Pummelling is the fight for that inside position.","tags":["Clinch","Body Lock","Underhook"],"objective":"Win the underhook so you control their posture and hips. Two underhooks lock the body for trips, throws and back takes.","mechanics":"Underhook: your arm goes under their armpit, hand on their shoulder blade or upper back, elbow tight to their side. Lift the elbow to turn their shoulder up and drive your head to their chest or jaw on the same side. To pummel, slide your hand inside theirs along your own chest, swim it under their arm and turn your hips into them at the same time. With double underhooks, lock your hands behind their lower back and pull their hips into yours.","defense":"They whizzer the underhook, pummel back inside, or get their hips square and away so the underhook loses its lift.","mistake":"Reaching for the underhook with your arm while your hips stay back. The hips have to come with the arm or they simply re-pummel.","drill":"Continuous pummelling: chest to chest, both swim for the inside. 3 × 1 minute, then add a rule: on double underhooks, finish a trip.","groups":["standing","mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Over-Under","Double Underhooks","Pummel"],"rel":["body_lock_takedown","whizzer","clinch_entry","cage_clinch"]}},{"id":"whizzer","cat":"defence","name":"Whizzer","tagline":"The overhook that kills underhooks and single legs. Heavy hips and a turning shoulder.","tags":["Clinch","Takedown Defence","Overhook"],"objective":"Stop their underhook or leg attack by overhooking their arm, driving your hip down onto them and turning them away from your legs.","mechanics":"Wrap your arm over their underhooking arm, as high as you can toward their shoulder. Clamp it tight to your side. Drive your hip into them and down — your weight goes into their shoulder, not just your arm. Turn your chest away and point your near hip at the mat. Use your free hand to block their head or push it to the mat. Against a single leg, keep the whizzer heavy while you circle and step your trapped leg out.","defense":"They come up into you to take away your hip pressure, switch to a double leg, or run their feet behind you for the back.","mistake":"A whizzer with only the arm. Without the hip driving down, you hang on their shoulder and they finish.","drill":"Whizzer reaction drill: partner takes a single leg or underhook on a signal; you sink the whizzer and turn the hip in one motion. 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["standing","defence","mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Overhook Defence"],"rel":["underhooks_pummel","single_leg_defence","sprawl","fence_defence"]}},{"id":"high_crotch","cat":"takedown","name":"High Crotch","tagline":"A single leg that lands with your head inside and your hips under theirs. Hard to sprawl on when it's hit right.","tags":["Wrestling","Single Leg","Level Change"],"objective":"Attack their lead leg with your head on the inside, then finish by running the pipe, switching to a double, or lifting.","mechanics":"Off a set-up that raises their arms, level-change and step your lead foot between their feet. Your head goes on the inside of their thigh, tight to their chest. Your inside arm wraps deep behind their knee, your outside hand grips behind their thigh or knee. Bring your hips under you — your back leg steps up so you are on your feet, not on your knee. Finish by turning the corner toward their back, switching to the double, or lifting the leg high and turning them.","defense":"They sprawl hard and whizzer, crossface to turn your head out, or push your head down to the mat.","mistake":"Leaving your head outside or dropping it below their hips. With the head out they whizzer you; with it low they sprawl over the top.","drill":"Shadow and partner entries: 3 × 10 high crotch penetrations off a collar-tie snap. Finish the last 5 with a run-the-pipe.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Inside Single"],"rel":["single_leg_wrestling","double_leg","russian_tie","single_leg_finishes"]}},{"id":"low_single","cat":"takedown","name":"Low Single","tagline":"A fast shot at the lead ankle from distance. Low, quick, and awkward to sprawl on.","tags":["Wrestling","Single Leg","Shot"],"objective":"Shoot under their hands to the ankle, pull it to your chest and come up to finish before they can reset their stance.","mechanics":"From a long distance, drop low and step your knee toward their lead foot, sliding your head to the outside of their knee. Both hands grab the ankle and heel. Pull the foot to your chest and turn your head into their shin so they cannot push it down. Step up onto your feet, keep the ankle tight to your hip and either drive into the knee or lift the leg and pivot to finish.","defense":"They sprawl the leg back, push your head down with a crossface, or kick the leg free before you stand.","mistake":"Staying on your knees after the catch. You win the ankle but they sprawl on you; come up to your feet fast.","drill":"Low single on a reaction: partner steps forward; you sweep the lead foot. 3 × 8. Add a finish on the last 3.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Sweep Single","Ankle Single"],"rel":["single_leg_wrestling","ankle_pick","high_crotch"]}},{"id":"outside_single","cat":"takedown","name":"Outside Single","tagline":"The single leg with your head outside their hip. Easier to reach, but you must finish before the whizzer.","tags":["Wrestling","Single Leg"],"objective":"Capture the leg from the outside angle and finish quickly by running the pipe or driving across their body.","mechanics":"Step to the outside of their lead leg and drop your level. Your head goes outside their hip, pressed tight into their side. Both arms wrap the leg, hands locked behind the knee. Stand up with the leg between your thighs or on your hip. Finish by turning away and running the pipe, or by driving your head into their hip while you pull the leg so they fall back.","defense":"The whizzer is the main counter — they overhook your near arm and drive your head down. They may also hop and turn to face you.","mistake":"Letting the head drift away from their hip. That gap is where the whizzer and the crossface come in.","drill":"Finish-from-catch: start already holding an outside single; partner whizzers at 50%. Finish 3 different ways. 3 × 5.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Head-Outside Single"],"rel":["single_leg_wrestling","single_leg_finishes","snatch_single"]}},{"id":"snatch_single","cat":"takedown","name":"Snatch Single","tagline":"A single leg taken without shooting. You reach down and pull the leg up off a tie.","tags":["Wrestling","Single Leg","No Shot"],"objective":"Catch their lead leg from a standing tie-up when their weight is off it, and lift it before they react.","mechanics":"From a collar tie, snap their head to load weight onto their lead leg, then release. As they step back to re-balance, drop your inside hand behind their knee and snatch the leg up to your hip in one motion. Keep the collar tie or wrist control with the other hand. Once the leg is up, turn them with the head control or run the pipe.","defense":"They keep their weight on the back leg and step back, or sprawl and whizzer as soon as your hand touches the leg.","mistake":"Reaching for the leg when their weight is on it. Time it to the step, not to your own plan.","drill":"Partner walks forward and back in stance; snatch the lead leg every time it lightens. 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","rel":["single_leg_wrestling","russian_tie","collar_tie"]}},{"id":"single_leg_finishes","cat":"takedown","name":"Single Leg Finishes","tagline":"Catching the leg is half the takedown. These are the ways to put them on the mat.","tags":["Wrestling","Single Leg","Finishing"],"objective":"Have three finishes ready so you can change direction when they defend the first.","mechanics":"Run the pipe: hold the leg low on your hip, turn your back toward them and drive in a circle away while dropping your outside knee, pulling the leg out from under them. Shelf: lift the leg high onto your shoulder or chest, then drive forward into their hip or sweep the standing foot. Dump: with the leg on your hip, step behind their standing leg and turn to drop them backward. Keep your head up and your hips under you throughout.","defense":"They hop, whizzer, and fight your hands. Each finish beats a different defence: run the pipe beats hopping, shelf beats the whizzer, the dump beats a heavy lean forward.","mistake":"Holding the leg and squeezing while waiting. Every second on a single leg is time for their whizzer and hand fight.","drill":"Single-leg finish ladder: partner defends with a different reaction each rep. 3 × 6, change finish to match the reaction.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Run the Pipe","Shelf","Dump"],"rel":["single_leg_wrestling","high_crotch","outside_single","single_leg_defence"]}},{"id":"duck_under","cat":"takedown","name":"Duck Under","tagline":"Duck under their arm and come out behind them. The pay-off for a collar tie fight.","tags":["Wrestling","Go-Behind","Clinch"],"objective":"Use their arm on your neck as a doorway: pop their elbow up, duck your head under it and take their back standing.","mechanics":"From a collar tie exchange, push their elbow up with your hand or shoulder while you level-change. Step your near foot deep between their feet and duck your head under their armpit, keeping your head tight to their side. Pull the arm over your head with your far hand. Step around behind them, lock your hands around their waist and finish with a mat return or trip.","defense":"They drop the elbow tight to their side, pull the arm back, or turn with you so you never reach the back.","mistake":"Ducking without stepping. Your head goes under but your feet stay out front and they just face you again.","drill":"Collar tie to duck under: 3 × 8 each side. Partner gives the tie; you pop, step and lock behind.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","rel":["collar_tie","arm_drag_standing","spin_behind"]}},{"id":"fireman_carry","cat":"takedown","name":"Fireman's Carry","tagline":"A big-scoring drop throw: their arm over your neck, your arm between their legs, and over they go.","tags":["Wrestling","Throw","Arm Control"],"objective":"Drop under an arm you control, load their weight across your shoulders and roll them over your back to the mat.","mechanics":"Control their same-side arm at the elbow or wrist. Drop to your knees in front of them, inserting your head under their armpit so their arm drapes over your neck. Your other arm goes between their legs and hooks the near thigh. Pull the arm across your neck and lift the thigh, rolling across your shoulders so they cartwheel over you. Follow them to the mat and come up on top.","defense":"They sprawl their hips back, pull the arm free before you drop, or sit down onto your back when you are low.","mistake":"Dropping in front of them without the arm control. You end up on your knees under a sprawl.","drill":"Fireman's carry on a crash mat: 3 × 5 each side. Add the set-up from a Russian tie on the last set.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Kata-Guruma (wrestling)"],"rel":["russian_tie","kata_guruma","high_crotch"]}},{"id":"lateral_drop","cat":"takedown","name":"Lateral Drop","tagline":"A high-risk, high-reward over-under throw. When it lands it often ends near a pin.","tags":["Wrestling","Throw","Over-Under"],"objective":"From an over-under clinch, step across, drop your hips under theirs and throw them sideways over your body.","mechanics":"Get an underhook on one side and an overhook on the other, chest to chest. Step your underhook-side foot between their feet, then drop your hips low under theirs. Arch backward and turn toward your overhook side, using the overhook to pull and the underhook to lift. They fly over your hip. Keep turning so you land on top, chest to chest, not under them.","defense":"They sense the step and sprawl back, block the hip with their own, or follow you over and come out on top.","mistake":"Throwing without dropping your hips under theirs. Without the level change you fall back and they land on you.","drill":"Lateral drop on a crash mat: 3 × 5. Partner feeds the over-under; you focus on the drop and the turn.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Wrestling","rel":["underhooks_pummel","body_lock_takedown","harai_goshi"]}},{"id":"knee_tap","cat":"takedown","name":"Knee Tap","tagline":"Pull on the head, block the knee, and they fall over their own leg. Low risk and quick.","tags":["Wrestling","Collar Tie","Low Risk"],"objective":"Load their weight forward with the collar tie, then block the knee they are standing on so they fall forward and sideways.","mechanics":"Take a collar tie and pull their head toward you and across, making them step forward. As their lead foot lands, drop your level and put your free hand on the outside of that knee. Keep pulling the head across their own leg while you push the knee the other way. They fall to the side. Follow them down to a top position before they can turn into you.","defense":"They keep their weight back, step the leg away as you reach, or sprawl when your head comes down.","mistake":"Tapping the knee without moving the head. The head pull is what takes their balance; the tap only blocks the leg.","drill":"Knee tap timing: partner steps forward on your pull; tap the stepping leg. 3 × 10 each side.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Wrestling","rel":["collar_tie","snap_down","ankle_pick"]}},{"id":"slide_by","cat":"takedown","name":"Slide-By","tagline":"Slide their arm past you and step to the back. A quiet, fast go-behind.","tags":["Wrestling","Go-Behind"],"objective":"Move a pushing or reaching arm across your body and step around to their back before they turn.","mechanics":"When they reach or push with one arm, grab the wrist and push their elbow across your body with your other hand. Your same-side shoulder slides under their arm. Step forward past their hip at the same time. Lock around the waist from behind or attack the far leg before they can square up.","defense":"They pull the arm back and turn with you, or drop their level so you can't reach the waist.","mistake":"Pushing the arm without moving your feet. The angle comes from your step, not the push.","drill":"Partner pushes on your chest; slide by and lock the waist. 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Arm Slide-By"],"rel":["arm_drag_standing","duck_under","russian_tie"]}},{"id":"shuck","cat":"takedown","name":"Shuck","tagline":"Throw their head past you and step behind. Works off a collar tie or a lazy shot.","tags":["Wrestling","Go-Behind","Front Headlock"],"objective":"Move their head and upper body past your hip so you can circle behind them.","mechanics":"With your hand on the back of their neck or upper arm, pull their head down and past your hip in a short, sharp motion while you step back and to the side. Their head goes past you and their body follows. Step around behind them, with your chest over their back, and take control of the hips.","defense":"They keep their head up and posture, or follow the shuck with a shot of their own while you step.","mistake":"Shucking without stepping off the line. They fall straight onto you instead of past you.","drill":"Partner shoots a soft single; shuck and spin behind. 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Shrug","Head Shuck"],"rel":["snap_down","spin_behind","front_headlock_td"]}},{"id":"single_leg_defence","cat":"defence","name":"Single Leg Defence","tagline":"Once they have your leg, every second counts. Heavy hips, a whizzer and pressure on their head.","tags":["Wrestling","Takedown Defence"],"objective":"Stop the finish, then free your leg: weight on them, hips away and their head pushed down.","mechanics":"Immediately whizzer the arm on the side of your trapped leg and drive your hip down onto their shoulder. Push their head down and away with your free hand. Point your trapped knee toward the mat and back so the leg is low and hard to lift. Hop and circle away from the direction they are turning. When their grip weakens, kick the leg free and step it back into stance.","defense":"They counter by changing finishes — run the pipe, switch to a double, or come up to a high single.","mistake":"Hopping on one leg with your weight up. Without your weight on them you are just waiting for the finish.","drill":"Start with the leg caught; partner tries to finish at 70%. Free the leg within 10 seconds. 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["standing","defence"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","rel":["single_leg_wrestling","whizzer","sprawl","single_leg_finishes"]}},{"id":"spin_behind","cat":"transition","name":"Spin Behind","tagline":"After a sprawl or snap down, circle to their back. The cleanest score off a failed shot.","tags":["Wrestling","Front Headlock","Back Take"],"objective":"From a front headlock or sprawl, move around their head to their back and take control of their hips.","mechanics":"Keep your chest heavy on their upper back with your hips back. Block their near arm with your hand so they can't turn in. Walk your feet around their head in short steps, keeping your chest in contact the whole time. As you reach their side, drop your chest over their hips and grab the far hip or waist. Finish with your knee driving into their near hip to stop the sit-out.","defense":"They turn with you, sit out, or come up to their feet into a stand-up as soon as you leave their head.","mistake":"Losing chest contact while you circle. The gap lets them turn in and shoot or recover guard.","drill":"Sprawl, spin behind, sprawl again: 3 × 1 minute. Partner shoots at 50%, you spin to the back each time.","groups":["standing","headlock","transitions"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Go-Behind","Snap and Spin"],"rel":["sprawl","front_headlock_td","snap_down","shuck"]}},{"id":"guard_pull","cat":"transition","name":"Guard Pull","tagline":"Choose to start on the bottom. A legal tactic in BJJ — but know your ruleset before you use it.","tags":["BJJ","Standing","Ruleset"],"objective":"Bring the match to your guard safely, with grips that let you attack straight away, without giving up a takedown.","mechanics":"Take grips first — collar and sleeve in the gi, a collar tie or wrist control in no-gi. Put one foot on their hip or bicep, then sit down close to them, not far away. Land with your feet already connected to their hips or legs. In no-gi, sit to a seated guard and immediately get to a butterfly or shin-to-shin connection. Never pull guard from distance with no grips.","defense":"They pass immediately as you land, step back so you sit to nothing, or score a takedown on your sitting motion.","mistake":"Pulling guard without grips. They step back, you sit alone on the mat, and they start passing from a standing position.","drill":"Grip, pull, connect: 3 × 8. Land in your guard of choice with two connections within 2 seconds.","groups":["standing","open"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["seated_guard","guard_closed","collar_sleeve","wrestling_shot"]}},{"id":"referee_position","cat":"position","name":"Referee's Position","tagline":"Bottom on hands and knees, top on the side. The start of every folkstyle period and the base of mat wrestling.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Folkstyle"],"objective":"Bottom: get to your feet or reverse. Top: break them down flat and turn them for back points.","mechanics":"Bottom: hands shoulder-width under your shoulders, knees under your hips, weight slightly back on your knees, head up. Top: kneel at their side, one hand on the near elbow, the other arm around the waist with your hand on their navel. On the whistle, bottom explodes into a stand-up or sit-out; top chops the near arm and drives their hips forward to flatten them.","defense":"This is the start position for both sides. Each attack here has a direct counter: stand-ups meet the mat return, sit-outs meet the tight waist.","mistake":"Bottom: leaning forward onto your hands. Top: lying across their back. Both kill your first move.","drill":"Whistle drill: 10 starts per side. Bottom must reach their feet or a neutral position within 5 seconds; top must break them flat.","groups":["wrestling_mat"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Par Terre","Bottom / Top Start"],"rel":["stand_up","sit_out","tight_waist","switch"]}},{"id":"stand_up","cat":"defence","name":"Stand-Up","tagline":"The first escape every wrestler learns: get to your feet and face them.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Escape"],"objective":"Rise from the bottom position to your feet with your back to them, control their hands, then turn to face them.","mechanics":"On the start, drive your back into their chest and step your outside foot up. Rise with your back upright and your hips forward. Immediately control their hand on your waist with both of yours, peeling it off your body. Keep your elbows tight. Once the grip is broken, turn in toward them and back away into stance.","defense":"Top answers with a mat return — lifting and returning you to the mat — or by locking hands and dragging you back down.","mistake":"Standing up leaning forward. Your hips stay back and they pull you straight back to the mat.","drill":"Stand-up chain: 3 × 8 from the referee's position, partner gives light resistance on the waist.","groups":["wrestling_mat","defence"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Bottom Stand-Up"],"rel":["referee_position","mat_return","sit_out","technical_standup"]}},{"id":"sit_out","cat":"defence","name":"Sit-Out & Turn-In","tagline":"Sit your hips through, then turn to face them. A fast escape from the bottom.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Escape"],"objective":"Change the angle from on your knees to sitting with your back to them, then spin in to face them.","mechanics":"Step your outside foot forward and kick your inside leg through under your body so you sit on your hip, facing away from them. Keep your elbows tight and your head up. As they follow, turn your shoulder in toward them and come to your knees facing them, controlling their hands as you turn.","defense":"Top follows the sit-out with a tight waist and chops the arm, or gets their hips behind you before you turn.","mistake":"Sitting out flat on your back. You need to stay on your hip, upright, with your hands working.","drill":"Sit-out and turn-in: 3 × 10, with a partner who follows at 50%.","groups":["wrestling_mat","defence"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Sit-Out"],"rel":["referee_position","stand_up","switch","granby_roll"]}},{"id":"switch","cat":"defence","name":"Switch","tagline":"Use their own arm as a lever to reverse position from the bottom.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Reversal"],"objective":"Trap their arm around your waist and lever over it so you come out on top.","mechanics":"From the bottom, sit out to your near side and reach your inside arm over their arm that is around your waist, down to their inner thigh. Lean back onto that arm and hip out away from them — the pressure on their shoulder levers them forward. Swing your hips behind them and come up on top, controlling their hips.","defense":"They pull the arm out, reswitch, or step their hips away so there is nothing to lever against.","mistake":"Reaching over without moving your hips out. Without the hip movement there is no leverage.","drill":"Switch and reswitch chain: 3 × 1 minute, alternating who switches.","groups":["wrestling_mat","defence"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","rel":["sit_out","referee_position","granby_roll"]}},{"id":"granby_roll","cat":"defence","name":"Granby Roll","tagline":"A shoulder roll that turns you out from under them. Also a core BJJ guard-recovery movement.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Scramble"],"objective":"Roll across your shoulders to change your angle, escape their control and come up facing them or on top.","mechanics":"From the bottom, walk your feet toward one side and drop your inside shoulder to the mat, tucking your head. Roll across your shoulders, not your head, kicking your legs over. As you come over, your hips face them. In wrestling, you come up to your feet or a switch; in BJJ, you land with your legs in front for guard.","defense":"They follow the roll and stay chest to back, or block your hips before you can turn over.","mistake":"Rolling over your head or neck. The roll is across the shoulders, with your chin tucked.","drill":"Granby rolls across the mat, both directions: 3 lengths. Then from turtle with a partner on top at 50%.","groups":["wrestling_mat","defence","headlock"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","rel":["sit_out","turtle_bottom","guard_recovery"]}},{"id":"tight_waist","cat":"position","name":"Tight Waist & Chop","tagline":"The basic top breakdown: arm around the waist, chop the near arm, drive them flat.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Top"],"objective":"Take away their base so they are flat on their stomach and can't stand up or sit out.","mechanics":"Wrap your arm tight around their waist, hand on the far hip. With your other hand, chop their near arm at the elbow, pulling it toward you. At the same moment, drive your hips forward into theirs so their weight falls onto the missing arm. They go flat. Keep your chest on their back and your weight on their hips.","defense":"They post the arm back, stand up, or sit out as soon as you chop.","mistake":"Chopping without driving your hips. They lose the arm but stay on their knees.","drill":"Breakdown reps: 3 × 8. Partner on all fours resists at 50%.","groups":["wrestling_mat"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Breakdown"],"rel":["referee_position","half_nelson","spiral_ride"]}},{"id":"half_nelson","cat":"transition","name":"Half Nelson","tagline":"The basic pinning turn. Lever the head and arm to roll them onto their back.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Turn","Pin"],"objective":"From a flattened opponent, use the half nelson to lever them onto their back for back points and a pin.","mechanics":"Slide your arm under their near armpit and put your hand on the back of their head. Step your knees up toward their head and drive your chest into their shoulder at an angle. Lift the elbow and push the head away from you so their shoulders turn. Walk around toward their head, keeping the lever, until they roll to their back. Finish chest to chest, perpendicular, with the half nelson deep.","defense":"They keep their elbow tight to their side, turn away, or post their head and come up.","mistake":"Sinking the half nelson and pushing straight down. The turn comes from walking your body around their head.","drill":"Half nelson turns: 3 × 6 each side from a flattened partner.","groups":["wrestling_mat"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Wrestling","rel":["tight_waist","cradle","cross_face"]}},{"id":"cradle","cat":"transition","name":"Cradle","tagline":"Lock their head and knee together and roll them. One of wrestling's most reliable pins.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Pin"],"objective":"Connect their head and their near knee inside your arms, lock your hands and roll them onto their back.","mechanics":"Near-side cradle: one arm around the back of their neck, the other around the back of their near knee. Pull them together until you can lock your hands — a gable grip with palms together. Drive your shoulder into them and roll them toward their back, keeping the lock tight. Cross-face cradle: your arm crosses their face to the far knee before locking.","defense":"They keep their knee away from their head, post a hand between the lock, or straighten their leg.","mistake":"Trying to lock before the head and knee are close. Pull them together first, then lock.","drill":"Cradle lock speed: 3 × 6 each side from a balled-up partner.","groups":["wrestling_mat"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Near-Side Cradle","Cross-Face Cradle"],"rel":["half_nelson","cross_face","front_headlock_td"]}},{"id":"cross_face","cat":"position","name":"Cross-Face","tagline":"Your forearm across their jaw turns their head away — and where the head goes, the body follows.","tags":["Wrestling","Pressure","Control"],"objective":"Turn their face away from you so they can't turn in, bridge into you or recover guard.","mechanics":"Drive your forearm or shoulder across their jaw from the near side and grip their far arm or shoulder. Pull your elbow toward you so their head turns away from you. Keep your weight on the arm. In wrestling it sets up turns; in BJJ it is the key to passing half guard and holding side control.","defense":"They post their hand on your face or bicep, turn their chin in, or bridge as you lift the cross-face.","mistake":"A cross-face with no pressure. Rest your weight on it — it should be uncomfortable for them.","drill":"From half guard top: establish the cross-face and underhook, hold for 30 seconds against resistance. 5 rounds.","groups":["wrestling_mat","side"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["side_control","half_guard_top","cradle"]}},{"id":"spiral_ride","cat":"transition","name":"Spiral Ride","tagline":"Wrap the far hip and drive in a spiral. They come apart and you take the back.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Back Take"],"objective":"Break down a turtled or kneeling opponent and expose their back by driving them in a circle.","mechanics":"Reach under their near arm and across to the far hip or inner thigh. Hook your other arm deep under their near armpit. Drive your chest into their shoulder at an angle and walk your feet in a circle toward their head. The spiral pressure folds them onto their side. As they turn, insert your hooks or lock a seatbelt for the back.","defense":"They sit through, stand up, or turn into you before the spiral pressure builds.","mistake":"Driving straight forward. The ride works on a diagonal into their shoulder.","drill":"Spiral ride to back take: 3 × 6 from a partner in turtle.","groups":["wrestling_mat","transitions"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","rel":["tight_waist","back_take_turtle","back_control"]}},{"id":"leg_ride","cat":"position","name":"Leg Ride","tagline":"Wrestling's version of back control: a leg hooked inside theirs to ride and turn them.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Control"],"objective":"Control them from behind with your leg wrapped in theirs, then turn them with arm control.","mechanics":"From behind, insert one leg between theirs and wrap your foot around their shin — the grapevine. Keep your hip tight to their hip. With your arms, attack the far arm or use a cross-face. Your leg holds their base so they can't stand up. Turn them by chicken-winging the near arm or a power half. In BJJ, this is the same hook that leads to back control and the truck.","defense":"They kick the leg back and free your hook, sit through, or roll toward you.","mistake":"A shallow leg. If your foot doesn't wrap their shin they kick straight out.","drill":"Ride for 30 seconds with legs in while they try to stand. 5 rounds, switch.","groups":["wrestling_mat","transitions"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Legs In","Riding Legs"],"rel":["back_take_turtle","back_control","tilt"]}},{"id":"tilt","cat":"transition","name":"Tilt","tagline":"Roll them over your body while holding them, exposing their back for points.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Back Points"],"objective":"Turn a turtled opponent onto their side or back by rolling them over you while controlling an arm and leg.","mechanics":"Hook a leg with yours or wrap their near leg with your arm. Control the far arm or waist with your other arm. Drop your hip to the mat and roll back, bringing them over your body so their back faces the ceiling. Hold them there to score back points before they can turn to their stomach.","defense":"They post their free arm, base out wide with their legs, or roll through to come out on top.","mistake":"Rolling without control of the leg. They roll over you and come up in a better position.","drill":"Tilt from referee's top: 3 × 6. Hold for a 3-count each time.","groups":["wrestling_mat"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Turk","Navy Ride"],"rel":["leg_ride","gut_wrench","half_nelson"]}},{"id":"gut_wrench","cat":"transition","name":"Gut Wrench","tagline":"The freestyle turn: lock around their waist and roll them over and over for points.","tags":["Wrestling","Freestyle","Par Terre","Turn"],"objective":"Lock tight around their waist from the side and roll them across your body repeatedly.","mechanics":"From the top in par terre, lock your hands around their waist from the side, gripping at their far side. Pull their hips tight to your chest. Walk your feet to their head side, drop your near shoulder and roll — bridging and turning so they go over you. Keep the lock and repeat. Each turn that shows their back scores.","defense":"They spread their legs wide, keep their hips heavy, and fight your grip lock at the waist.","mistake":"Locking your hands loose around their back. The lock has to be tight around the waist or it slips.","drill":"Gut wrench rolls: 3 × 5 turns in a row against light resistance.","groups":["wrestling_mat"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","rel":["tilt","leg_lace","referee_position"]}},{"id":"leg_lace","cat":"transition","name":"Leg Lace","tagline":"Lock their ankles together and roll. The other great freestyle turn.","tags":["Wrestling","Freestyle","Par Terre","Turn"],"objective":"Trap both of their ankles in a lace and roll them repeatedly over their own legs.","mechanics":"From behind and to the side, wrap one arm around their ankles from the outside, the other arm under. Cross their ankles together and lock your hands, trapping their feet against your chest. Sit through and roll toward their head, turning their legs and hips over. Keep the ankles tight and repeat to score again.","defense":"They keep their legs apart and away from your hands, and turn their hips to face down.","mistake":"A loose lace. If their ankles aren't crossed and pinned, they kick out halfway through.","drill":"Lace and roll: 3 × 4 each side.","groups":["wrestling_mat"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Ankle Lace","Gator Roll"],"rel":["gut_wrench","tilt"]}},{"id":"peterson_roll","cat":"defence","name":"Peterson Roll","tagline":"Roll them over your body using their own arm. A reversal that can land you on top in a pin.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Reversal"],"objective":"Trap their arm that is around your waist and roll across your shoulders so they are carried over you.","mechanics":"From the bottom, trap their arm around your waist tight with your same-side arm. Reach back with your other hand to their near leg. Step your outside foot forward, drop your shoulder and roll toward the trapped arm, pulling their leg. They have no arm to post and roll with you. Come out on top, chest to chest.","defense":"They pull the trapped arm out or spread their base before you roll.","mistake":"Rolling without trapping the arm. They post and you roll alone.","drill":"Peterson rolls: 3 × 5 each side with a cooperative partner, then at 50%.","groups":["wrestling_mat","defence"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Wrestling","rel":["switch","granby_roll","sit_out"]}},{"id":"chicken_wing","cat":"transition","name":"Chicken Wing","tagline":"Bend their arm behind their back and lever them over. In BJJ the same grip becomes a kimura.","tags":["Wrestling","Mat Work","Turn"],"objective":"Trap their near arm behind their back and use it as a lever to turn them over.","mechanics":"From top, reach your arm under their near arm from behind and up to their back, bending their elbow behind them. Pull the elbow up and drive your shoulder into theirs, walking toward their head. They roll over their trapped arm. Keep the arm trapped to hold them on their back. In submission grappling, this grip is a step from a kimura; keep it legal for your ruleset.","defense":"They keep their elbow tight to their body, roll with you, or pull the arm free.","mistake":"Cranking the arm instead of driving your body. The turn comes from your shoulder pressure.","drill":"Chicken wing turns: 3 × 6 each side, slow and controlled.","groups":["wrestling_mat"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Wrestling","rel":["half_nelson","leg_ride","kimura"]}},{"id":"de_ashi_harai","cat":"judo","name":"De-Ashi-Harai","tagline":"Sweep the foot as it steps forward, just before their weight lands. Pure timing.","tags":["Judo","Ashi-Waza","Foot Sweep","Timing"],"objective":"Catch their advancing foot at the moment it is about to take weight, and sweep it in the direction it is travelling.","mechanics":"As they step forward with their right foot, sweep it with the sole of your left foot, contacting just below the ankle. Sweep in the direction of their step — forward and across. At the same time, lift with your sleeve hand and turn your lapel hand down so their upper body goes the other way. The sweep is light and fast; it uses their own movement. Done well, they fall with no resistance at all.","defense":"They shorten their steps, keep their weight centred, or lift the foot over your sweep.","mistake":"Sweeping after the weight has landed. Then you're kicking a planted leg and it hurts you more than them.","drill":"Moving uchikomi: partner walks forward and back, you sweep the advancing foot. 3 × 1 minute, focus on timing not force.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Advancing Foot Sweep"],"rel":["okuri_ashi_harai","kumi_kata","ko_soto_gari"]}},{"id":"okuri_ashi_harai","cat":"judo","name":"Okuri-Ashi-Harai","tagline":"Sweep both feet together as they step sideways. They go up and drop flat.","tags":["Judo","Ashi-Waza","Foot Sweep"],"objective":"When they step sideways, sweep the trailing foot into the leading foot so both feet leave the mat at once.","mechanics":"Move them sideways with your grips, matching their steps. As their feet come together, step in with your support foot and sweep their trailing ankle with the sole of your foot, carrying it into the other foot. Lift up and across with both hands so their body rises while their feet go sideways. They fall flat on their side.","defense":"They keep a wide stance and don't let their feet come together, or step out of the line of the sweep.","mistake":"Sweeping with your leg only. The lift with your hands is what takes their weight off their feet.","drill":"Side-stepping uchikomi: 3 × 1 minute, sweep each time their feet come together.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Sliding Foot Sweep","Double Foot Sweep"],"rel":["de_ashi_harai","kumi_kata"]}},{"id":"sasae_tsurikomi_ashi","cat":"judo","name":"Sasae-Tsurikomi-Ashi","tagline":"Block their ankle and pull them over it. A forward throw with almost no risk.","tags":["Judo","Ashi-Waza","Block"],"objective":"Pull them forward and around, then block their lead ankle so they trip over your foot.","mechanics":"Pull them forward and to your side with both hands so they step toward you. As they step, place the sole of your foot on the front of their lead ankle — a block, not a sweep. Keep pulling up and around in a circle, turning your body. They fall forward over the blocked ankle.","defense":"They stop stepping, drop their weight back, or lift the blocked foot and step over it.","mistake":"Pushing with the blocking foot. The foot is a wall; the throw comes from the pull.","drill":"Blocking uchikomi: 3 × 10 each side, partner steps into the block.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Propping Drawing Ankle"],"rel":["hiza_guruma","de_ashi_harai","tai_otoshi"]}},{"id":"hiza_guruma","cat":"judo","name":"Hiza-Guruma","tagline":"Block the knee and turn them like a wheel. Close cousin of sasae-tsurikomi-ashi.","tags":["Judo","Ashi-Waza","Block"],"objective":"Turn them around a block placed on the side of their knee.","mechanics":"Draw them forward with your sleeve hand as they step. Place the sole of your foot against the outside of their lead knee. Turn your upper body and steer them in a circle around the blocked knee with both hands, like turning a steering wheel. They roll over the blocked leg.","defense":"They straighten and plant the leg, or step around your foot.","mistake":"Placing the foot too low on the shin. On the knee the block works; below it they step over.","drill":"Static uchikomi: 3 × 10 each side, then moving.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Knee Wheel"],"rel":["sasae_tsurikomi_ashi","tai_otoshi"]}},{"id":"o_guruma","cat":"judo","name":"O-Guruma","tagline":"A leg block high across their hips. They wheel over your straight leg.","tags":["Judo","Ashi-Waza"],"objective":"Pull them forward onto their toes and turn them over your leg blocked across their upper thigh.","mechanics":"Break their balance forward onto their toes with a strong pull. Turn in and extend your leg straight across the front of their hips or upper thighs. Pull them around and over the leg with both hands, turning your head and shoulders. They rotate over the leg like a wheel turning on an axle.","defense":"They drop their hips below your leg or step around it.","mistake":"Bending the blocking leg. It must be straight and high, or it becomes a weak hip throw.","drill":"Turn-in reps: 3 × 8 each side, focus on the high, straight block.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Large Wheel"],"rel":["harai_goshi","hiza_guruma"]}},{"id":"ashi_guruma","cat":"judo","name":"Ashi-Guruma","tagline":"Like o-guruma, but the block is at the knee. Good against an opponent who bends forward.","tags":["Judo","Ashi-Waza"],"objective":"Block their leg at the knee and turn them over it.","mechanics":"Pull them forward and to your side. Turn in and extend your leg across the front of their knee, keeping it straight. Rotate your upper body and pull them over the blocking leg. The lower block works well when they lean forward and the hip is out of reach.","defense":"They step around the block or sit back.","mistake":"Turning in too far, so your hip ends up in front of them. Then it is neither a hip throw nor a wheel.","drill":"Uchikomi with a moving partner: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Leg Wheel"],"rel":["o_guruma","harai_goshi"]}},{"id":"ko_soto_gake","cat":"judo","name":"Ko-Soto-Gake","tagline":"Hook their heel from the outside and drive them back over it.","tags":["Judo","Ashi-Waza","Hook"],"objective":"Hook behind their heel with your foot and push their weight back over the trapped leg.","mechanics":"Push them back onto their heels with your grips. Step close and hook behind the heel of their lead leg with the sole of your foot, from the outside. Pull the heel toward you while you drive your chest and hands forward and down. They fall back over the hooked leg.","defense":"They keep their weight forward, step the leg away, or counter with their own hook.","mistake":"Hooking from too far away. You need to be close so your weight drives through the hook.","drill":"Ko-soto-gake from a backward push: 3 × 10 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Small Outer Hook"],"rel":["ko_soto_gari","o_soto_gari"]}},{"id":"kibisu_gaeshi","cat":"judo","name":"Kibisu-Gaeshi","tagline":"Pick the heel and push them back. Judo's ankle pick — check your ruleset before using it.","tags":["Judo","Leg Grab","Ankle Pick"],"objective":"Grab their heel or ankle as you push their upper body back, so they fall with no leg to step with.","mechanics":"Drive them back with your collar grip or tie. Drop your level and grab the back of their lead heel with your free hand. Pull the heel toward you as you push their upper body back and down. They fall onto their back. Under current IJF rules direct leg grabs are penalised; in freestyle judo, sambo, BJJ and wrestling it is legal.","defense":"They keep their weight forward and their feet back out of reach.","mistake":"Reaching for the heel without the push. The push is what puts their weight on the heel.","drill":"Push-and-pick: 3 × 10 each side with a moving partner.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Heel Trip Reversal","Heel Pick"],"rel":["ankle_pick","ko_uchi_gari"]}},{"id":"ippon_seoi_nage","cat":"judo","name":"Ippon-Seoi-Nage","tagline":"Trap one arm over your shoulder and throw. Works in the gi and without one.","tags":["Judo","Te-Waza","Shoulder Throw","No-Gi Friendly"],"objective":"Turn in under their arm, trap it in the crook of your elbow, and throw them over your shoulder.","mechanics":"Pull their sleeve arm forward and up. Turn in, stepping your feet inside theirs, and drive your other arm up under their armpit so their upper arm is trapped in your elbow crook. Bend your knees so your hips are below theirs. Straighten your legs and pull down and around with both hands, bowing forward, so they go over your shoulder.","defense":"They drop their hips, step around, or pull their arm free before you turn in.","mistake":"Turning in with straight legs. You must drop below their centre of gravity to lift them.","drill":"Uchikomi: 3 × 10 each side, then 5 throws on the crash mat.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Judo","aka":["One-Arm Shoulder Throw"],"rel":["seoi_nage","seoi_otoshi","kumi_kata"]}},{"id":"seoi_otoshi","cat":"judo","name":"Seoi-Otoshi","tagline":"A seoi-nage where you drop to your knees. Fast and hard to see coming.","tags":["Judo","Te-Waza","Drop Throw"],"objective":"Turn in and drop low under them, throwing them over your shoulder as you go down.","mechanics":"Take a seoi-nage grip and turn in fast. Instead of lifting with your legs, drop onto one or both knees directly between their feet, pulling them forward and down over your shoulder. The drop takes you under their centre of gravity in one motion.","defense":"They sprawl their hips back or sit onto your back as you drop.","mistake":"Dropping before you turn in. You end up on your knees in front of them in a bad position.","drill":"Drop-in reps on a soft mat: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Shoulder Drop"],"rel":["ippon_seoi_nage","seoi_nage"]}},{"id":"uki_otoshi","cat":"judo","name":"Uki-Otoshi","tagline":"A throw with the hands alone. Pull them forward and drop to one knee.","tags":["Judo","Te-Waza","Hands Only"],"objective":"Break their balance forward in a circle so strongly that they fall with no leg contact.","mechanics":"As they step forward, pull them sharply forward and down in a circle with both hands. At the same moment, drop to one knee at their side. Their weight is pulled past their front foot and they fall forward in a roll.","defense":"They keep their weight back and resist the pull, or step quickly to catch their balance.","mistake":"Pulling straight down instead of in a circle. The circle is what takes them past their feet.","drill":"Kuzushi drill: 3 × 10, partner rolls out with ukemi.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Floating Drop"],"rel":["sumi_otoshi","kumi_kata"]}},{"id":"sumi_otoshi","cat":"judo","name":"Sumi-Otoshi","tagline":"Throw them toward their rear corner using only your hands and their own step.","tags":["Judo","Te-Waza","Hands Only"],"objective":"Push them diagonally backward over the corner of their heel as they step.","mechanics":"As they step back, step in close to their side and push them diagonally backward toward their rear corner, lifting with the sleeve and driving with the lapel hand. With nothing behind them, they fall backward. There is no leg contact — it relies on timing and the direction of the push.","defense":"They keep their weight forward and step back smoothly.","mistake":"Pushing straight back. The direction is diagonal, toward the corner where they have no foot.","drill":"Partner steps back; push to the corner on each step. 3 × 8.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Corner Drop","Air Throw"],"rel":["uki_otoshi"]}},{"id":"tani_otoshi","cat":"judo","name":"Tani-Otoshi","tagline":"Slide behind them and drop backward. A classic counter to forward throws.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Counter"],"objective":"When they turn in for a throw or bend forward, slide your leg behind both of theirs and sit down so they fall back over it.","mechanics":"Get your arm around their back or keep a strong lapel grip. Slide your leg behind both of their heels, low to the mat. Drop to your side, pulling them backward over your outstretched leg. They fall onto their back beside you.","defense":"They keep their weight forward and step over your leg, or turn to face you.","mistake":"Sitting down too far from them. Your body must be close behind their legs.","drill":"Counter drill: partner turns in for uchi-mata at 30%; hit tani-otoshi. 3 × 5.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Valley Drop"],"rel":["uchi_mata","harai_goshi","ura_nage"]}},{"id":"kata_guruma","cat":"judo","name":"Kata-Guruma","tagline":"Load them across your shoulders and wheel them over. Judo's fireman's carry.","tags":["Judo","Te-Waza","Leg Grab"],"objective":"Drop under them, load their body across both shoulders, then turn and throw them over.","mechanics":"Pull their sleeve arm across your shoulders. Drop low, putting your head under their armpit, and reach between their legs to their near thigh. Stand up with them across your shoulders, or roll them over from your knees. Under IJF rules, the leg grab version is not allowed; drop versions that grab the sleeve only are still used.","defense":"They pull their arm back and sprawl, or step over your head.","mistake":"Bending at the waist to reach the leg. Drop with your legs, keeping your back straight.","drill":"Kata-guruma reps on the crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Shoulder Wheel","Fireman's Carry"],"rel":["fireman_carry"]}},{"id":"koshi_guruma","cat":"judo","name":"Koshi-Guruma","tagline":"The headlock hip throw. It works in a gi, without one, and in the clinch.","tags":["Judo","Koshi-Waza","Headlock","No-Gi Friendly"],"objective":"Wrap their head, turn your hips past theirs and wheel them over your hip.","mechanics":"Wrap your arm around the back of their neck, gripping their collar or your own wrist. Control their other arm at the sleeve or elbow. Turn in, stepping your feet so your hips go past theirs. Bend your knees, then straighten and pull their head around and down as you turn. They wheel over your hip.","defense":"They drop their hips, step around, or take your back as you turn in.","mistake":"Not getting your hips past theirs. If your hip stops short, they step around and take your back.","drill":"Uchikomi: 3 × 10, then 5 throws each side.","groups":["judo","standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Hip Wheel","Headlock Throw"],"rel":["o_goshi","harai_goshi","underhooks_pummel"]}},{"id":"uki_goshi","cat":"judo","name":"Uki-Goshi","tagline":"A short hip throw where they float over a hip that barely turns in.","tags":["Judo","Koshi-Waza"],"objective":"Draw them onto your hip with an arm around the waist and turn them over it.","mechanics":"Wrap your arm around their lower back, holding their belt or waist. Pull their sleeve forward. Step in so your hip touches their front, turning only slightly. Pull them tight to your hip and twist your upper body, so they float around and over the hip.","defense":"They push their hips forward or step around your hip.","mistake":"Turning in too deep. Then it becomes o-goshi with poor kuzushi.","drill":"Uchikomi: 3 × 10 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Floating Hip"],"rel":["o_goshi","koshi_guruma"]}},{"id":"tsurikomi_goshi","cat":"judo","name":"Tsurikomi-Goshi","tagline":"Lift with the lapel, drop your hips low, throw. Good against upright opponents.","tags":["Judo","Koshi-Waza","Low Hip"],"objective":"Pull them up onto their toes with a lapel and sleeve grip, then turn in low and throw them over your hips.","mechanics":"Pull up with your lapel hand (tsuri) and forward with the sleeve hand (komi), making them rise onto their toes. Turn in with your hips low, below theirs. Keep lifting with the lapel hand as you straighten your legs and turn. They go over your hips.","defense":"They keep their weight low, block with their hip, or step around.","mistake":"Dropping the lapel hand as you turn. The lift must continue all the way through the throw.","drill":"Uchikomi with emphasis on the lift: 3 × 10 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Lifting-Pulling Hip"],"rel":["sode_tsurikomi_goshi","o_goshi"]}},{"id":"sode_tsurikomi_goshi","cat":"judo","name":"Sode-Tsurikomi-Goshi","tagline":"Lift their sleeve high, drop under it and throw. Hard to read and hard to block.","tags":["Judo","Koshi-Waza","Sleeve Grip"],"objective":"Drive their arm up with a sleeve grip, turn in under it and throw them over your hips.","mechanics":"Grip both sleeves. Drive one sleeve straight up above their head, opening their side. Turn in low under the lifted arm, your hips below theirs, keeping the arm up. Pull forward with the other sleeve and straighten your legs to throw. It can also be done dropping to the knees.","defense":"They pull the lifted arm down, or step back as you turn.","mistake":"Lifting the sleeve forward instead of straight up. Up is what makes them rise and opens the side.","drill":"Grip, lift, turn: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Sleeve Lift Hip"],"rel":["tsurikomi_goshi","seoi_nage"]}},{"id":"utsuri_goshi","cat":"judo","name":"Utsuri-Goshi","tagline":"Counter their hip throw: lift them off your hip and slide your own hip in.","tags":["Judo","Koshi-Waza","Counter"],"objective":"When they attempt a hip throw, lift them up off the ground and swing your hip under theirs to throw them back.","mechanics":"As they turn in for a hip throw, wrap your arm around their waist and drop your hips. Lift them off the ground with your legs and hips. While they are in the air, swing your hip in front of theirs. As they come down, they land on your hip and you throw them over it.","defense":"They don't commit to the hip throw, or they keep their hips low so you can't lift them.","mistake":"Trying it without lifting them first. The counter only works while their feet are off the mat.","drill":"Partner turns in for o-goshi; lift and switch. 3 × 5, slowly.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Changing Hip"],"rel":["ushiro_goshi","o_goshi"]}},{"id":"ushiro_goshi","cat":"judo","name":"Ushiro-Goshi","tagline":"They turn in, you lift them backward off their feet and drop them in front of you.","tags":["Judo","Koshi-Waza","Counter"],"objective":"Counter a hip throw by lifting them from behind and dropping them on their back.","mechanics":"As they turn in, drop your hips and wrap their waist from behind. Thrust your hips forward into their backside to lift them off the mat. Drop your hips back away and let them fall in front of you. It is the judo version of a back lift.","defense":"They don't turn their back fully, or they sit down onto your hips.","mistake":"Lifting with your back instead of your hips. Thrust from the hips with a straight back.","drill":"Partner turns in; lift and drop on a crash mat. 3 × 5.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Rear Hip"],"rel":["utsuri_goshi","mat_return"]}},{"id":"ura_nage","cat":"judo","name":"Ura-Nage","tagline":"Lift and throw them backward over your own body. A big counter that needs a crash mat to learn.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Counter"],"objective":"Counter a forward attack by lifting them and falling back so they go over you.","mechanics":"When they attack forward, step behind them, wrap your arm around their waist and put your other hand on their abdomen. Drop your hips under them and arch backward, lifting with your hips and pushing with the hand. They go over your shoulder as you fall back. Turn so you land on top.","defense":"They stop their forward attack and keep their hips away.","mistake":"Falling back without getting your hips under them. You fall and they land on you.","drill":"Crash mat only: 3 × 3 each side, fully supervised.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Rear Throw"],"rel":["tani_otoshi","ushiro_goshi"]}},{"id":"soto_makikomi","cat":"judo","name":"Soto-Makikomi","tagline":"Wrap their arm and roll your whole body to the mat, taking them with you.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Wrap"],"objective":"Trap their arm tight to your body and fall into a rolling sacrifice so they go over you.","mechanics":"Hold their sleeve tight and release your lapel grip. Swing your free arm over their trapped arm and turn in, wrapping it to your body. Step across and fall forward, rotating your whole body. Your weight pulls them over you as you roll. Land on top of them.","defense":"They pull the arm out or sprawl back before you commit.","mistake":"Releasing the trapped arm as you fall. Keep the arm wrapped or you land on your own.","drill":"Wrap and roll on a crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Outer Winding"],"rel":["harai_goshi","koshi_guruma"]}},{"id":"hikikomi_gaeshi","cat":"judo","name":"Hikikomi-Gaeshi","tagline":"Drop under them and roll them over. In BJJ, the entry often goes straight to the back.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Back Take"],"objective":"Pull them down over you as you sit under them, lifting with a leg hook so they roll over your body.","mechanics":"Grip over the back (belt or body) and their sleeve, or hook an underhook in no-gi. Sit down under them, pulling them forward. Your foot or shin hooks the inside of their thigh. Roll back and lift with the hook so they flip over you. In BJJ, players often use this entry to roll under and take the back or land in a top position.","defense":"They sprawl their hips back or step around your hook.","mistake":"Sitting too far away. Your hips need to be under theirs when you drop.","drill":"Hikikomi drop and roll: 3 × 5 each side on a soft mat.","groups":["judo","transitions"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Pulling-In Reversal"],"rel":["sumi_gaeshi","tomoe_nage","back_control"]}},{"id":"renraku_waza","cat":"concept","name":"Renraku-Waza","tagline":"One throw sets up the next. Their defence to the first is the opening for the second.","tags":["Judo","Combinations","Chains"],"objective":"Attack with a throw that makes them react in a known direction, then throw them that way.","mechanics":"Classic combinations: ko-uchi-gari forward into seoi-nage (they step back from ko-uchi, putting weight forward into seoi). O-uchi-gari into uchi-mata (they widen their legs, opening the inside). Ko-soto-gari into o-soto-gari. The first attack must be a real threat. Plan combinations in opposite directions: back then forward, left then right.","defense":"Experienced opponents don't overreact to the first throw, so it must be committed enough to force a reaction.","mistake":"A fake first attack. If it isn't a real threat they ignore it and you've wasted the set-up.","drill":"Combination uchikomi: 3 × 10 for each pair. Then in randori, only score with the second throw.","groups":["judo","concepts"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Combinations"],"rel":["ko_uchi_gari","seoi_nage","chain_attacks","action_reaction_entries"]}},{"id":"kaeshi_waza","cat":"concept","name":"Kaeshi-Waza","tagline":"Throw them with their own attack. Counters work when they commit and miss.","tags":["Judo","Counters","Timing"],"objective":"Recognise their attack early, stop it, and throw them in the direction their failed attack has left them.","mechanics":"A counter has two parts: block or avoid their attack, then throw. Against forward throws (uchi-mata, harai-goshi), counters go backward: tani-otoshi, ura-nage, ushiro-goshi. Against hooking foot attacks, counters sweep or step around: ko-uchi against o-uchi. The safest counters start from a strong posture with your hips back and low.","defense":"Good players attack with combinations so there is no single committed moment to counter.","mistake":"Waiting to counter without attacking. Passive play gets penalised and teaches them your rhythm.","drill":"Counter randori: one player attacks only, the other only counters. 3 × 2 minutes.","groups":["judo","concepts"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Counter Throws"],"rel":["tani_otoshi","utsuri_goshi","ura_nage","renraku_waza"]}},{"id":"osaekomi_rules","cat":"concept","name":"Osaekomi: How Judo Pins Score","tagline":"In judo, holding someone on their back wins the match. Know what counts as a pin.","tags":["Judo","Rules","Pins","Ne-Waza"],"objective":"Understand the conditions of a pin so you control the right way: their back on the mat, your body on top, and their legs not trapping you.","mechanics":"An osaekomi (hold) is called when they are on their back or shoulders, you control them from above or the side, and their legs are not wrapped around your legs or body. Under current IJF rules, a 20-second hold scores ippon (wins) and 10 seconds scores waza-ari. If they trap one of your legs with theirs, the hold is broken (toketa). This is why judo pins focus on keeping your legs free.","defense":"They bridge, shrimp and try to trap a leg to break the hold, or turn onto their stomach.","mistake":"Holding someone tight with your legs tangled in theirs. In judo that isn't a pin.","drill":"Pin-and-escape rounds: 20-second holds from each pin, partner escapes. 5 rounds per pin.","groups":["judo_ground"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Osaekomi","Hold-Downs"],"rel":["kesa_gatame","yoko_shiho_gatame","kami_shiho_gatame","tate_shiho_gatame"]}},{"id":"kuzure_kesa_gatame","cat":"position","name":"Kuzure-Kesa-Gatame","tagline":"The scarf hold with your arm under their far shoulder instead of the head. More stable and easier to keep.","tags":["Judo","Pin","Scarf Hold"],"objective":"Pin them on their back from the side with their near arm trapped and your arm under their far shoulder.","mechanics":"Sit at their side, facing their head, with your hip tight against their ribs. Trap their near arm under your armpit, holding the sleeve or wrist. Your other arm goes under their far armpit, hand on the mat or gripping their collar. Spread your legs wide, front leg bent, back leg extended, for a stable triangle base. Keep your head low.","defense":"They bridge into you, try to pull their trapped arm free, or roll you over the top.","mistake":"Legs close together. A narrow base lets them bridge and roll you.","drill":"20-second holds against a full escape: 5 rounds, switch.","groups":["judo_ground","side"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Broken Scarf Hold"],"rel":["kesa_gatame","kesa_escape","osaekomi_rules"]}},{"id":"yoko_shiho_gatame","cat":"position","name":"Yoko-Shiho-Gatame","tagline":"Judo's side control: chest on chest, one arm between the legs, one at the head.","tags":["Judo","Pin","Side Control"],"objective":"Pin them from the side, controlling the head and the hips with your chest flat on theirs.","mechanics":"Lie across them from the side, chest on chest. One arm goes between their legs and grips their belt or the far trouser leg. The other arm goes under or around their neck and grips their collar or shoulder. Your knees are tight to their side, or your legs spread wide for base. Keep your hips low.","defense":"They frame against your neck and hip, shrimp away and try to get a knee in or turn to their stomach.","mistake":"Hips up in the air. Low hips kill their bridge.","drill":"20-second holds: 5 rounds, switch.","groups":["judo_ground","side"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Side Four-Corner Hold"],"rel":["side_control","osaekomi_rules","kami_shiho_gatame"]}},{"id":"kami_shiho_gatame","cat":"position","name":"Kami-Shiho-Gatame","tagline":"Pin from above their head. Judo's north-south.","tags":["Judo","Pin","North-South"],"objective":"Pin them from above their head, holding their belt on both sides with your chest flat on theirs.","mechanics":"Kneel or lie above their head, chest on their chest. Reach both arms under their arms to grip their belt at the sides. Pull their arms tight with your elbows. Keep your head to one side. Spread your knees, or extend your legs back, to stay heavy.","defense":"They push your head or hips, shrimp to the side and turn their hips toward you.","mistake":"Light chest pressure. Without your weight on their chest they turn out easily.","drill":"20-second holds: 5 rounds.","groups":["judo_ground","side"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Upper Four-Corner Hold","North-South Hold"],"rel":["north_south","north_south_choke","kuzure_kami_shiho_gatame"]}},{"id":"kuzure_kami_shiho_gatame","cat":"position","name":"Kuzure-Kami-Shiho-Gatame","tagline":"North-south at an angle, with one arm trapped. Tighter than the basic version.","tags":["Judo","Pin"],"objective":"Pin from above at an angle, with one of their arms trapped over your shoulder.","mechanics":"From the head side, slide to an angle. One arm goes over their arm and under their shoulder, trapping their arm against your body. The other arm goes under their far armpit to grip the belt or collar. Your chest presses down on their chest at the angle.","defense":"They turn into the trapped arm side or bridge and shrimp.","mistake":"Letting the trapped arm slide free. Keep it pinned with your shoulder.","drill":"20-second holds: 5 rounds.","groups":["judo_ground"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Broken Upper Four-Corner"],"rel":["kami_shiho_gatame","side_control"]}},{"id":"tate_shiho_gatame","cat":"position","name":"Tate-Shiho-Gatame","tagline":"Judo's mount. Legs hooked around theirs and one arm trapped.","tags":["Judo","Pin","Mount"],"objective":"Pin them from mount, with your legs wrapped around theirs and one of their arms trapped by your head.","mechanics":"Sit astride them. Hook your feet under their thighs or wrap your legs around theirs to stop the bridge. Wrap one arm around their head and one of their arms so the arm is trapped next to their head. Keep your chest low on theirs.","defense":"They bridge and roll, or shrimp to bring a knee in and trap a leg.","mistake":"Sitting upright with your legs loose. They bridge you off.","drill":"20-second holds: 5 rounds.","groups":["judo_ground","mount"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Vertical Four-Corner Hold","Judo Mount"],"rel":["mount","osaekomi_rules","mount_escape"]}},{"id":"ushiro_kesa_gatame","cat":"position","name":"Ushiro-Kesa-Gatame","tagline":"Scarf hold facing their legs. Unusual, and they often don't know how to escape it.","tags":["Judo","Pin"],"objective":"Pin them from the side while facing their legs, trapping their far arm.","mechanics":"Sit at their side facing their feet, your hip against their armpit. Reach over and trap their far arm with yours, or hold their belt. Your other arm controls their near arm. Spread your legs for base, and lean your back on their chest.","defense":"They push your back, bridge and turn toward you.","mistake":"Sitting upright. Lean your weight back into them.","drill":"20-second holds: 5 rounds.","groups":["judo_ground"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Reverse Scarf Hold"],"rel":["kesa_gatame","kuzure_kesa_gatame"]}},{"id":"kesa_escape","cat":"defence","name":"Scarf Hold Escape","tagline":"Free the trapped arm, turn into them and get your back off the mat.","tags":["Escape","Scarf Hold","Judo"],"objective":"Get your trapped arm free, then turn into them so you are no longer on your back.","mechanics":"First, get your trapped arm free: grip your own hands and pull your elbow out, or turn your thumb down and slide out. Then bridge into them, lifting them onto their side. As they post, turn onto your side facing them, slide your knee in and come up to your knees. Alternatively, wrap their leg with yours to break the hold or roll them over you with a big bridge toward your head.","defense":"They widen their base, keep the arm trapped, or switch to another pin as you turn.","mistake":"Pushing on their head while your arm is still trapped. Free the arm first.","drill":"Start in kesa-gatame; escape within 20 seconds. 5 rounds each side.","groups":["judo_ground","defence"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Kesa-Gatame Escape"],"rel":["kesa_gatame","kuzure_kesa_gatame","side_control_escape"]}},{"id":"judo_sankaku","cat":"transition","name":"Sankaku Turnover","tagline":"Lock a triangle on a turtled opponent and roll them onto their back into a pin or choke.","tags":["Judo","Turtle","Triangle"],"objective":"Trap their head and arm in a triangle from turtle, then roll them so they land on their back.","mechanics":"From the front or side of a turtled opponent, insert your leg under their arm and around their neck. Lock the triangle with your legs, trapping their head and one arm. Roll toward the trapped arm, taking them with you onto their back. Finish with a pin (sankaku-gatame) or tighten the triangle for a choke.","defense":"They keep their elbows tight to their knees so you can't insert your leg.","mistake":"Rolling before the triangle is locked. They slip out as you roll.","drill":"Sankaku entries on a turtled partner: 3 × 5, slow and controlled.","groups":["judo_ground","headlock"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Judo Sankaku","Triangle Turnover"],"rel":["turtle_top","triangle","rear_triangle"]}},{"id":"okuri_eri_jime","cat":"submission","name":"Okuri-Eri-Jime","tagline":"The basic gi choke from the back: one hand deep in the collar, the other pulling down the lapel.","tags":["Gi","Choke","Back Control","Judo"],"objective":"Choke from the back by pulling their own collar across their neck.","mechanics":"From behind, reach your choking hand around their neck and grip deep in the far collar, thumb inside. Your other hand goes under their armpit and pulls down the opposite lapel to tighten it. Pull the choking hand back across their neck while pulling the lapel down. The collar compresses both sides of the neck.","defense":"They pull down on the choking arm, tuck their chin and turn toward the choking side.","mistake":"A shallow first grip. The first hand has to be deep in the collar.","drill":"From back control: get the first grip in under 3 seconds. 3 × 5.","groups":["judo_ground","back"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","aka":["Sliding Collar Choke"],"rel":["bow_arrow","back_control","kata_ha_jime"]}},{"id":"kata_ha_jime","cat":"submission","name":"Kata-Ha-Jime","tagline":"Collar grip plus their arm lifted behind their head. A powerful choke from the back or turtle.","tags":["Gi","Choke","Back Control","Turtle"],"objective":"Choke with a deep collar grip while trapping their arm up so they can't defend.","mechanics":"Take a deep collar grip from behind as for okuri-eri-jime. Your other arm goes under their armpit, lifts their arm up and your hand slides behind their neck. Push their head forward with that hand while pulling the collar grip back. The lifted arm can't defend the choke.","defense":"They keep their elbow tight to their body so you can't lift the arm.","mistake":"Lifting the arm without pushing the head. The push behind the neck finishes it.","drill":"From the back or turtle: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo_ground","back","headlock"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","aka":["Single Wing Choke"],"rel":["okuri_eri_jime","bow_arrow","clock_choke"]}},{"id":"spider_guard","cat":"position","name":"Spider Guard","tagline":"Both sleeves gripped, feet on the biceps. You steer their arms with your legs.","tags":["Gi","Open Guard","Sleeve Grips"],"objective":"Control both of their arms with sleeve grips and feet on the biceps, so you can off-balance them and set up sweeps and triangles.","mechanics":"Grip both sleeves at the wrist with a pistol or four-finger grip. Put the soles of your feet on the inside of their biceps, knees pointing out. Pull your sleeve grips toward you as you push with your feet, stretching their arms. Keep your hips off the mat slightly and move them to angle off. Change to one foot on the hip, or a lasso, when they adjust.","defense":"They break the grips, step back to straighten your legs, or pin your foot to their hip and pass.","mistake":"Pushing with your feet but not pulling the sleeves. Without tension in both directions, the guard is loose.","drill":"Spider guard retention: partner tries to break grips and pass at 50% for 1 minute. 3 rounds.","groups":["gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","rel":["lasso_guard","spider_sweep","triangle","collar_sleeve"]}},{"id":"lasso_guard","cat":"position","name":"Lasso Guard","tagline":"Your leg wrapped around their arm, sleeve in hand. One of the hardest guards to break.","tags":["Gi","Open Guard","Sleeve Grips"],"objective":"Lock one of their arms with your leg wrapped around it, so they can't free it or pass on that side.","mechanics":"Grip their sleeve. Wrap your leg around the outside of their arm, over the top and under, so your shin crosses their arm and your foot is on the inside of their bicep or across their chest. Keep your knee pointing out to tighten the wrap. Your other foot goes on their hip, bicep or knee. From here, sweep toward the lasso side or attack an omoplata.","defense":"They stack you, drive their knee toward your hips, or walk to the opposite side of the lasso.","mistake":"A loose lasso with your knee pointing in. The knee pointing out is what locks the arm.","drill":"Lasso retention and sweep: 3 × 1 minute, sweep when they try to step around.","groups":["gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","rel":["spider_guard","lasso_sweep","omoplata"]}},{"id":"dlr_guard","cat":"position","name":"De La Riva Guard","tagline":"A hook around the outside of their lead leg. The base of modern open guard and the berimbolo.","tags":["Open Guard","Hook","Berimbolo"],"objective":"Hook their lead leg from the outside so you can off-balance them, sweep or get underneath them.","mechanics":"Wrap your outside leg around the outside of their lead leg, your foot hooking the inside of their thigh. Grip the ankle of the same leg with your same-side hand (or their trouser cuff). Your other foot pushes their far hip or bicep, or you grip a sleeve or collar. Keep your hips close to their ankle. The hook pulls their knee out while the other foot pushes, so they can't stand stable.","defense":"They step back to break the hook, or knee-cut over your hook and pass.","mistake":"Sitting too far from their foot. The hook only works when your hip is right next to their ankle.","drill":"DLR off-balancing: partner stands, you stay connected and make them post their hands. 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["gi_guard","open"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["DLR"],"rel":["rdlr_guard","dlr_sweep","berimbolo","x_guard","slx"]}},{"id":"rdlr_guard","cat":"position","name":"Reverse De La Riva","tagline":"The hook goes inside their lead leg. Good against pressure passers who try to knee-cut.","tags":["Open Guard","Hook","Inversion"],"objective":"Hook the inside of their lead leg to block a knee-cut pass and set up sweeps, back takes and leg entries.","mechanics":"Thread your outside leg between their legs and hook your foot around the outside of their lead leg from the inside. Hold their ankle, sleeve or collar. Your other leg frames on their hip or knee. Turn your hips toward them, keeping your knee pointing in. From here, roll under for the kiss of the dragon, sweep them back, or enter a leg entanglement.","defense":"They drop their weight on your hook, square their hips and pass to the opposite side.","mistake":"Letting their knee come across your hips. Once the knee crosses, the guard is gone.","drill":"RDLR retention against the knee cut: 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["gi_guard","open"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["RDLR"],"rel":["dlr_guard","kiss_of_the_dragon","berimbolo"]}},{"id":"collar_sleeve","cat":"position","name":"Collar-Sleeve Guard","tagline":"One hand on the collar, one on the sleeve, one foot on the bicep. Simple, safe and full of sweeps.","tags":["Gi","Open Guard","Grips"],"objective":"Control their posture with the collar and one arm with the sleeve, then sweep or switch to another guard.","mechanics":"Grip their collar deep with one hand and the opposite sleeve with the other. Put the foot on the sleeve side against their bicep. Your other foot hooks behind their knee, sits on their hip, or goes into a De La Riva hook. Pull the collar to break their posture and push the bicep to stop them reaching your legs.","defense":"They posture up and break the collar grip, or step their leg back away from your foot.","mistake":"A shallow collar grip. A deep collar grip controls their posture; a shallow one is easily broken.","drill":"Collar-sleeve sweep chain: 3 × 8 of tripod and sickle sweeps.","groups":["gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi","rel":["spider_guard","dlr_guard","tripod_sweep","guard_pull"]}},{"id":"worm_guard","cat":"position","name":"Worm Guard","tagline":"Their own lapel wrapped around their leg. A grip they can't break because it's tied to them.","tags":["Gi","Open Guard","Lapel"],"objective":"Pull their lapel out and wrap it around their leg so you have a near-unbreakable connection for sweeps and back takes.","mechanics":"From De La Riva, pull their lapel out from under their belt. Feed it behind their lead leg from the inside to the outside and grip it with your hand, or pass it to your other hand. Their leg is now tied to their own lapel. Use the tension to pull them forward and off balance, sweep them, or come up under them for the back.","defense":"They keep their lapel tucked in, or pull their leg back before you feed it.","mistake":"Feeding the lapel loose. Take out the slack so the lapel is tight around the leg.","drill":"Lapel feed: 3 × 8 from De La Riva against a static partner.","groups":["gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi","aka":["Lapel Guard"],"rel":["dlr_guard","rdlr_guard","berimbolo"]}},{"id":"spider_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"Spider Guard Sweep","tagline":"Stretch one arm, take out a leg, and they fall into your sweep.","tags":["Gi","Spider","Sweep"],"objective":"Use the spider grips to stretch them in one direction and remove their base leg in the other.","mechanics":"From spider guard, pull one sleeve while pushing the bicep with that foot to stretch them to one side. Release the other foot from their bicep and hook it behind their ankle on the same side. Pull the ankle toward you while pushing with the spider foot. They fall back toward the side with no support. Come up on top.","defense":"They step back with the hooked leg or lean into the spider foot.","mistake":"Pushing them straight back. Stretch them diagonally, toward their weak corner.","drill":"Spider sweep: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","aka":["Spider Tripod Sweep"],"rel":["spider_guard","tripod_sweep"]}},{"id":"lasso_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"Lasso Sweep","tagline":"Push the lasso arm away and pull their leg. They roll over toward the trapped arm.","tags":["Gi","Lasso","Sweep"],"objective":"Use the lasso to keep one arm trapped, then remove a leg so they fall toward the side they can't post on.","mechanics":"From lasso guard, put your free foot on their hip on the non-lasso side. Push with the lasso leg to drive their trapped arm across, while pulling the sleeve. Hook their far ankle with your free hand or foot and pull it. They fall toward the trapped arm side, with no hand to post. Follow them over to the top.","defense":"They lean their weight to the free side or step back.","mistake":"Losing the sleeve grip as you sweep. Without the sleeve the lasso unwraps.","drill":"Lasso sweep: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","rel":["lasso_guard","spider_sweep","omoplata"]}},{"id":"dlr_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"De La Riva Sweep","tagline":"Hook, pull and push. They fall back over their trapped leg.","tags":["Open Guard","DLR","Sweep"],"objective":"Use the De La Riva hook to off-balance them backward and come up on top.","mechanics":"From De La Riva, grip their far sleeve or collar. Put your free foot on their far hip. Pull with your grip as you push their hip and extend the DLR hook. Their weight goes onto their back foot. Sit up toward their trapped leg, grab it and drive them back over it, or roll them backward with the hook.","defense":"They base out with their back foot or step out of the hook.","mistake":"Pushing them back without holding the trapped leg. They just step back.","drill":"DLR sweep: 3 × 8 against a partner who stands and resists at 50%. Then rounds where you must sweep within 30 seconds.","groups":["gi_guard","open"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["dlr_guard","berimbolo","tripod_sweep"]}},{"id":"tripod_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"Tripod Sweep","tagline":"Pull the ankle, push the hip. One of the first open-guard sweeps to learn.","tags":["Open Guard","Sweep","Ankle Grip"],"objective":"Pull one leg toward you and push their other hip away, so they fall back.","mechanics":"Grip their ankle on one side (or the trouser cuff). Put that same-side foot hooked behind their ankle, and the other foot on their hip or the opposite thigh. Pull the ankle as you push the hip with your foot. They have nothing behind them and fall back. Sit up and follow them to the top.","defense":"They lean into you to stay balanced, or step back with the hooked leg.","mistake":"Pushing with the foot without pulling the ankle. Both actions at the same moment.","drill":"Tripod sweep: 3 × 8 each side, then partner leans forward on every third rep so you switch to the sickle sweep.","groups":["open","gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["sickle_sweep","collar_sleeve","dlr_sweep"]}},{"id":"sickle_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"Sickle Sweep","tagline":"Hold the ankle, sweep the back of their other leg. The partner of the tripod sweep.","tags":["Open Guard","Sweep"],"objective":"When they defend the tripod sweep by leaning forward, sweep the back of their other leg.","mechanics":"From the tripod position, hold their ankle. Instead of pushing the hip, swing your free leg behind their other heel like a sickle. Pull the ankle toward you and sweep the heel. They fall backward. Use it when they lean forward to defend the tripod.","defense":"They step the leg away from the sickle or sprawl their hips back.","mistake":"Sweeping their calf instead of their heel. Low contact gives the most leverage.","drill":"Tripod and sickle chain: 3 × 10, switching sweeps on the partner's reaction.","groups":["open","gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["tripod_sweep","collar_sleeve"]}},{"id":"balloon_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"Balloon Sweep","tagline":"Feet on their hips, roll back and launch them over your head. BJJ's tomoe-nage.","tags":["Open Guard","Sweep","Feet on Hips"],"objective":"When they lean forward on you, put both feet on their hips and send them over your head.","mechanics":"Grip their sleeves or collar. Put both feet on their hips. Pull them forward over you as you roll back onto your shoulders. Extend your legs up and over your head to lift them. As they go over, keep your grips and roll back with them so you land in mount.","defense":"They keep their weight back and their hips low.","mistake":"Pushing them straight up. You must pull them forward over you first.","drill":"Balloon sweep with a cooperative partner on a soft mat: 3 × 5.","groups":["open","closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Overhead Sweep","Tomoe Sweep"],"rel":["tomoe_nage","hip_bump","flower_sweep"]}},{"id":"inverted_guard","cat":"position","name":"Inverted Guard","tagline":"Upside down on your shoulders, legs still facing them. Used to recover guard and to get underneath.","tags":["Open Guard","Inversion","Advanced"],"objective":"Keep your legs between you and the passer by rolling onto your shoulders, and use the inversion to attack the back or legs.","mechanics":"When they pass around your legs, roll onto your shoulders, rotating your hips so your legs keep facing them. Keep your chin tucked and your weight on your shoulders, not your neck. Use your legs to hook and frame. From the inversion, come back to an open guard, enter a leg entanglement, or roll under them for a back take.","defense":"They pressure down into your hips to stack you, or move to the side you are rolling away from.","mistake":"Inverting onto your neck. Only invert if your shoulders and neck are ready; build it up slowly.","drill":"Solo inversions on a soft mat: 3 × 10 each side, slowly. Never under a heavy stack.","groups":["open"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Inversion"],"rel":["berimbolo","guard_retention","kiss_of_the_dragon"]}},{"id":"flower_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"Flower Sweep","tagline":"Swing your leg like a pendulum and roll them toward the arm they can't post with.","tags":["Closed Guard","Sweep"],"objective":"Trap one of their arms and remove the leg on that side, then use a leg swing to roll them over.","mechanics":"From closed guard, control their sleeve or wrist on one side and hook your arm under their opposite leg. Open your guard and swing your free leg high like a pendulum, then down. At the same time pull them toward the trapped arm side and lift the leg you're holding. They roll over toward the trapped arm. Follow them up into mount.","defense":"They posture up, widen their knees or post their free hand.","mistake":"Forgetting the arm control. They post with that hand and the sweep stops.","drill":"Flower sweep: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Pendulum Sweep"],"rel":["hip_bump","scissor","armbar","guard_closed"]}},{"id":"overhook_guard","cat":"position","name":"Overhook Guard","tagline":"Overhook their arm from closed guard. It stops them posturing and sets up triangles and armbars.","tags":["Closed Guard","Overhook","Control"],"objective":"Clamp one of their arms with an overhook to break their posture and attack from that grip.","mechanics":"From closed guard, wrap your arm over their arm and grip your own collar, their collar, or clamp it tight to your side. Pull their head down with your other hand. Shift your hips to the overhook side. From here, the arm can't escape, which sets up the triangle, armbar and omoplata.","defense":"They posture up hard, push their arm deeper to stack, or punch their arm free.","mistake":"An overhook with no hip angle. Shift your hips toward the overhook to make it tight.","drill":"Overhook to triangle: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Whizzer Guard","Closed Guard Overhook"],"rel":["guard_closed","triangle","omoplata","armbar"]}},{"id":"rubber_guard","cat":"position","name":"Rubber Guard","tagline":"Your leg high over their shoulder, held by your arm. Strong posture control — but it needs flexible hips.","tags":["Closed Guard","Flexibility","Advanced"],"objective":"Hold their posture down with your leg high across their back, setting up omoplatas, triangles and gogoplatas.","mechanics":"From closed guard, break their posture. Bring one leg high over their shoulder and across their upper back. Grab your own shin with the opposite hand to hold it there — this is the mission control position. Your other leg is on their hip or back. From here, rotate for an omoplata, step to a triangle, or slide your shin across their throat for a gogoplata.","defense":"They posture up, stack you, or step up to stand.","mistake":"Forcing the position without the flexibility for it. Knee injuries are common; build mobility first.","drill":"Only with good hip mobility: entries from closed guard 3 × 5 each side, slowly.","groups":["closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["High Guard"],"rel":["guard_closed","gogoplata","omoplata","triangle"]}},{"id":"gogoplata","cat":"submission","name":"Gogoplata","tagline":"A choke with your shin across their throat. Rare, but it catches people in rubber guard.","tags":["Choke","Rubber Guard","Advanced"],"objective":"Push your shin across the front of their throat and pull their head down onto it.","mechanics":"From rubber guard, slide your foot across under their chin so your shin is across their throat. Grab the back of their head with both hands, or grip your own foot, and pull their head down onto the shin. Your hips must be close under their chin. Check your ruleset — it is illegal for many lower belt levels.","defense":"They posture up before the shin seats or turn their head to the side.","mistake":"Trying it without the flexibility to get your shin across. Don't force the leg.","drill":"Slow and controlled from rubber guard: 3 × 3 each side.","groups":["closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["rubber_guard","omoplata","triangle"]}},{"id":"cross_collar_choke","cat":"submission","name":"Cross Collar Choke","tagline":"Both hands deep in their collar, wrists crossed. The first gi choke most people learn.","tags":["Gi","Choke","Closed Guard","Mount"],"objective":"Grip deep on both sides of their collar and pull your elbows out so the collar squeezes both sides of the neck.","mechanics":"Get the first hand deep into their collar, thumb inside, palm up, all the way behind their neck. The second hand goes into the other side of the collar, crossing over the first arm (thumb in or fingers in). Pull your elbows apart and toward the mat, bringing their head down. From closed guard, pull them down with your legs; from mount, drop your forehead to the mat beside their head.","defense":"They posture up, push your elbows together, or block the second grip.","mistake":"A shallow first grip. The deeper the first hand, the tighter the choke.","drill":"First grip depth: 3 × 10. Then the full choke from guard and mount, 3 × 5.","groups":["closed","mount"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi","aka":["Juji-Jime","X-Choke"],"rel":["guard_closed","mount","loop_choke","ezekiel_choke"]}},{"id":"loop_choke","cat":"submission","name":"Loop Choke","tagline":"One collar grip and their own head does the rest. Catches people who duck their head while passing.","tags":["Gi","Choke","Front Headlock"],"objective":"Grip their collar, loop your arm over their neck and choke as they push forward.","mechanics":"Grab their collar on the far side, deep and with your thumb inside. When their head comes down, push their head through the loop of your arm and bring your other arm over the back of their neck. Turn your choking wrist and roll or turn toward the gripping side, pulling them down. The collar and your forearm squeeze both sides of the neck.","defense":"They keep their head up, posture, or turn their head toward the gripping hand.","mistake":"Too much slack in the collar grip. Take the slack out before you loop.","drill":"Loop choke from guard and from front headlock: 3 × 5 each.","groups":["closed","headlock"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","rel":["cross_collar_choke","guillotine","clock_choke"]}},{"id":"knee_shield","cat":"position","name":"Knee Shield Half Guard","tagline":"Your knee across their chest keeps them away while you work the underhook.","tags":["Half Guard","Frame","Distance"],"objective":"Hold distance with a knee frame so they can't flatten you, and use it to set up sweeps and recover full guard.","mechanics":"From half guard, put your top knee across their chest or hip, shin angled across their body. Hold their collar, wrist or the back of the head. Your bottom leg holds their leg in half guard. Stay on your side, never flat. Use the frame to make space, then go for the underhook, a sweep or full guard recovery.","defense":"They flatten the knee, crossface, or go around the knee to pass.","mistake":"Lying flat on your back with the knee shield. Stay on your side.","drill":"Knee shield retention: partner tries to flatten the knee for 1 minute. 3 rounds.","groups":["half"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Z-Guard"],"rel":["half_guard_bottom","knee_shield_pass","dogfight","kimura_trap"]}},{"id":"deep_half","cat":"position","name":"Deep Half Guard","tagline":"Get your whole body underneath their leg. Hard to pass, easy to sweep from.","tags":["Half Guard","Underneath","Sweeps"],"objective":"Go underneath their hips and hug their leg, so their weight is over you and they can't base out.","mechanics":"From half guard, slide your head and shoulders under their hips toward their trapped leg. Wrap both arms around their thigh. Your legs keep their leg trapped, often crossed or in a figure-four. Your body is now under their centre of mass. Push their hips over you with your legs or come out the back for a sweep.","defense":"They put their weight back, step their free leg away, or attack your legs.","mistake":"Going deep with your head exposed to a guillotine or crossface. Get under quickly and keep your head tight to their leg.","drill":"Deep half entries: 3 × 8 from regular half guard.","groups":["half"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["half_guard_bottom","waiter_sweep","old_school"]}},{"id":"waiter_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"Waiter Sweep","tagline":"From deep half, lift their free leg like a tray and roll them over.","tags":["Deep Half","Sweep"],"objective":"Lift their free leg from underneath so they lose base and fall to the side.","mechanics":"From deep half, hug their trapped leg with one arm. With your other hand, reach to the inside of their free leg's ankle or knee and lift it up like carrying a tray. At the same time push their trapped leg away with your legs. They fall to their side. Come up on top.","defense":"They keep their free leg back out of reach, or sprawl their weight onto you.","mistake":"Lifting the leg without moving their hips with your legs. The two must happen together.","drill":"Waiter sweep: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["half"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["deep_half","electric_chair"]}},{"id":"lockdown","cat":"position","name":"Lockdown","tagline":"Lock their trapped leg in a figure-four with your legs and stretch it. They can't pass while it's held.","tags":["Half Guard","No-Gi","Leg Control"],"objective":"Hold their leg completely still from half guard, then stretch it to break their posture and sweep.","mechanics":"From half guard, wrap your outside leg over their trapped leg and hook your foot under your other ankle, locking their leg between your legs. Extend your legs back to stretch their leg straight — the whip-up. They lose base. Combine with an underhook or double underhook on their body to sweep.","defense":"They keep their leg bent and their hips heavy, or turn and kick the leg free.","mistake":"Holding the lockdown without the underhook. Without the upper-body connection they crossface you flat.","drill":"Lockdown and whip-up: 3 × 8.","groups":["half"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["half_guard_bottom","electric_chair","old_school"]}},{"id":"electric_chair","cat":"sweep","name":"Electric Chair","tagline":"From the lockdown, lift their other leg and split them. It sweeps or submits.","tags":["Half Guard","Lockdown","Sweep","Submission"],"objective":"Use the lockdown on one leg while lifting the other, stretching their hips until they fall or tap.","mechanics":"From the lockdown, go under to deep half. Reach for their far leg and lift it onto your shoulder. Keep the lockdown on the trapped leg. Extend your legs to stretch one leg while pulling the other leg up and away. They fall to the side (sweep) or their hips stretch into a submission. Apply the stretch slowly.","defense":"They keep their free leg back and their weight down, or turn to face you.","mistake":"Losing the lockdown as you reach for the far leg. Keep the legs locked throughout.","drill":"Electric chair: 3 × 5 each side, controlled and slow on the stretch.","groups":["half"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["lockdown","waiter_sweep","banana_split"]}},{"id":"dogfight","cat":"position","name":"Dogfight","tagline":"Half guard on your knees with the underhook. A wrestling fight you can win.","tags":["Half Guard","Underhook","Wrestling"],"objective":"Come up from half guard to your knees with an underhook, then take their back, sweep or take them down.","mechanics":"From half guard bottom, get the underhook and come up onto your elbow, then your knee. Keep their leg trapped between yours. Your head goes into their chest or under their chin. From here, drive forward to come up on top, take their back by going behind, or reach for their far leg for a single leg.","defense":"They whizzer the underhook, crossface, or sprawl their weight onto you.","mistake":"Coming up without the underhook. You get crossfaced back down.","drill":"Half guard to dogfight: 3 × 8. Add finishing the sweep or back take.","groups":["half"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["half_guard_bottom","old_school","wrestle_up"]}},{"id":"half_guard_top","cat":"position","name":"Half Guard Top","tagline":"Win the underhook and the crossface, flatten them, then free your leg.","tags":["Half Guard","Top","Pressure"],"objective":"Flatten them with a crossface and underhook so they can't move, then free your trapped leg and pass.","mechanics":"Crossface: your arm across their jaw, gripping behind their far shoulder. Underhook their far arm and keep your head low on that side. Flatten them onto their back with chest pressure. Now free your leg: use your other foot to push their knee down, or walk your trapped leg out. Slide your knee across into side control or mount.","defense":"They fight for the underhook, frame against your neck, or come up to a dogfight.","mistake":"Trying to free your leg before they're flat. Flatten first, then pass.","drill":"Half guard top: flatten and pass in under a minute. 5 rounds.","groups":["half","passing"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Passing Half Guard"],"rel":["cross_face","smash_pass","knee_shield_pass","half_guard_bottom"]}},{"id":"standing_guard_break","cat":"pass","name":"Breaking the Closed Guard","tagline":"You can't pass a closed guard until it's open. Posture first, then open the legs.","tags":["Passing","Closed Guard","Posture"],"objective":"Establish posture so you're safe from attacks, then open their ankles — kneeling or standing — and start passing.","mechanics":"Posture: hips forward, back straight, head up, both hands on their hips or belt. Kneeling break: put one knee into their tailbone, step the other leg back, and push their knee down with your elbow until the ankles open. Standing break: control both sleeves or one hand on their chest, step up one foot at a time, stand tall and drop your hips back so their ankles slide open.","defense":"They break your posture with their legs and collar grips, or attack with armbars and triangles as you open.","mistake":"Trying to open the guard with your posture broken. Fix your posture first, every time.","drill":"Closed guard break: 3 × 1 minute, partner tries to break your posture while you open the guard.","groups":["passing","closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Guard Opening","Standing Guard Break"],"rel":["guard_closed","guard_bottom_closed_detail","over_under"]}},{"id":"headquarters","cat":"position","name":"Headquarters Position","tagline":"A knee between their legs, pinning one leg. The hub most modern passes start from.","tags":["Passing","Leg Pin","Position"],"objective":"Pin one of their legs to the mat with your knee between their legs, so you can pass to either side.","mechanics":"Step your lead knee between their legs and pin their inside leg to the mat with your shin or knee. Your back foot is out wide for base. Your hands control their knees or hips. From here, knee slice to one side, long step to the other, leg weave, or backstep. Keep your hips low and your weight on the pinned leg.","defense":"They pummel their knee back inside, recover a hook, or invert.","mistake":"Standing too tall in HQ. Low hips keep the leg pinned.","drill":"HQ passing: 3 × 1 minute, pass to either side based on their reaction.","groups":["passing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["HQ"],"rel":["knee_slice","long_step_pass","leg_weave_pass","backstep_pass"]}},{"id":"long_step_pass","cat":"pass","name":"Long Step Pass","tagline":"Step your trapped leg back and over, landing on the other side in side control.","tags":["Passing","Leg Pin"],"objective":"When they block your knee slice, step around to the other side of their legs.","mechanics":"From HQ or half guard, put your weight on your hands on their knee and hip. Step your trapped leg back in a long arc behind you and around to the opposite side. Your hips swing around and you drop to that side, facing their head. Settle your chest onto theirs in side control.","defense":"They follow you with their legs and re-guard, or grab your leg as you step.","mistake":"Stepping without your weight on them. Without pressure they turn and recover guard.","drill":"Knee slice to long step chain: 3 × 8.","groups":["passing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["headquarters","knee_slice","leg_drag"]}},{"id":"x_pass","cat":"pass","name":"X-Pass","tagline":"Push their knee one way and step to the other side. A fast standing pass.","tags":["Passing","Speed Pass","Standing"],"objective":"From standing, push their knees in one direction and step around the other way to the side.","mechanics":"Stand in front of their open guard. Grip their knee or pants and push it to one side. Step your leg diagonally across toward the other side, crossing your feet in an X. Drop your weight around their legs and land in side control or knee on belly.","defense":"They follow you with their legs and catch a hook, or shrimp away.","mistake":"Stepping before you move their knees. Move the legs out of the way first.","drill":"X-pass: 3 × 8 each side against a seated guard, then rounds where the guard player follows your step and you must re-enter to the opposite side.","groups":["passing"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["torreando","leg_drag","long_step_pass"]}},{"id":"leg_weave_pass","cat":"pass","name":"Leg Weave Pass","tagline":"Weave your arm under one leg and pin the other. Their legs stack together and can't move.","tags":["Passing","Pressure","Leg Pin"],"objective":"Trap both of their legs together so they can't retain guard, then walk around to side control.","mechanics":"From HQ, put your knee on their inside leg. Weave your arm under their other leg, lifting it onto your shoulder or hip. Pin the bottom leg with your knee and push the top leg across. Their legs are stacked and pinned. Walk your hips around to side control.","defense":"They kick the woven leg free, or get their bottom knee back in between you.","mistake":"Letting the bottom leg go free. Keep it pinned the whole time.","drill":"Leg weave from HQ: 3 × 6 each side.","groups":["passing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["headquarters","over_under","smash_pass"]}},{"id":"backstep_pass","cat":"pass","name":"Backstep","tagline":"Spin your back toward them to free a trapped leg. It passes or enters a leg entanglement.","tags":["Passing","Leg Entanglement","Advanced"],"objective":"When they hold your leg in half guard, step backward over their leg to free yourself and pass or attack.","mechanics":"From HQ or half guard, put your weight on your hands. Step your free leg back over their trapped leg, turning your back toward them. Your hips switch direction. You either free your leg and land beside them, or end up in a saddle or 50/50 with a leg attack.","defense":"They follow you and catch your back, or hold your leg in a leg entanglement of their own.","mistake":"Exposing your back too long. The step is fast and you face them again immediately.","drill":"Backstep from HQ: 3 × 6, slowly, then at speed.","groups":["passing","legs"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["headquarters","saddle","knee_slice"]}},{"id":"pressure_passing","cat":"concept","name":"Pressure vs Speed Passing","tagline":"Two passing styles: crush them flat, or move faster than their legs. Elite passers mix both.","tags":["Passing","Strategy"],"objective":"Know when to pressure and when to move, and switch between them.","mechanics":"Pressure passing: get chest to chest or pin their hips, take away their space, and move slowly around their legs (over-under, smash, body lock). Speed passing: stay standing, move their legs out of the way and go around before they recover (torreando, X-pass, leg drag). When they push you away, switch to pressure. When they cling to you, switch to speed.","defense":"Against pressure passers they invert and frame; against speed passers they stay connected to the legs.","mistake":"Using one style only. Good guard players adapt to it within a minute.","drill":"Pass for 1 minute pressure-only, 1 minute speed-only, 1 minute mixed. 3 rounds.","groups":["passing","concepts"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["smash_pass","torreando","over_under","x_pass"]}},{"id":"side_to_mount","cat":"transition","name":"Side Control to Mount","tagline":"Slide your knee across their belly and you're in mount. The most common positional advance.","tags":["Transition","Side Control","Mount"],"objective":"Move from side control to mount without giving them a chance to recover half guard.","mechanics":"From side control, block their near hip with your hand so they can't turn in. Keep your chest on theirs. Slide your near knee across their belly, low and tight. When your knee reaches the mat on the other side, sit up into mount. If their knee blocks you, walk it down with your hand first.","defense":"They put their knee up to block, or trap your sliding leg in half guard.","mistake":"Lifting your hips as you move your knee. Keep your weight on them.","drill":"Side to mount: 3 × 8. Partner blocks with a knee every few reps.","groups":["side","mount","transitions"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Knee Slide to Mount"],"rel":["side_control","mount","knee_on_belly"]}},{"id":"far_side_armbar","cat":"submission","name":"Far-Side Armbar","tagline":"Step over their head and armbar the far arm when they push you away.","tags":["Armbar","Side Control"],"objective":"When they push on your face or hips from bottom side control, catch the far arm and step over their head.","mechanics":"From side control, when their far arm pushes or reaches, trap it with your arm. Step your near leg over their head while you sit back toward their far side. Squeeze your knees together on the arm. Lie back and lift your hips, thumb pointing up.","defense":"They pull the arm back, turn into you, or hold their hands together.","mistake":"Stepping over without trapping the arm first. They pull it out as you move.","drill":"Far-side armbar: 3 × 6 each side.","groups":["side"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Step-Over Armbar"],"rel":["armbar","side_control","kimura"]}},{"id":"von_flue_choke","cat":"submission","name":"Von Flue Choke","tagline":"They hold a guillotine from bottom side control. Your shoulder chokes them with their own arm.","tags":["Choke","Counter","Guillotine Counter"],"objective":"Counter a guillotine by passing to their opposite side and driving your shoulder into their neck.","mechanics":"When they hold a guillotine from guard, pass to the side opposite their choking arm. Their arm is now around your neck with you on top. Drive your shoulder down into the side of their neck, keeping your weight on it, until they release or tap.","defense":"They let go of the guillotine before you settle on their side.","mistake":"Trying it while the guillotine is still deep and tight. Pass and relieve pressure first.","drill":"Partner holds a loose guillotine; pass and finish the von flue. 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["side","headlock"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["guillotine","guillotine_escape","side_control"]}},{"id":"paper_cutter_choke","cat":"submission","name":"Paper Cutter Choke","tagline":"A collar choke from side control: one hand deep, forearm across the throat.","tags":["Gi","Choke","Side Control"],"objective":"Choke them from side control with a collar grip and your forearm cutting across their neck.","mechanics":"From side control, slide your near hand deep into their far collar, thumb inside. Bring your other forearm over their neck, across the throat like a paper cutter. Drop your weight and pull the collar grip while you drive the forearm down.","defense":"They block the collar grip or turn into you.","mistake":"Pushing with the forearm only. Pull the collar grip at the same time.","drill":"From side control: 3 × 5.","groups":["side"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","rel":["side_control","baseball_bat_choke","cross_collar_choke"]}},{"id":"baseball_bat_choke","cat":"submission","name":"Baseball Bat Choke","tagline":"Two hands on the collar like holding a bat, then spin around their head.","tags":["Gi","Choke","Side Control","Knee on Belly"],"objective":"Grip their collar with both hands like a baseball bat and rotate to tighten.","mechanics":"Grip deep in their collar with one hand, thumb in. Grip the other side of the collar with the second hand, thumb out, so your hands are like holding a bat. Then step around their head or roll over them toward their head. The rotation closes the collar on both sides of the neck.","defense":"They turn into you, block your second grip, or follow you as you rotate.","mistake":"Grips not deep enough. Both hands must be close to their neck.","drill":"From knee on belly: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["side","mount"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","rel":["paper_cutter_choke","knee_on_belly","cross_collar_choke"]}},{"id":"twister_side","cat":"position","name":"Twister Side Control","tagline":"Side control facing their legs with their legs trapped. A path to the twister.","tags":["Side Control","Twister","Advanced"],"objective":"Control them from the side facing their legs with one leg trapped, setting up the twister and the back.","mechanics":"From side control, switch your hips so you face their legs. Trap their near leg between your legs. Your arms control their far arm or head. From here, take the back or work toward the truck and twister.","defense":"They turn into you and recover guard, or free the trapped leg.","mistake":"Losing upper-body control while facing their legs. Keep their far arm or head.","drill":"Twister side entry: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["side"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["twister","truck","side_control"]}},{"id":"knee_on_belly_escape","cat":"defence","name":"Knee on Belly Escape","tagline":"Push the knee off, turn to your side and get your guard back.","tags":["Escape","Knee on Belly"],"objective":"Remove their knee from your stomach and recover guard before they settle.","mechanics":"Push their knee down and away from you with both hands. At the same time, turn onto your side and shrimp your hips away from their knee. As space opens, bring your knee in between you and recover guard. Alternatively, push their knee toward their back and turn toward them to come up.","defense":"They switch to mount or side control as soon as you turn.","mistake":"Pushing up on their knee. Push it down and to the side.","drill":"Partner holds knee on belly; escape to guard within 15 seconds. 5 rounds.","groups":["side","defence"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["knee_on_belly","side_control_escape","guard_recovery"]}},{"id":"north_south_escape","cat":"defence","name":"North-South Escape","tagline":"Protect your neck from the choke, frame their hips and turn to your knees or guard.","tags":["Escape","North-South"],"objective":"Escape north-south safely, starting by preventing the choke.","mechanics":"First, keep your near arm inside to stop the north-south choke, hand by your neck. Frame against their hips with your other arm. Turn onto your side, away from the choke side, and shrimp to make space. Come up to your knees facing them or bring your knee in for guard.","defense":"They attack the north-south choke or kimura as you turn.","mistake":"Turning without protecting your neck. You walk into the choke.","drill":"From north-south: escape within 20 seconds. 5 rounds.","groups":["side","defence"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["north_south","north_south_choke","side_control_escape"]}},{"id":"s_mount","cat":"position","name":"S-Mount","tagline":"One leg up by their head, the other under their arm. The setup for the mounted armbar.","tags":["Mount","Armbar","High Mount"],"objective":"Isolate one of their arms from high mount so you can finish an armbar.","mechanics":"From high mount, move one knee up next to their head. Your other leg slides under their arm, foot near their hip, forming an S shape with your legs. Your body is upright and their arm is trapped against your chest. From here, swing your leg over their head for the armbar.","defense":"They pull the arm back, turn into you, or bridge.","mistake":"Sitting back on their belly. Stay high on their chest with your hips over their arm.","drill":"High mount to S-mount to armbar: 3 × 6 each side.","groups":["mount"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["mount","armbar","technical_mount"]}},{"id":"technical_mount","cat":"position","name":"Technical Mount","tagline":"Mount where they've turned to their side. A step from the back.","tags":["Mount","Back Take"],"objective":"Stay on top when they turn to their side, and take the back or return to mount.","mechanics":"When they turn to their side to escape, keep one knee by their head and the other leg behind their back. Your hips stay on their hip. From here, insert a hook and take their back, or attack the arm. Keep your weight on them so they can't turn further.","defense":"They turn back to face you or come up to their knees.","mistake":"Letting your hips come off them. They shrimp out.","drill":"Mount to technical mount to back: 3 × 6.","groups":["mount","back"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["mount","back_control","mount_to_back"]}},{"id":"mount_to_back","cat":"transition","name":"Mount to Back Take","tagline":"When they turn from mount, they give you their back. Take it.","tags":["Transition","Mount","Back"],"objective":"When they turn away from you to escape mount, take their back with hooks or a body triangle.","mechanics":"As they turn onto their side, grab a seatbelt grip from behind. Slide your bottom leg in as a hook as you fall to your side. Bring your top leg over as the second hook. If they keep turning, follow them to their stomach and flatten them, or roll to your side with both hooks.","defense":"They turn back toward you or keep their elbows tight to block the seatbelt.","mistake":"Chasing the hooks before the seatbelt. Upper body first.","drill":"Partner turns from mount on a signal; take the back. 3 × 8.","groups":["mount","back","transitions"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["mount","technical_mount","back_control","gift_wrap"]}},{"id":"gift_wrap","cat":"position","name":"Gift Wrap","tagline":"Wrap their arm across their own neck. They can't defend their back or their neck with it.","tags":["Mount","Arm Control","Back Take"],"objective":"Trap one of their arms across their neck, then take the back or finish a choke.","mechanics":"From mount, grab their wrist and push it across their neck. Reach behind their head and grab the same wrist with your other hand. Their arm is wrapped across their neck. Now roll them toward the trapped arm and take their back, or attack the choke.","defense":"They pull the arm back before you secure the grip, or turn toward you.","mistake":"Pushing the arm without catching it behind the head. They pull it free.","drill":"Gift wrap to back: 3 × 6 each side.","groups":["mount","back"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["mount","mount_to_back","rnc"]}},{"id":"mounted_triangle","cat":"submission","name":"Mounted Triangle","tagline":"A triangle locked from on top. Hard to escape, and it often leads to an armbar.","tags":["Triangle","Mount","Choke"],"objective":"From high mount, trap one arm and their head in a triangle with your legs.","mechanics":"From high mount, push one of their arms up toward their head. Slide your knee over the arm and up beside their head, then bring your other leg across behind their head. Lock your legs into a triangle around their head and arm. Sit back and pull their head up while squeezing your knees.","defense":"They pull the arm down before your knee passes it, or bridge.","mistake":"Locking the triangle with their arm outside your legs. You need the arm and head inside.","drill":"High mount to mounted triangle: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["mount"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["triangle","mount","armbar","s_mount"]}},{"id":"ezekiel_choke","cat":"submission","name":"Ezekiel Choke","tagline":"A sleeve choke you can do from mount, and even from inside someone's guard.","tags":["Choke","Mount","Sleeve"],"objective":"Choke them using your forearm across their throat while your hand is anchored in your own sleeve.","mechanics":"From mount, wrap one arm behind their neck and grip inside your other sleeve (in no-gi, grab your wrist or forearm). Bring your other hand across their throat, blade of the forearm on their neck. Pull your arms together, driving the blade into their throat. In no-gi, the same arms work by gripping your own forearm.","defense":"They block the forearm, turn their head to the side or bridge.","mistake":"Placing the blade on their chin instead of their throat.","drill":"From mount: 3 × 5. Then in no-gi with the forearm grip.","groups":["mount","closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Sode Guruma Jime"],"rel":["mount","cross_collar_choke"]}},{"id":"seatbelt","cat":"position","name":"Seatbelt Grip","tagline":"One arm over the shoulder, one under the arm, hands locked at their chest. The grip that controls the back.","tags":["Back Control","Grip"],"objective":"Hold their upper body so you can control the back without needing hooks, and set up the choke.","mechanics":"From behind, one arm goes over their shoulder and across their chest. The other goes under their armpit and across. Lock your hands together at their chest, with the bottom hand gripping the top wrist. Keep your chest tight to their back and your head next to theirs on the under-arm side. This is the hub for every back attack.","defense":"They fight your top hand, pull your arms down, and turn toward the under-arm side.","mistake":"Holding your head on the over-arm side. Your head belongs on the under-arm side, where they try to escape.","drill":"Seatbelt control: partner tries to turn out for 1 minute. 5 rounds.","groups":["back","transitions"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Harness"],"rel":["back_control","rnc","back_take_turtle"]}},{"id":"short_choke","cat":"submission","name":"Short Choke","tagline":"A choke from the back when your arm isn't deep enough for the RNC.","tags":["Choke","Back Control"],"objective":"Finish a choke even when your forearm is on their jaw instead of under the chin.","mechanics":"From back control, with your choking arm across their jaw rather than under it, grip your own other hand or bicep. Pull your choking arm back into their neck while pushing their head forward or toward the arm with your other hand. Drive your chest into their back for extra pressure.","defense":"They tuck their chin harder or turn toward the choking arm.","mistake":"Cranking their jaw instead of compressing the neck. Make sure the pressure is on the neck.","drill":"From back control, when the RNC is blocked: 3 × 5.","groups":["back"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Short Arm Choke"],"rel":["rnc","back_control","seatbelt"]}},{"id":"rear_triangle","cat":"submission","name":"Rear Triangle","tagline":"Lock a triangle from the back around their head and arm. A strong finish when they defend the RNC.","tags":["Triangle","Back Control"],"objective":"Trap their head and one arm in a triangle with your legs from behind.","mechanics":"From back control, push one of their arms up and over your leg. Bring that leg around the front of their neck. Lock your other leg over your foot to make a triangle around their neck and arm. Squeeze your knees together and pull them back into you.","defense":"They keep their elbows tight to their body so you can't get your leg over the arm.","mistake":"Losing back control while setting up the triangle. Keep your hooks or seatbelt.","drill":"From back control: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["back"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Back Triangle"],"rel":["triangle","back_control","judo_sankaku"]}},{"id":"high_elbow_guillotine","cat":"submission","name":"High-Elbow Guillotine","tagline":"A guillotine with your elbow lifted high. The angle makes it tight from many positions.","tags":["Guillotine","Front Headlock","No-Gi"],"objective":"Choke from a front headlock by lifting your choking elbow so your forearm cuts up into their throat.","mechanics":"Wrap your arm around their neck from the front, forearm under their throat. Grip with your other hand in a palm-to-palm or a figure-four. Lift your choking elbow up high toward the ceiling, turning your forearm into their throat. Your chest pushes down on their head. Finish standing, from the front headlock, or by falling to guard.","defense":"They keep their head up, turn into you and posture, or get their hands on your wrist.","mistake":"Pulling the elbow down. The lift of the elbow is what tightens it.","drill":"From front headlock: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["headlock"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"No-Gi","aka":["Marcelotine"],"rel":["guillotine","arm_in_guillotine","front_headlock_td"]}},{"id":"arm_in_guillotine","cat":"submission","name":"Arm-In Guillotine","tagline":"A guillotine with one of their arms trapped inside. Harder to finish, harder to escape.","tags":["Guillotine","Front Headlock"],"objective":"Choke when their arm is inside your guillotine, using your shoulder and their own arm.","mechanics":"Wrap your arm around their neck and one of their arms, so the arm is inside the choke. Grip your hands together. Drive your shoulder and chest into them, closing their arm against their own neck. Squeeze your elbow toward your hip and arch. From guard, close your legs around their body.","defense":"They keep their trapped arm straight or turn into the arm-in side.","mistake":"Trying to finish it like a normal guillotine. It needs the shoulder and the angle.","drill":"From front headlock: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["headlock","closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["guillotine","high_elbow_guillotine","darce"]}},{"id":"peruvian_necktie","cat":"submission","name":"Peruvian Necktie","tagline":"A front headlock choke where your legs drive their head down. Brutal on a turtled opponent.","tags":["Choke","Turtle","Front Headlock","Advanced"],"objective":"Lock an arm-in grip from the front headlock, then drop your legs onto their back to finish the choke.","mechanics":"From the front headlock on a turtled opponent, wrap your arm around their neck and one arm, locking your hands. Sit to the side and bring your leg over their back and head. The other leg goes over the back too. Push down with your legs while pulling up with your arms.","defense":"They keep their head up, keep their arm out of the grip or roll toward you.","mistake":"Applying it with a weak grip. The grip must be tight before you bring your legs over.","drill":"From front headlock: 3 × 3 each side, slow and controlled.","groups":["headlock"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["darce","anaconda","front_headlock_td"]}},{"id":"japanese_necktie","cat":"submission","name":"Japanese Necktie","tagline":"A d'arce-style choke where you roll over their back. Very strong pressure.","tags":["Choke","Front Headlock","Advanced"],"objective":"Lock a d'arce-style grip on a turtled opponent and roll over their back to finish.","mechanics":"From a front headlock, slide your arm under their arm and around their neck, gripping like a d'arce. Lie across their back and press your chest down on their head and shoulder. Bring your legs out to the side and walk them around. The pressure from your chest finishes the choke.","defense":"They keep their head up, posture, or roll with you.","mistake":"Putting all the pressure on the arm squeeze. The chest pressure finishes it.","drill":"From front headlock: 3 × 3 each side.","groups":["headlock"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["darce","peruvian_necktie","anaconda"]}},{"id":"back_take_turtle","cat":"transition","name":"Back Take from Turtle","tagline":"Seatbelt first, then the hooks. The safest way into back control from turtle.","tags":["Back Take","Turtle","Hooks"],"objective":"From a turtled opponent, get the seatbelt grip, then put in your hooks without losing control.","mechanics":"From the side of a turtled opponent, slide your far arm under their far armpit and your near arm over their near shoulder. Lock the seatbelt. Put your near-side hook in at their hip. Roll toward the side of your under-arm, pulling them on top of you as you insert the second hook.","defense":"They keep their elbows tight to their knees, sit out, or stand up.","mistake":"Putting the hooks in before the seatbelt. They roll over the hooks and escape.","drill":"From turtle: seatbelt, hook, roll. 3 × 8.","groups":["headlock","back","transitions"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["turtle_top","back_control","seatbelt","spiral_ride"]}},{"id":"outside_ashi","cat":"position","name":"Outside Ashi-Garami","tagline":"Your outside leg crosses over their hip. More control of their knee line than standard ashi.","tags":["Leg Entanglement","Ashi-Garami"],"objective":"Control one of their legs with your outside leg over their hip, so you can attack the outside heel hook, ankle lock and toe hold.","mechanics":"Trap their leg between your legs. Your inside foot goes on their hip or under their buttock; your outside leg crosses over the outside of their hip, foot pointing into their other leg. Their knee is trapped between your thighs, pointing up or out. Hold their foot at your armpit. Keep your knees pinched to stop them turning out.","defense":"They turn toward the outside to free their knee, or step over your outside leg.","mistake":"Loose knees. If your thighs don't pinch, their knee slips free.","drill":"Outside ashi retention: partner tries to free their knee for 1 minute. 3 rounds each side.","groups":["legs"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"No-Gi","aka":["Outside Ashi","Outside Leg Control"],"rel":["ashi_inside","heel_hook_outside","ankle_lock","saddle"]}},{"id":"fifty_fifty","cat":"position","name":"50/50 Guard","tagline":"Both players have the same leg entanglement. Whoever controls the heel and the knee line first wins.","tags":["Leg Entanglement","Symmetrical"],"objective":"Hold a symmetrical leg entanglement while protecting your own heel and attacking theirs, or use it to sweep.","mechanics":"Your legs and theirs are crossed in a mirror image: your outside leg over their hip and your inside foot behind their leg, and the same for them. Hide your own heel by turning your foot and keeping your knee bent. Fight for the heel with your hands. From here, attack the inside heel hook, straight ankle lock or Estima lock, or come up on top.","defense":"Both players defend the same way: hide the heel, turn the knee and stand up or move to a better angle.","mistake":"Leaving your heel exposed while you attack. In 50/50 the counter is identical to your attack.","drill":"50/50 heel fight: 30-second rounds, first to secure the heel grip wins. 6 rounds.","groups":["legs"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["heel_hook_inside","ankle_lock","estima_lock","saddle"]}},{"id":"butterfly_ashi","cat":"position","name":"Butterfly Ashi-Garami","tagline":"A leg entanglement entered from butterfly guard. Quick and connected to sweeps.","tags":["Leg Entanglement","Butterfly"],"objective":"From butterfly guard, trap one leg with a butterfly hook and the other leg, setting up heel hooks and sweeps.","mechanics":"From butterfly guard, keep one butterfly hook inside their thigh. Swing your other leg over their other leg, hooking around their hip or knee. Their leg is trapped between your legs while the butterfly hook lifts the other. Attack the trapped heel or use the lift to sweep.","defense":"They step back out of the entanglement or drive their knee to the mat.","mistake":"Entering too far from their hips. Butterfly ashi needs you close.","drill":"Butterfly to butterfly ashi: 3 × 6 each side.","groups":["legs","open"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","aka":["Butterfly Ashi"],"rel":["butterfly","ashi_inside","heel_hook_outside"]}},{"id":"false_reap","cat":"position","name":"False Reap","tagline":"A leg position that connects heel hooks and back takes. Check your ruleset for reaping rules.","tags":["Leg Entanglement","Back Take","Advanced"],"objective":"Trap their leg with your outside leg across their thigh, setting up heel hooks, back takes and leg-to-back transitions.","mechanics":"From an open guard, put your inside leg across the front of their thigh, crossing their knee line. Your other leg hooks behind their knee. Hold their foot. This position lets you go to the saddle, attack the heel, or come up behind them for the back. Under some rulesets (IBJJF below brown belt), reaping is illegal.","defense":"They step over your leg, turn toward you to kill the angle or push your knee off.","mistake":"Using it in a ruleset where reaping is penalised. Know the rules.","drill":"False reap entries from open guard: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["legs"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["saddle","ashi_inside","back_control"]}},{"id":"truck","cat":"position","name":"Truck","tagline":"Their leg trapped behind you while you sit beside them. Leads to the back, the twister and the calf slicer.","tags":["Leg Entanglement","Back Take","Twister"],"objective":"Trap one of their legs from the side of a turtled or half-turned opponent, then take the back or attack.","mechanics":"From the turtle, side or a half-turned position, trap their near leg with your legs in a lockdown style, sitting to their side and slightly behind. Your upper body controls their far arm or shoulder. From here, roll them toward you to take the back, attack the twister, or slide to the calf slicer.","defense":"They turn toward you and free the trapped leg, or flatten to stop the roll.","mistake":"Holding the leg without upper-body control. They turn and face you.","drill":"Truck entries from turtle: 3 × 5. Then truck to back take, 3 × 5.","groups":["legs","transitions","back"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["twister","calf_slicer","back_control","twister_side"]}},{"id":"estima_lock","cat":"submission","name":"Estima Lock","tagline":"A foot lock applied with your foot, not your hands. It can catch people very fast.","tags":["Foot Lock","Leg Lock"],"objective":"Lock their foot with your own foot on top, then apply pressure by rotating.","mechanics":"When their foot is on your hip (common in 50/50 or open guard), hook your foot over the top of their foot. Grip your own foot or ankle to hold their foot in place. Twist your body toward their foot, rotating their ankle inward. Apply slowly; the joint can give suddenly.","defense":"They pull their foot off your hip early.","mistake":"Snapping it on. This lock works quickly — apply it slowly in training.","drill":"Slow entries from 50/50 and open guard: 3 × 3 each side.","groups":["legs"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["ankle_lock","fifty_fifty","toe_hold"]}},{"id":"calf_slicer","cat":"submission","name":"Calf Slicer","tagline":"Your shin behind their knee, then fold the leg. A compression lock that ends scrambles.","tags":["Compression Lock","Leg Lock","Truck"],"objective":"Put your shin behind their knee and fold their leg over it, crushing the calf and stretching the knee.","mechanics":"From the truck or back, slide your shin deep into the back of their knee. Trap their leg around your shin with your legs locked in a triangle or lockdown. Pull their foot toward their buttocks with your hands while pushing your hips forward. Apply slowly.","defense":"They straighten their leg before the shin is deep, or roll out of the truck.","mistake":"Applying fast. Compression locks can damage the knee quickly.","drill":"From the truck: 3 × 3 each side, slow application.","groups":["legs","back"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Calf Crush"],"rel":["truck","twister","kneebar"]}},{"id":"aoki_lock","cat":"submission","name":"Aoki Lock","tagline":"A reverse toe hold from ashi-garami that twists the foot outward.","tags":["Leg Lock","Toe Hold","Advanced"],"objective":"From ashi-garami, grip the foot with a figure-four and rotate it outward instead of in.","mechanics":"From ashi-garami, take a figure-four grip on their foot: one hand grips the outside of their foot, your other arm goes under their ankle and grips your wrist. Rotate the foot outward, the opposite way to a toe hold, while keeping their knee trapped. Apply slowly.","defense":"They turn their knee and foot with the rotation and pull out.","mistake":"Rotating with their knee free. Without the knee trapped, they turn with you.","drill":"Slow grip and rotation: 3 × 3 each side.","groups":["legs"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["toe_hold","ankle_lock","ashi_inside"]}},{"id":"wrist_lock","cat":"submission","name":"Wrist Lock","tagline":"Small joint, big pain. Catches people who leave their hand on your chest.","tags":["Joint Lock","Wrist"],"objective":"Bend their wrist past its range while it's trapped against your body or the mat.","mechanics":"When their hand is flat on your chest or the mat, trap it there. Place your hands or forearm on the back of their hand and push their fingers toward their forearm, bending the wrist. Keep their elbow bent. Apply slowly; wrist locks come on fast. Check your ruleset — many beginner divisions don't allow them.","defense":"They pull their hand away or straighten the arm.","mistake":"Applying fast. Wrists can be injured quickly.","drill":"Slow application from guard and side control: 3 × 3 each side.","groups":["closed","side","mount"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["kimura","americana","armbar"]}},{"id":"bicep_slicer","cat":"submission","name":"Bicep Slicer","tagline":"Your forearm in their elbow crease, fold the arm. A compression lock when the armbar is defended.","tags":["Compression Lock","Arm"],"objective":"Crush the bicep by folding their arm over your forearm placed in their elbow crease.","mechanics":"When they bend their arm to defend an armbar, slide your forearm into the crease of their elbow. Grip your hands together. Fold their forearm toward their shoulder over your forearm, compressing the bicep. Apply slowly. It is banned in many rulesets below brown belt.","defense":"They straighten the arm or turn into you.","mistake":"Applying hard. Compression locks injure quickly.","drill":"From a defended armbar: 3 × 3 each side, slowly.","groups":["side","mount"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Bicep Crush"],"rel":["armbar","kimura"]}},{"id":"baratoplata","cat":"submission","name":"Baratoplata","tagline":"A shoulder lock using your knee and leg. Works from guard and from top positions.","tags":["Shoulder Lock","Advanced"],"objective":"Trap their bent arm and rotate the shoulder using your leg as the lever.","mechanics":"When their arm is bent and trapped (often in a kimura attempt), put your leg over their wrist and your knee behind their elbow. Pull their elbow toward you and push their wrist away with your leg, rotating the shoulder. Apply slowly.","defense":"They straighten their arm or roll with the pressure.","mistake":"Losing the knee position behind the elbow.","drill":"Slow entries from closed guard: 3 × 3 each side.","groups":["closed","side"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["omoplata","kimura","tarikoplata"]}},{"id":"tarikoplata","cat":"submission","name":"Tarikoplata","tagline":"When they defend the kimura by gripping their belt or arm, trap the arm behind their back and rotate.","tags":["Shoulder Lock","Kimura","Advanced"],"objective":"Turn a defended kimura into a shoulder lock by trapping their arm behind their back.","mechanics":"From a kimura grip that they defend, push their arm behind their back. Trap it with your legs or your body. Rotate your body to drive their elbow up their back, rotating the shoulder. Apply slowly.","defense":"They keep the kimura defensive grip or roll toward the attack.","mistake":"Pulling with your arms. The rotation comes from your body.","drill":"From a kimura attempt: 3 × 3 each side.","groups":["closed","mount"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["kimura","baratoplata","omoplata"]}},{"id":"banana_split","cat":"submission","name":"Banana Split","tagline":"A hip stretch from the truck. It is more often used to force a back take than to finish.","tags":["Hip Lock","Truck","Advanced"],"objective":"Spread their legs apart from the truck until they roll or tap.","mechanics":"From the truck, keep their near leg trapped in your legs. Hook your arm under their far leg. Pull the far leg toward you while extending your legs, spreading their legs apart. Apply very slowly. It is illegal in many rulesets.","defense":"They roll toward the trapped leg or turn to face you.","mistake":"Applying fast. Hip injuries are serious.","drill":"Positional only in most training: 3 × 3 entries.","groups":["back","legs"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","aka":["Crotch Ripper"],"rel":["truck","electric_chair","twister"]}},{"id":"twister","cat":"submission","name":"Twister","tagline":"A spinal twist from the truck. Illegal in most BJJ rulesets — know it, train it with care.","tags":["Spinal Lock","Truck","Advanced"],"objective":"From the truck, lock their head and twist their spine away from the trapped leg.","mechanics":"From the truck, wrap your arm around their head from the front and pull it toward you. Their leg is trapped in your legs. Twist their head and shoulders while your legs hold the hips. It is a spinal lock — illegal in IBJJF and many other rulesets. Use it in training only with care.","defense":"They turn into you and free their leg or stay flat.","mistake":"Applying it with force. Neck and spine injuries are serious.","drill":"Use the truck position for back takes; train the twister only slowly and with permission.","groups":["back","legs"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["truck","twister_side","back_control"]}},{"id":"buggy_choke","cat":"submission","name":"Buggy Choke","tagline":"A choke from bottom side control. It surprises people who think they're safe on top.","tags":["Choke","Bottom Side Control"],"objective":"From bottom side control, trap their head and arm with your arms and legs to choke.","mechanics":"From bottom side control, wrap your arm around their head, gripping your own hands with their arm trapped inside. Bring your far leg over and cross your legs. Pull your arms and squeeze your legs together. The choke is like an arm triangle from the bottom.","defense":"They keep their arm out of your grip or move to north-south.","mistake":"Trying it without trapping their arm. The arm is what makes the choke.","drill":"From bottom side control: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["side","defence"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["side_control_escape","arm_triangle","triangle"]}},{"id":"ude_gatame","cat":"submission","name":"Ude-Gatame","tagline":"A straight armlock where you press their straight arm with your hands. Common in judo and BJJ.","tags":["Armlock","Judo","Straight Arm"],"objective":"Straighten their arm and press against the elbow with your hands or forearm.","mechanics":"When their arm is straight (often from guard or side), trap their wrist on your shoulder or against your neck. Put your hands on their elbow from above. Pull the elbow toward you while the wrist stays pinned. Apply slowly.","defense":"They bend the arm or turn their elbow down.","mistake":"Pressing on the forearm. The pressure must be on the elbow.","drill":"From guard: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["side","judo_ground"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Straight Armlock","Ude-Hishigi-Ude-Gatame"],"rel":["armbar","kimura","americana"]}},{"id":"armbar_escape","cat":"defence","name":"Armbar Escape","tagline":"Clasp your hands, stack them or turn your thumb toward the floor. Act before the arm is straight.","tags":["Escape","Armbar"],"objective":"Stop the arm from straightening, then free it by stacking or turning.","mechanics":"Clasp your hands together and keep your elbow bent. From guard, stand up and stack their weight onto their shoulders, driving your knees toward their head, then pull the arm out. From mount or side, turn your thumb toward the mat (hitchhiker) and rotate into them, pulling the elbow out as you turn.","defense":"They break your grip by kicking your arms apart or switch to a triangle.","mistake":"Pulling a straight arm. Bend the elbow first.","drill":"Partner sets up the armbar at 30%; escape both ways. 3 × 5.","groups":["defence","closed","mount"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Hitchhiker Escape","Stack Escape"],"rel":["armbar","triangle_escape"]}},{"id":"triangle_escape","cat":"defence","name":"Triangle Escape","tagline":"Posture up, get the trapped arm back inside or past their hip, and stack.","tags":["Escape","Triangle"],"objective":"Stop the choke by posture and arm position, then open their legs.","mechanics":"As soon as their leg comes over your neck, posture up straight. Keep the trapped arm inside or across to their hips — don't leave it hanging out. Drive your knees forward and stack them onto their shoulders. Grab the leg that's over your neck and push it off or step your leg over to pass.","defense":"They pull your head down, adjust the angle or switch to an armbar.","mistake":"Pulling your head back while your posture is broken. Posture first.","drill":"Partner locks the triangle at 30%; escape. 3 × 5.","groups":["defence","closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["triangle","armbar_escape","guard_closed"]}},{"id":"guillotine_escape","cat":"defence","name":"Guillotine Escape","tagline":"Relieve the pressure first, then pass to the side of their choking arm.","tags":["Escape","Guillotine"],"objective":"Stop the choke by relieving pressure on your neck, then pass to safety.","mechanics":"Pull down on their choking wrist with your hands to relieve the choke. From guard, put your shoulder into their neck and walk around to the side opposite their choking arm. Pass their legs and settle; their arm becomes trapped. If they have closed guard, stand up or turn toward the choking arm side.","defense":"They switch to a high-elbow or arm-in guillotine as you move.","mistake":"Pulling your head straight back. That only tightens the choke.","drill":"Partner holds a guillotine at 30%; escape. 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["defence","headlock"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["guillotine","von_flue_choke","high_elbow_guillotine"]}},{"id":"kimura_defence","cat":"defence","name":"Kimura Defence","tagline":"Grab your own belt, trouser or thigh to keep the arm bent and close.","tags":["Escape","Kimura"],"objective":"Stop the shoulder rotation by gripping your own body, then free the arm.","mechanics":"As soon as they take the figure-four grip, grab your own belt, trousers or thigh with the attacked hand. Keep the elbow tight to your body. Turn into them, toward the attacked shoulder. When they can't rotate, pull the arm free or reverse the position.","defense":"They switch to a tarikoplata, armbar or back take.","mistake":"Letting the elbow leave your body. Keep it tight.","drill":"Partner attacks the kimura at 50%; defend. 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["defence"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["kimura","kimura_trap","tarikoplata"]}},{"id":"ghost_escape","cat":"defence","name":"Ghost Escape","tagline":"Slide under them and turn out the back of side control. Fast when it works.","tags":["Escape","Side Control","Advanced"],"objective":"Escape side control by turning away and sliding your hips under them to come out to your knees.","mechanics":"From bottom side control, turn onto your side facing away. Bring your far leg over and roll onto your shoulder, sliding your hips under them. Turn out to your knees behind or beside them. Keep your head tucked.","defense":"They follow you and take your back.","mistake":"Turning away slowly. If they follow, you give up your back.","drill":"From side control at 50%: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["defence","side"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["side_control_escape","granby_roll"]}},{"id":"framing","cat":"concept","name":"Framing","tagline":"Use bones, not muscle. Frames create space; hip movement fills it.","tags":["Defence","Structure","Escapes"],"objective":"Make solid shapes with your arms and legs that hold their weight, so you can move your hips into the space.","mechanics":"A frame is a straight or angled bone structure — forearm across their neck, hand on their hip, knee against their body. Frames hold their weight; they don't push. Once the frame holds, move your hips away (shrimp) to create space, then put a knee or leg into the space. The rule is frame, then move.","defense":"Top players crush frames by moving around them or by changing the angle of their weight.","mistake":"Pushing with straight arms. Pushing tires you out and gives them an armbar.","drill":"Frame-and-shrimp from side control: 3 × 1 minute, top applies pressure.","groups":["defence","concepts"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Frames"],"rel":["side_control_escape","mount_escape","hip_movement","guard_recovery"]}},{"id":"fighting_stance","cat":"concept","name":"MMA Fighting Stance","tagline":"A stance that can strike, defend kicks and stop takedowns. Higher than wrestling, lower than boxing.","tags":["MMA","Striking","Foundation"],"objective":"Stand so you can punch and kick, defend strikes, and sprawl on a takedown — all from the same position.","mechanics":"Feet a little wider than shoulder width, lead foot forward, toes of the back foot behind the lead heel. Knees bent, weight balanced between both feet. Hands up: lead hand at eye level in front, rear hand by your chin. Elbows in to protect the body. Chin down, eyes up. Keep your hips under you, ready to drop into a sprawl. A slightly wider, lower stance than boxing helps against takedowns and leg kicks.","defense":"Opponents test your stance with feints, leg kicks and level changes. If you react to every feint, they will time your reaction.","mistake":"Hands dropping when you get tired. The guard comes down, and that's when strikes land.","drill":"Shadowboxing in stance: 3 × 2 minutes. Add a sprawl on a clap and return to stance with hands up.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Stance & Guard"],"rel":["jab","footwork_striking","stance_motion","sprawl"]}},{"id":"footwork_striking","cat":"concept","name":"Footwork & Distance","tagline":"Control the distance and you control the fight. Footwork decides where strikes and takedowns happen.","tags":["MMA","Striking","Footwork"],"objective":"Move in and out of range on your terms, and take angles so you can hit them while they can't hit you.","mechanics":"Move the foot closest to where you're going first: step forward with the lead foot, back with the back foot. Never cross your feet. Keep your stance width as you move. Pivot on your lead foot to take an angle after a combination. Use small, balanced steps — big steps leave you unbalanced. Against the cage, circle away from their power hand rather than straight back.","defense":"Opponents cut off the cage and use feints to make you step into their range.","mistake":"Retreating in a straight line. You run out of space and end up against the cage.","drill":"Footwork ladder: forward, back, left, right, pivot. 3 × 2 minutes in stance.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"MMA","rel":["fighting_stance","distance_management","jab"]}},{"id":"head_movement","cat":"defence","name":"Slips, Rolls & Head Movement","tagline":"Move your head off the line of the punch. Less damage, and it sets up your counters.","tags":["MMA","Striking","Defence"],"objective":"Avoid straight punches by slipping and hooks by rolling under them, staying in position to counter.","mechanics":"Slip: rotate your shoulders and shift your weight slightly so your head moves just outside the line of a straight punch, bending at the knees, not the waist. Roll: bend your knees and move your head under a hook in a U shape, coming up on the other side. Keep your eyes on them and your hands up. Small movements are better than large ones.","defense":"Opponents double up on the same side or throw knees and uppercuts at a lowered head.","mistake":"Ducking low with your head forward. In MMA that walks into knees and front headlocks.","drill":"Partner throws slow jabs and hooks; slip and roll. 3 × 2 minutes.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Slip","Bob and Weave"],"rel":["blocking_covering","jab","cross","counterstriking"]}},{"id":"blocking_covering","cat":"defence","name":"Blocking & Parrying","tagline":"Catch, parry or absorb strikes on your arms and shoulders instead of your head.","tags":["MMA","Striking","Defence"],"objective":"Stop punches reaching your head and body using your hands, forearms and shoulders.","mechanics":"Parry a jab with your rear hand by tapping it to the side, then return the hand to your chin. Block a hook by raising your arm so your glove covers your ear and your forearm is against your head. Block body shots with your elbows. Cover up: both forearms in front of your face, elbows tight, chin down — only for short moments.","defense":"Opponents strike around or between your arms, or hit the body when you cover high.","mistake":"Covering up for too long. Blocking is a short-term fix; move or counter.","drill":"Partner throws light combinations; block and parry. 3 × 2 minutes.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Cover","Parry"],"rel":["head_movement","checking_kicks","fighting_stance"]}},{"id":"checking_kicks","cat":"defence","name":"Checking Leg Kicks","tagline":"Lift your shin to meet the kick. Their shin hits yours, not your thigh.","tags":["MMA","Striking","Defence","Kicks"],"objective":"Stop low kicks from damaging your leg by blocking them with your raised shin.","mechanics":"When you see a low kick, lift your lead knee up and slightly out so your shin faces the kick. Keep your hands up. The kick lands on your shin rather than your thigh or calf. Plant the foot back down quickly into stance. Against calf kicks, also turn your lead foot slightly out and check earlier.","defense":"Opponents feint the kick, then punch while you're on one leg.","mistake":"Checking late, or lifting the leg straight up. The shin must face the kick.","drill":"Partner throws light kicks; check them. 3 × 1 minute each side.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["leg_kick","calf_kick","fighting_stance"]}},{"id":"counterstriking","cat":"concept","name":"Counterstriking","tagline":"Make them miss, then hit them. The most efficient strikes land when they've just thrown.","tags":["MMA","Striking","Timing"],"objective":"Avoid or block their strike and hit back in the moment they're exposed.","mechanics":"Classic counters: slip the jab and throw a cross over it; roll under the hook and throw your own hook; check a kick and step in with a punch. The counter comes right after the defence, while they're still recovering. Learn their patterns — most fighters repeat the same combinations.","defense":"Opponents feint to draw your counter, then hit your counter.","mistake":"Waiting to counter without throwing. Passive fighters lose rounds.","drill":"Partner throws one known strike; counter each time. 3 × 2 minutes.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"MMA","rel":["head_movement","cross","hook_punch"]}},{"id":"jab","cat":"strike","name":"Jab","tagline":"The fastest punch and the most important. It measures distance, sets up everything else.","tags":["MMA","Punch","Lead Hand"],"objective":"Hit them with your lead hand quickly to control distance, score and set up combinations or takedowns.","mechanics":"From stance, extend your lead hand straight out, turning your fist palm-down at the end. Your lead shoulder rises to protect your chin. Step forward with the lead foot as you throw for more reach. Return the hand straight back to your face the same way it went out. Keep your rear hand by your chin.","defense":"They parry, slip outside it, or time a counter cross over the top.","mistake":"Dropping the hand after the jab. Return it straight to your face.","drill":"Jab on pads or bag: 3 × 2 minutes, single and double jabs.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"MMA","rel":["cross","fighting_stance","footwork_striking"]}},{"id":"cross","cat":"strike","name":"Cross","tagline":"The rear-hand straight punch. Power from the hips and the back foot.","tags":["MMA","Punch","Power"],"objective":"Throw your strongest straight punch, usually after a jab.","mechanics":"Push off the ball of your rear foot, turning your rear hip and shoulder forward. Your rear hand goes straight out to the target, palm down. Your lead hand stays by your chin. Your weight shifts slightly forward but stays balanced. Return the hand straight back to your chin.","defense":"They slip outside and counter, or level-change under it for a takedown.","mistake":"Throwing with your arm only. The power comes from the hip turn.","drill":"Jab-cross on pads: 3 × 2 minutes.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Straight Right","Rear Straight"],"rel":["jab","hook_punch","overhand"]}},{"id":"hook_punch","cat":"strike","name":"Hook","tagline":"A short, curving punch to the side of the head or body.","tags":["MMA","Punch","Power"],"objective":"Hit around their guard to the side of the head or the body.","mechanics":"Lift your elbow so your arm is bent at about 90 degrees, level with your fist. Turn your hips and shoulders, pivoting on your lead foot. Your fist travels in a short arc to the side of their head. To the body, bend your knees and drop your level so the punch lands under the elbow. Keep the other hand by your chin.","defense":"They roll under it, block with their arm, or counter with a straight punch inside it.","mistake":"Swinging wide. The hook is short and tight.","drill":"Jab-cross-hook on pads: 3 × 2 minutes.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Lead Hook","Body Hook"],"rel":["cross","uppercut","head_movement"]}},{"id":"uppercut","cat":"strike","name":"Uppercut","tagline":"A rising punch through their guard. Punishes opponents who duck their heads.","tags":["MMA","Punch","Close Range"],"objective":"Hit up under their chin when they're close or ducking low.","mechanics":"Drop your level slightly by bending your knees. Drive up from the legs and turn your hip, bringing your fist up in a short vertical arc, palm toward you. The punch goes up through the middle of their guard. Keep it short and return to guard.","defense":"They lean back, cover, or tie you up in the clinch.","mistake":"Winding up by dropping your hand. It telegraphs the punch.","drill":"Hook-uppercut combinations on pads: 3 × 2 minutes.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"MMA","rel":["hook_punch","cross","head_movement"]}},{"id":"overhand","cat":"strike","name":"Overhand","tagline":"A looping power punch over their guard. Often combined with a level change for a takedown.","tags":["MMA","Punch","Power"],"objective":"Land a powerful punch over the top of their lead hand while moving your head off the centre line.","mechanics":"Drop your head off the centre line slightly as you throw. Your rear hand loops over and down, landing on the side of their head over their lead hand. Your body weight drops into the punch. In MMA, the same movement leads into a level change and double leg, so they can't tell which is coming.","defense":"They counter with a straight punch or uppercut, or step back.","mistake":"Throwing it from too far. It's a mid-range punch.","drill":"Overhand to level change on pads and a partner: 3 × 8.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["cross","double_leg","head_movement"]}},{"id":"superman_punch","cat":"strike","name":"Superman Punch","tagline":"Fake a kick, then jump forward into a straight punch. A surprise strike.","tags":["MMA","Punch","Feint"],"objective":"Close distance quickly by faking a rear kick and jumping into a cross.","mechanics":"Lift your rear leg as if to kick. As you swing it back down, push off the lead foot and throw your rear hand forward in a straight punch. Your body launches forward. Land in stance.","defense":"They step back out of range or counter as you land.","mistake":"Using it often. Once they expect it, they counter.","drill":"Bag: 3 × 5 each side, slowly first. Land balanced in stance every rep before throwing the next.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"MMA","rel":["cross","teep"]}},{"id":"teep","cat":"strike","name":"Teep","tagline":"A straight kick with the ball of the foot. It pushes them away and disrupts their attack.","tags":["MMA","Kick","Distance"],"objective":"Stop them coming forward, break their rhythm or push them toward the cage.","mechanics":"Lift the knee of your lead or rear leg high in front of you. Extend the leg straight out, landing with the ball of your foot or the sole on their stomach or hip. Push through with your hips. Bring the leg back quickly and land in stance.","defense":"They catch the leg, step off line or counter with a punch.","mistake":"Kicking without lifting the knee first. It loses power and is easier to catch.","drill":"Teep on a bag or pads: 3 × 10 each leg.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Push Kick","Front Kick"],"rel":["fighting_stance","leg_kick","footwork_striking"]}},{"id":"leg_kick","cat":"strike","name":"Low Kick","tagline":"A roundhouse kick to the thigh. Low risk, high damage over a fight.","tags":["MMA","Kick","Muay Thai"],"objective":"Damage their lead or rear leg to slow them down and reduce their power.","mechanics":"Step out at an angle with your lead foot, pivoting on the ball of the foot. Turn your hips over and swing your rear leg in an arc, landing your shin (not your foot) on the side of their thigh. Keep your hand up on the same side. Return the leg to stance or let it follow through.","defense":"They check it with their shin, or step back and counter.","mistake":"Kicking with the foot instead of the shin. It's weaker and hurts your foot.","drill":"Bag or pads: 3 × 10 each leg.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Leg Kick","Low Roundhouse"],"rel":["calf_kick","checking_kicks","body_kick"]}},{"id":"calf_kick","cat":"strike","name":"Calf Kick","tagline":"A low kick to the calf of the lead leg. Hard to check and damages mobility fast.","tags":["MMA","Kick","Low Kick"],"objective":"Kick the outside of their lead calf to take away their movement.","mechanics":"Throw a low roundhouse, but aim lower — your shin lands on the back or side of their calf. The kick is often thrown on a slightly downward angle. It's effective against opponents who stand heavy on their lead leg.","defense":"They turn their lead foot out and check early, or shift weight off the lead leg.","mistake":"Kicking from too far. You need to be close enough to reach the calf with your shin.","drill":"Bag: 3 × 10 each leg, then pads with a partner who checks every third kick so you reset your stance.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["leg_kick","checking_kicks"]}},{"id":"body_kick","cat":"strike","name":"Body Kick","tagline":"A roundhouse kick to the ribs. Hard to catch when it's fast and returned.","tags":["MMA","Kick","Muay Thai"],"objective":"Land a powerful kick to the body to sap their energy and break their guard.","mechanics":"Step out with your lead foot at an angle and pivot. Turn your hips over and kick with your shin into their ribs, under the elbow. Throw your arm on the kicking side down for balance and power. Return the leg to stance.","defense":"They block with their elbow and raised knee, or catch the kick.","mistake":"Kicking slowly with no set-up. Body kicks get caught and turned into takedowns.","drill":"Pads: 3 × 10 each side, then combine with a punch combination before or after.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Middle Kick","Roundhouse to the Body"],"rel":["leg_kick","head_kick","teep"]}},{"id":"head_kick","cat":"strike","name":"Head Kick","tagline":"A roundhouse kick to the head. It can end a fight, but it needs flexibility and set-ups.","tags":["MMA","Kick","Power"],"objective":"Kick over their guard to the side of the head.","mechanics":"Like the body kick but higher. Pivot fully on the lead foot, lean back slightly for balance and lift the kick up to head height, landing with the shin. It's usually set up by kicking the body or legs first so they lower their guard.","defense":"They block with a raised arm and shoulder, lean back, or step in to smother the kick.","mistake":"Throwing it cold with no set-up. It's easy to see coming.","drill":"Pads at head height: 3 × 6 each side, focus on balance.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","aka":["High Kick"],"rel":["body_kick","leg_kick"]}},{"id":"spinning_back_kick","cat":"strike","name":"Spinning Back Kick","tagline":"Turn your back and drive your heel into their stomach. Powerful, but risky if it misses.","tags":["MMA","Kick","Spinning"],"objective":"Land a heel strike to the body by spinning and kicking straight back.","mechanics":"Step across with your lead foot and turn your back to them, looking over your shoulder at the target. Lift your rear knee and drive your heel straight back into their stomach. Turn back to face them quickly as you land.","defense":"They step back out of range, or take your back as you turn.","mistake":"Spinning without looking. Always see the target before you kick.","drill":"Bag: 3 × 5 each side, slowly first. Land balanced in stance every rep before throwing the next.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"MMA","rel":["teep","body_kick"]}},{"id":"upkick","cat":"strike","name":"Upkick","tagline":"A kick from your back at a standing opponent. Keeps them from diving into your guard.","tags":["MMA","Kick","Guard"],"objective":"Stop a standing opponent attacking you on the ground by kicking up at their head or body.","mechanics":"On your back or side with your feet toward them, keep one leg cocked. When they lean in, extend the leg up into their head, chest or hips. Return the foot quickly and keep your legs between you and them. Use it to create space and stand up.","defense":"They step around your legs or pass to the side.","mistake":"Kicking with no plan to stand. Use the space to get up.","drill":"Partner circles while you upkick their pads; stand up when they step back. 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["striking","mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["mma_guard","wall_walk","technical_standup"]}},{"id":"straight_knee","cat":"strike","name":"Knee Strike","tagline":"Drive your knee into their body or head from close range. A key clinch weapon.","tags":["MMA","Knee","Clinch"],"objective":"Hit them with your knee in the clinch, against the cage or as they shoot for a takedown.","mechanics":"From close range, drive your hips forward and lift your knee into their body or head, pointing your toes down. Pull their head or body into the knee with your hands. Return the leg to stance. Knees to the head of a downed opponent are illegal under the Unified Rules.","defense":"They block with their forearms, push your hips away or take you down off a single leg.","mistake":"Kneeing with your hips back. The hips drive the knee.","drill":"Knee strikes on a bag: 3 × 10 each side.","groups":["striking","mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Straight Knee"],"rel":["thai_clinch","flying_knee","cage_clinch"]}},{"id":"flying_knee","cat":"strike","name":"Flying Knee","tagline":"Jump into a knee to their head. It catches opponents who duck or shoot.","tags":["MMA","Knee","Spectacular"],"objective":"Close the distance with a jumping knee, often timed against a level change.","mechanics":"Step forward and jump off the lead foot, driving the opposite knee up toward their head. Throw your hands forward to protect your face and pull their head if you reach it. Land in stance. Time it for when they duck or shoot.","defense":"They step back, block with their arms or take you down as you land.","mistake":"Throwing it from too far away. It's a short-distance strike.","drill":"Bag or pads: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"MMA","rel":["straight_knee","double_leg"]}},{"id":"horizontal_elbow","cat":"strike","name":"Horizontal Elbow","tagline":"A short slicing elbow at close range. It cuts and hurts.","tags":["MMA","Elbow","Close Range"],"objective":"Strike with the point or edge of your elbow when you're too close to punch.","mechanics":"From close range, raise your elbow so your forearm is level. Turn your hip and shoulder like a hook, swinging the elbow horizontally across. Your hand moves toward your opposite shoulder. Keep the other hand up.","defense":"They block with their forearm or tie up your arm.","mistake":"Throwing it from punching range. Elbows are for very close range.","drill":"Pads: 3 × 10 each side, then combine with a punch combination before or after.","groups":["striking","mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["thai_clinch","dirty_boxing","hook_punch"]}},{"id":"downward_elbow","cat":"strike","name":"Downward Elbow","tagline":"Elbows dropped from top position. One of the most damaging ground strikes.","tags":["MMA","Elbow","Ground and Pound"],"objective":"Strike down from top position with your elbow when you have posture and space.","mechanics":"From top position (half guard, side, mount), create a small space by lifting your posture. Drop your elbow down into their head or body, using your body weight. Return to a controlling position immediately. Under the Unified Rules, straight down 12-to-6 elbows are illegal; angled elbows are allowed.","defense":"They hold you tight to stop the space, or frame and move.","mistake":"Giving up position to throw elbows. Position first, strikes second.","drill":"Ground pads from half guard and side: 3 × 10.","groups":["striking","mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Ground Elbow"],"rel":["ground_and_pound","mma_top_control"]}},{"id":"spinning_back_elbow","cat":"strike","name":"Spinning Back Elbow","tagline":"Turn and swing your elbow back into their head. Fast and powerful when it surprises them.","tags":["MMA","Elbow","Spinning"],"objective":"Land an elbow by spinning, usually as they step in or circle.","mechanics":"Step across with your lead foot and turn your back, looking over your shoulder. Swing your rear elbow back around at head height. Finish the turn and return to stance.","defense":"They step back out of range or take your back.","mistake":"Turning without seeing your target.","drill":"Pads: 3 × 5 each side. Look over your shoulder at the pad before every strike.","groups":["striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"MMA","rel":["horizontal_elbow","spinning_back_kick"]}},{"id":"thai_clinch","cat":"position","name":"Thai Clinch","tagline":"Both hands behind their head, forearms on their collarbones. You control their head and knee them.","tags":["MMA","Clinch","Muay Thai"],"objective":"Control their head with both hands so you can knee and off-balance them.","mechanics":"Clasp your hands behind their head (one on top of the other, not interlaced fingers). Squeeze your elbows together and push your forearms into their collarbones. Pull their head down. Knee them, turn them to break their balance or throw them. Keep your hips close.","defense":"They push your hips away, swim their arms inside, or take you down.","mistake":"Interlacing your fingers — a pull on them can injure your fingers.","drill":"Clinch fighting: 3 × 1 minute, win the clinch and land knees.","groups":["striking","mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Plum","Double Collar Tie"],"rel":["straight_knee","collar_tie","horizontal_elbow"]}},{"id":"dirty_boxing","cat":"strike","name":"Dirty Boxing","tagline":"Hold them with one hand and punch with the other. Short shots from the clinch.","tags":["MMA","Clinch","Punches"],"objective":"Control them with a collar tie or wrist grip while landing short punches and elbows.","mechanics":"Take a single collar tie or control one wrist. With your free hand, throw short uppercuts, hooks and elbows. Pull them into your strikes. Use your head position to stop them squaring up. Against the cage, combine it with underhooks and knees.","defense":"They break the grip, tie up your striking arm or take you down.","mistake":"Holding on and not striking. The clinch must be active.","drill":"Partner wears gloves; hold a collar tie and throw short shots. 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["striking","mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["thai_clinch","cage_clinch","uppercut","horizontal_elbow"]}},{"id":"cage_clinch","cat":"position","name":"Cage Clinch","tagline":"Pin them against the fence with underhooks. The cage changes wrestling.","tags":["MMA","Clinch","Cage"],"objective":"Hold them against the cage so they can't move freely, then strike, take them down or score.","mechanics":"Get an underhook and drive them back into the cage. Put your head on their chest or jaw. Your hips push into theirs, pinning them. From here, take their legs out (double leg, single leg), strike with knees to the legs, or dirty box.","defense":"They whizzer, pummel for their own underhook, or circle off the fence.","mistake":"Leaning on them with no plan. Referees break inactive clinches.","drill":"Cage clinch: 3 × 1 minute, pin and score or escape.","groups":["mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Fence Clinch","Wall Wrestling"],"rel":["underhooks_pummel","cage_double_leg","fence_defence","wall_walk"]}},{"id":"cage_double_leg","cat":"takedown","name":"Double Leg Against the Cage","tagline":"The fence stops them sprawling back. Change direction to finish.","tags":["MMA","Takedown","Cage"],"objective":"Take them down when they're against the cage, using it to stop their sprawl.","mechanics":"From the cage clinch, drop your level and wrap both their legs. Your head is on their chest or ribs. Pull the legs together and drive your shoulder into them, turning them sideways off the cage so they fall. Or lift them and drop them to the side. Follow them down into top position.","defense":"They whizzer, keep their legs apart, or stand up using the cage.","mistake":"Driving straight into the cage. Turn them sideways off it.","drill":"From the cage clinch: 3 × 8. Partner whizzers at 50% on the last set.","groups":["mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["double_leg","cage_clinch","fence_defence"]}},{"id":"fence_defence","cat":"defence","name":"Takedown Defence on the Fence","tagline":"Underhooks, a wide base and your back off the fence.","tags":["MMA","Cage","Takedown Defence"],"objective":"Stop takedowns while against the cage and get back to the centre.","mechanics":"Fight for underhooks and keep your hips square. Widen your stance and lower your level so they can't wrap your legs. Use the cage behind you to stay upright — lean your back into it. When you have an underhook, turn them into the cage, or circle away along the fence back to the centre.","defense":"They switch from double to single or attack the legs with trips.","mistake":"Standing with your feet together. They pick you up easily.","drill":"Cage defence: 3 × 1 minute, partner attacks the legs.","groups":["mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["cage_clinch","whizzer","cage_double_leg","sprawl"]}},{"id":"wall_walk","cat":"defence","name":"Wall Walk","tagline":"Use the cage to climb back to your feet when you're taken down.","tags":["MMA","Cage","Get Up"],"objective":"Get back up from your back or bottom by walking your shoulders up the cage.","mechanics":"With your back near the cage, get your shoulders against it. Plant your feet and walk your shoulders up the cage while you push off the floor. Keep an underhook or wrist control to stop them holding you down. Once your hips are up, stand and fight for position.","defense":"They hold your legs or hips down, or take your back as you rise.","mistake":"Standing with your back exposed. Keep control of their arms.","drill":"Taken down near the cage; wall walk to stand. 3 × 5.","groups":["mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Getting Up on the Cage"],"rel":["technical_standup","cage_clinch","butterfly_wall"]}},{"id":"butterfly_wall","cat":"transition","name":"Butterfly to Wall Stand-Up","tagline":"Use butterfly hooks to create space, then stand up using the cage.","tags":["MMA","Butterfly","Get Up"],"objective":"From butterfly guard near the cage, lift them off you and stand.","mechanics":"From butterfly guard, lift with your hooks and hold an underhook. Move your back onto the cage. Lift them with the hooks to make space, plant your feet and walk up the cage. Once standing, hold the underhook to stay off the fence.","defense":"They flatten you or pass to the side.","mistake":"Waiting in butterfly guard. Use it to get up quickly.","drill":"Butterfly to stand-up near a wall: 3 × 5.","groups":["mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["butterfly","wall_walk","technical_standup"]}},{"id":"mma_guard","cat":"position","name":"Guard in MMA","tagline":"Hold them close so they can't strike, then attack or stand up.","tags":["MMA","Guard","Defence"],"objective":"From your back, stop strikes by controlling their posture and arms, then attack or get up.","mechanics":"Pull them close with your legs and control their wrists or tie up their head. Don't let them posture up and create space to punch. Use the hip bump, kimura or triangle when they posture. If they stand, upkick and stand up. In MMA, staying on your back too long loses rounds.","defense":"They posture up, stand up, or pin your hips and strike.","mistake":"Lying flat with an open guard while they strike you.","drill":"Closed guard against light strikes: 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","aka":["Closed Guard Against Strikes"],"rel":["guard_closed","upkick","wall_walk"]}},{"id":"mma_top_control","cat":"position","name":"Top Control in MMA","tagline":"Pin their hips, keep your base, and strike without giving up position.","tags":["MMA","Top Position","Ground and Pound"],"objective":"Hold top position while landing strikes, without letting them stand up or sweep you.","mechanics":"Keep your weight on their hips and chest. Your base is wide, knees pinning them. Control one wrist with one hand, strike with the other. Pass to half guard, side control or mount when they defend. Don't lose position to throw big shots.","defense":"They hold you tight, frame and wall walk, or sweep you.","mistake":"Standing up to throw big punches and letting them back up.","drill":"Top control rounds: 3 × 1 minute with light ground strikes on pads.","groups":["mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["ground_and_pound","half_guard_top","side_control","mount"]}},{"id":"ground_and_pound","cat":"strike","name":"Ground and Pound","tagline":"Strikes from the top position. Position first, then strike.","tags":["MMA","Ground Strikes"],"objective":"Land punches, hammerfists and elbows from top position while keeping control.","mechanics":"From top position, control their wrists or posture so you can strike. Throw short punches, hammerfists and angled elbows from half guard, side control and mount. Keep your hips low and base wide. When they cover up, pass or take a better position.","defense":"They hold your wrists, tie you up or frame and get up.","mistake":"Over-committing to strikes and getting swept.","drill":"Ground pads from guard, half and mount: 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["mma","striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","aka":["GnP"],"rel":["mma_top_control","downward_elbow","hammerfist"]}},{"id":"hammerfist","cat":"strike","name":"Hammerfist","tagline":"Strike with the bottom of your fist. Safe for your hand and strong from the top.","tags":["MMA","Ground Strikes"],"objective":"Hit with the meaty side of your fist from top position or in a scramble.","mechanics":"Make a fist and strike down with the side of it, like hammering a nail. From the top, raise your arm and bring it down with your body weight behind it. Return to control.","defense":"They cover or hold your arm.","mistake":"Lifting your whole body off them to throw it.","drill":"Ground pads: 3 × 10 each side.","groups":["mma","striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"MMA","rel":["ground_and_pound","downward_elbow"]}},{"id":"mma_back","cat":"position","name":"Back Control in MMA","tagline":"Strikes from the back force their hands up — then the choke opens.","tags":["MMA","Back Control","Strikes"],"objective":"Hold the back and strike so they defend their face, opening the neck for the choke.","mechanics":"Hold the back with a body triangle or hooks. Strike the side of their head with your free hand. When they raise their hands to block strikes, slide your arm under their chin for the rear naked choke. Keep your hips tight to theirs.","defense":"They turn into you, stand up with you on their back or slam you against the cage.","mistake":"Losing your hooks while striking.","drill":"From the back: strike, choke, repeat. 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["mma","back"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["back_control","body_triangle","rnc"]}},{"id":"mma_scramble","cat":"concept","name":"Scrambles & Getting Up","tagline":"In MMA, getting back up is worth more than a sweep. Every scramble ends standing or on top.","tags":["MMA","Scrambles","Strategy"],"objective":"When positions break down, come up to your feet or into top position before they settle.","mechanics":"Never stay on your back if you can stand. Use the technical stand-up, wall walk or butterfly stand-up. When turtled, come up to your knees, then feet, keeping their hands controlled. In a scramble, keep moving until you are up or on top.","defense":"Wrestlers ride you and chain takedowns so you can't get up.","mistake":"Staying on your back hoping to submit. Judges reward getting up.","drill":"Scramble rounds: start in a bad position, get up within 15 seconds. 5 rounds.","groups":["mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["technical_standup","wall_walk","sprawl"]}},{"id":"mma_gameplan","cat":"concept","name":"MMA Grappling Priorities","tagline":"Position, safety, damage, then submission. And always: get up from the bottom.","tags":["MMA","Strategy"],"objective":"Know what matters most in MMA grappling so you make the right decisions.","mechanics":"Priorities: 1) Don't get hit on the bottom — get up or control their arms. 2) On top, keep position and land strikes. 3) Submit when it's there, without losing position. 4) Against the cage, win the underhook. Guard pulling and staying on your back are much weaker in MMA than in BJJ.","defense":"Opponents use strikes to break your grips and your position.","mistake":"Fighting like a sport BJJ player — sitting to guard and waiting.","drill":"MMA grappling rounds with light strikes: 3 × 3 minutes.","groups":["mma","concepts"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"MMA","rel":["mma_scramble","mma_top_control","cage_clinch"]}},{"id":"arm_drag_back","cat":"transition","name":"Arm Drag to Back","tagline":"Drag their arm across and climb onto their back. Works from seated guard, closed guard and standing.","tags":["Back Take","Arm Drag","Guard"],"objective":"Pull their arm across your body so their back is exposed, then take it.","mechanics":"Grip their wrist with your same-side hand. With your other hand, grab behind their triceps. Pull the arm across your body while you move your hips out and toward their side. Their back is exposed. Reach your free arm over their back to the far hip or armpit, and climb behind them. Insert hooks or a seatbelt.","defense":"They pull the arm back, turn to face you, or sprawl and drive their weight onto you.","mistake":"Dragging the arm without moving your hips. Your body has to go to their side.","drill":"Seated guard arm drag to back: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["transitions","open","closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["arm_drag_standing","back_control","seatbelt","russian_tie"]}},{"id":"technical_standup","cat":"defence","name":"Technical Stand-Up","tagline":"Stand up from the ground safely, with your hands and feet protecting you.","tags":["Get Up","Open Guard","Self-Defence","MMA"],"objective":"Get to your feet from sitting or lying, keeping a frame between you and them so they can't attack as you rise.","mechanics":"Sit up on one hip with your hand posted behind you. Your other hand frames in front (or controls their wrist). Your top leg is bent in front of you. Lift your hips off the mat, using the posted hand and the planted foot. Swing your other leg back through under you, landing it behind you in a stance. Stand up with your hands up.","defense":"They push you back down or shoot as you rise.","mistake":"Standing straight up with no post. You're unbalanced and exposed.","drill":"Technical stand-ups: 3 × 10 each side, then with a partner pushing lightly.","groups":["transitions","open","defence","mma"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Get Up","Stand Up in Base"],"rel":["stand_up","wall_walk","upkick","seated_guard"]}},{"id":"chair_sit_back_take","cat":"transition","name":"Chair Sit Back Take","tagline":"When they stand up from turtle, sit behind them and pull them down onto your lap.","tags":["Back Take","Turtle","Standing"],"objective":"Take the back of an opponent who is standing up from turtle.","mechanics":"With a seatbelt or body lock from behind, as they stand, put one foot behind their heel. Sit down behind them, pulling them back onto you as you go. As they land on your lap, put your hooks in.","defense":"They turn to face you as they stand, or step forward away from you.","mistake":"Sitting too far away. You must be close behind them.","drill":"Partner stands up from turtle; chair sit to back. 3 × 6.","groups":["transitions","back"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["back_take_turtle","seatbelt","back_control"]}},{"id":"crab_ride","cat":"position","name":"Crab Ride","tagline":"Your legs controlling their hips from behind while seated. A bridge to the back.","tags":["Back Take","Leg Control","Advanced"],"objective":"Control their hips from behind while sitting, so they can't turn into you, then take the back.","mechanics":"From behind and seated, hook your feet inside their thighs, knees out. Your hands control their hips or a leg. Follow them as they move, keeping your hooks. Move up their body into back control when they stop moving.","defense":"They turn into you or stand up and step away.","mistake":"Hooks too shallow. The hooks need to be deep inside the thighs.","drill":"Crab ride and follow: 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["transitions","back"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["berimbolo","back_control","leg_ride"]}},{"id":"berimbolo","cat":"transition","name":"Berimbolo","tagline":"Invert under them from De La Riva and come out on their back.","tags":["Back Take","De La Riva","Inversion"],"objective":"From De La Riva, roll under them and take their back.","mechanics":"From De La Riva, grip their belt or trousers. Off-balance them so they sit back. Roll over your shoulder, inverting, keeping the DLR hook. Your hips go under them and your legs follow them as they fall. Come out behind them and climb into back control.","defense":"They follow you and step over, or sit back hard.","mistake":"Losing the De La Riva hook as you invert.","drill":"Berimbolo steps slowly: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["transitions","gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["dlr_guard","kiss_of_the_dragon","back_control","inverted_guard"]}},{"id":"kiss_of_the_dragon","cat":"transition","name":"Kiss of the Dragon","tagline":"From reverse De La Riva, invert between their legs and come out on their back.","tags":["Back Take","Reverse De La Riva","Inversion"],"objective":"Invert under them from RDLR and take their back.","mechanics":"From reverse De La Riva, grip their far leg or belt. Invert, rolling over your shoulder, passing your head between their legs. Your RDLR hook follows them and you come up behind them. Climb into back control.","defense":"They pressure down onto you or step away.","mistake":"Inverting onto your neck. Use your shoulders.","drill":"Slow reps: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["transitions","gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["rdlr_guard","berimbolo","back_control"]}},{"id":"collar_drag","cat":"transition","name":"Collar Drag","tagline":"Pull their head past you by the collar and step to their back.","tags":["Gi","Back Take","Seated Guard"],"objective":"Use the collar grip to drag them forward and past you, then take the back.","mechanics":"From seated guard, grip their collar deep. Pull it down and to the side, toward the mat beside you, while you move your hips out the other way. Their head goes past you. Climb onto their back.","defense":"They posture up or turn into you.","mistake":"Pulling without moving your hips.","drill":"Seated guard collar drag: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["transitions","gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","rel":["arm_drag_back","collar_sleeve","back_control"]}},{"id":"imanari_roll","cat":"transition","name":"Imanari Roll","tagline":"Roll under a standing opponent and land in a leg entanglement.","tags":["Leg Entanglement","Rolling Entry","Advanced"],"objective":"Enter a leg entanglement from standing by rolling sideways under them.","mechanics":"From standing, step close to their lead leg. Drop and roll sideways across your back, swinging your legs around their lead leg. Land in ashi-garami or saddle. Attack the heel immediately.","defense":"They step back or sprawl onto you.","mistake":"Rolling from too far away.","drill":"Slow rolls on a soft mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["transitions","legs"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["heel_hook_inside","saddle","ashi_inside"]}},{"id":"distance_management","cat":"concept","name":"Distance Management","tagline":"Every position has a safe distance and a danger distance. Decide which one you're in.","tags":["Concept","Distance","Guard"],"objective":"Control how far apart you are, so you are close when you attack and out of reach when they do.","mechanics":"In open guard: far distance (feet on hips) is safe; close distance (chest to chest) favours the top player unless you have underhooks. Passing: get close and pin, or stay far and move fast — the middle distance is where you get caught. Standing: outside striking range or inside the clinch, never lingering at mid range.","defense":"Good opponents change the distance with grips and feints.","mistake":"Staying at the distance that suits your opponent.","drill":"Distance rounds: one player keeps distance, the other closes. 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["concepts"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["framing","guard_retention","footwork_striking"]}},{"id":"base_posture","cat":"concept","name":"Base & Posture","tagline":"Base is your balance; posture is your alignment. Lose either and you get swept or submitted.","tags":["Concept","Balance","Top"],"objective":"Keep a wide, stable base and an upright, aligned posture so you can't be swept or attacked.","mechanics":"Base: your points of contact (knees, feet, hands) spread wide to make a stable shape. Posture: your back straight, head up, hips forward. In guard, posture stops submissions; base stops sweeps. When they push you one way, widen your base in that direction.","defense":"They pull you to break posture and push you to break base.","mistake":"Reaching with your hands while your posture is broken.","drill":"Base drill: partner pushes and pulls you from guard while you keep base. 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["concepts"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["guard_bottom_closed_detail","hip_bump","kuzushi_application"]}},{"id":"inside_position","cat":"concept","name":"Inside Position","tagline":"Whoever has their limbs inside controls the exchange — arms in the clinch, knees in guard.","tags":["Concept","Underhooks","Leg Control"],"objective":"Win the inside position with your arms and legs, so you control their movement.","mechanics":"Arms: underhooks and inside ties beat overhooks and outside ties. Legs: your knee inside their legs in guard stops passes; your leg inside their legs in entanglements controls their knee. Hands: inside hand position in grip fighting gives you the first move.","defense":"They pummel back inside with arms or legs.","mistake":"Holding on to an outside grip because it feels strong.","drill":"Pummelling with arms and with knees: 3 × 1 minute each.","groups":["concepts"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["underhooks_pummel","ashi_inside","hand_fighting"]}},{"id":"breathing_relaxation","cat":"concept","name":"Breathing & Relaxation","tagline":"Tension burns energy. Breathe out, stay calm, and move when it matters.","tags":["Concept","Endurance","Survival"],"objective":"Stay relaxed under pressure so you don't waste energy and can think clearly.","mechanics":"Breathe out through your mouth when you exert, and keep breathing in bad positions. Relax the muscles you're not using. Use frames and bone structure rather than muscle. In bad positions, focus on survival steps one at a time instead of panicking.","defense":"Opponents use pressure and grips to make you tense and tire.","mistake":"Holding your breath during effort. You gas out quickly.","drill":"Bottom side control rounds: 2 minutes, only breathe and frame.","groups":["concepts","defence"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["back_survival","framing","fluid_efficiency"]}},{"id":"training_methods","cat":"concept","name":"Training Methods","tagline":"Drill it, test it in positional sparring, then use it live. Each step matters.","tags":["Concept","Training"],"objective":"Use the right training method for each stage of learning a technique.","mechanics":"Drilling: repeat the technique with a cooperative partner until it's smooth. Positional sparring: start in the position with a goal and resistance, so you learn timing. Flow rolling: light, continuous movement to connect techniques. Live sparring: full resistance to test it. Spend the most time on positional sparring for new techniques.","defense":"Not applicable — this is how you train.","mistake":"Only sparring live. You keep doing what you already know.","drill":"For each new technique: 10 minutes drilling, 10 minutes positional, then try it live.","groups":["concepts"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Drilling, Positional Sparring, Flow Rolling"],"rel":["randori","chain_attacks"]}},{"id":"leglock_rules","cat":"concept","name":"Leg Lock Rules by Ruleset","tagline":"Which leg locks are legal depends on the ruleset and your level. Know before you compete.","tags":["Rules","Leg Locks","Safety"],"objective":"Know which leg locks and positions are allowed where you compete.","mechanics":"ADCC and most no-gi submission events allow heel hooks and reaping at advanced levels. IBJJF: straight ankle locks are allowed for all; kneebars and toe holds from brown belt in gi (and in no-gi for adults at brown and black); heel hooks only in adult brown/black no-gi; reaping is penalised below that. NAGA and local events vary by division. Always check the current rulebook — rules change.","defense":"Not applicable — this is about rules.","mistake":"Assuming one rulebook applies everywhere.","drill":"Before every event: read the rulebook for your division.","groups":["legs","concepts"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["heel_hook_inside","kneebar","toe_hold","false_reap"]}},{"id":"grip_breaks","cat":"defence","name":"Grip Breaks","tagline":"Break their grip before they use it. Every gi exchange starts with grips.","tags":["Gi","Grip Fighting"],"objective":"Free yourself from their grips on your sleeves and collar, using your whole body rather than your fingers.","mechanics":"Sleeve grip: make a fist, turn your hand toward their thumb (the weak point of their grip) and pull sharply while pushing their wrist with your other hand. Collar grip: two hands on their wrist and posture back. Spider grips: circle your hand inside and pull, or put your knee against their foot and strip it.","defense":"They re-grip quickly or switch to another grip.","mistake":"Pulling against their four fingers. Break toward the thumb.","drill":"Grip fighting rounds: 1 minute, only grip and break. 5 rounds.","groups":["gi_guard","defence","concepts"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi","rel":["hand_fighting","kumi_kata","spider_guard"]}},{"id":"clock_choke","cat":"submission","name":"Clock Choke","tagline":"A collar choke on a turtled opponent. You walk around them like the hands of a clock.","tags":["Gi","Choke","Turtle"],"objective":"Choke a turtled opponent with a deep collar grip and your body weight.","mechanics":"From the side of a turtled opponent, reach your near arm under their neck and grip deep in their far collar. Put your chest on their back. Walk your legs around toward their head, keeping your weight on them, like the hands of a clock. The collar closes on their neck.","defense":"They turn into you or pull the collar grip down.","mistake":"A shallow collar grip. Without a deep grip the walk-around only drags them, it does not choke.","drill":"From turtle: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["headlock","transitions"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","rel":["turtle_top","kata_ha_jime","loop_choke"]}},{"id":"morote_gari","cat":"judo","name":"Morote-Gari","tagline":"Judo's double leg. Banned in IJF competition since 2013, still legal in sambo, BJJ and wrestling.","tags":["Judo","Te-Waza","Leg Grab"],"objective":"Take both legs and drive through so they fall backward.","mechanics":"Drop your level and step in deep, wrapping both arms behind their knees. Your shoulder drives into their hips or stomach. Pull the legs toward you and drive forward with your shoulder so they fall onto their back. It is the same technique as the wrestling double leg, recorded in the judo syllabus.","defense":"They sprawl, push your head down or counter with tawara-gaeshi.","mistake":"Shooting from too far away with no set-up, which gives them time to sprawl.","drill":"Penetration steps: 3 × 10, then 5 finishes on a crash mat.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Double-Arm Reap"],"rel":["double_leg","kuchiki_taoshi","kibisu_gaeshi"]}},{"id":"kuchiki_taoshi","cat":"judo","name":"Kuchiki-Taoshi","tagline":"Hold one leg behind the knee and push them over like a falling tree.","tags":["Judo","Te-Waza","Leg Grab"],"objective":"Trap one leg behind the knee and push their upper body backward so they topple.","mechanics":"Grab behind their knee with one hand and pull the leg up toward you. Push their upper body backward with your other hand on their chest or lapel. With one leg off the mat and their weight pushed back, they fall like a tree. It is banned in IJF competition as a direct leg grab.","defense":"They hop and keep their weight forward, or sprawl the leg back.","mistake":"Pulling the leg without pushing the upper body.","drill":"Partner drill: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Single-Leg Takedown","Dead Tree Drop"],"rel":["single_leg_wrestling","morote_gari","kibisu_gaeshi"]}},{"id":"obi_otoshi","cat":"judo","name":"Obi-Otoshi","tagline":"Grab their belt from the side, lift and drop them backward.","tags":["Judo","Te-Waza","Belt Grip"],"objective":"Lift them by the belt and drop them backward over your leg.","mechanics":"Step to their side and grip the front of their belt with your hand, palm up. Put your other hand on their back or shoulder. Lift with the belt grip and push their upper body back. Step your leg behind theirs so they fall back over it.","defense":"They drop their weight, step around or turn to face you.","mistake":"Lifting with your arms alone. Use your legs and hips to lift.","drill":"Partner drill on a crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Belt Drop"],"rel":["ura_nage","ushiro_goshi"]}},{"id":"sukui_nage","cat":"judo","name":"Sukui-Nage","tagline":"Scoop their legs from behind and lift them off their feet.","tags":["Judo","Te-Waza","Lift"],"objective":"Get behind or beside them, scoop the backs of their legs and lift them backward.","mechanics":"Step behind or to the side of them. Reach across and scoop the backs of their legs or knees with one arm, while the other arm controls their upper body across the chest. Lift and tilt them backward off their feet. Lower them under control. Leg-grab versions are banned in IJF competition.","defense":"They turn to face you or drop their hips.","mistake":"Lifting with your back. Bend your knees and lift with your legs.","drill":"Crash mat only, slowly: 3 × 5. Partner breakfalls backward every rep.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Scooping Throw"],"rel":["ura_nage","ushiro_goshi","morote_gari"]}},{"id":"yama_arashi","cat":"judo","name":"Yama-Arashi","tagline":"A rare throw using a same-side lapel and sleeve grip, combining a hand pull with a leg sweep.","tags":["Judo","Te-Waza","Same-Side Grip"],"objective":"Turn in with a deep same-side lapel and sleeve grip, and sweep their leg while pulling them over.","mechanics":"Take their lapel and sleeve on the same side of their body. Turn in, pulling them forward and down, and sweep the outside of their leg with yours, close to harai-goshi. The same-side grip pulls their shoulder down while the sweep removes the leg.","defense":"They keep their weight back or step around.","mistake":"Turning in without the deep lapel grip.","drill":"Uchikomi: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Mountain Storm"],"rel":["harai_goshi","seoi_nage"]}},{"id":"tsuri_goshi","cat":"judo","name":"Tsuri-Goshi","tagline":"A hip throw with a belt grip that lifts them onto your hip.","tags":["Judo","Koshi-Waza","Belt Grip"],"objective":"Lift them by the belt onto your hip, then turn and throw.","mechanics":"Grip their belt at the back, either over their arm (o-tsuri) or under it (ko-tsuri). Turn in, bending your knees so your hips are below theirs. Lift with the belt grip as you straighten your legs, then turn and pull with the sleeve so they go over your hip.","defense":"They drop their weight, block your hip or step around.","mistake":"Not getting your hips low enough to lift.","drill":"Uchikomi: 3 × 10 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Lifting Hip Throw","O-Tsuri-Goshi","Ko-Tsuri-Goshi"],"rel":["o_goshi","tsurikomi_goshi"]}},{"id":"daki_age","cat":"judo","name":"Daki-Age","tagline":"Lifting an opponent from their guard. Listed in judo but not used to score, and slamming is illegal.","tags":["Judo","Lift","Not for Competition"],"objective":"Know what it is: lifting a guard player off the mat by standing up.","mechanics":"In the original syllabus, tori stands up from the opponent's guard, lifting them off the mat. In modern judo and BJJ, dropping or slamming someone from a lift is illegal and dangerous. Practically, standing up in closed guard to open it is a safe and useful skill; slamming is not.","defense":"They open their guard as you lift, or attack a triangle or armbar.","mistake":"Slamming. It is illegal and causes serious injuries.","drill":"Practise the standing guard break instead — never slams.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["High Lift"],"rel":["guard_closed"]}},{"id":"harai_tsurikomi_ashi","cat":"judo","name":"Harai-Tsurikomi-Ashi","tagline":"Sweep their foot up and around while lifting and pulling them forward.","tags":["Judo","Ashi-Waza","Foot Sweep"],"objective":"Pull them forward and up, then sweep the front of their lead ankle so they fall forward.","mechanics":"Lift and pull them forward with both hands so their weight moves onto their lead foot. Sweep the front of that ankle with the sole of your foot, carrying it forward and up. It is like sasae-tsurikomi-ashi, but you sweep rather than block.","defense":"They keep their weight back or step over the sweep.","mistake":"Sweeping with no lift. The pull and lift come first.","drill":"Moving uchikomi: 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Lift-Pull Foot Sweep"],"rel":["sasae_tsurikomi_ashi","de_ashi_harai"]}},{"id":"o_soto_guruma","cat":"judo","name":"O-Soto-Guruma","tagline":"Like o-soto-gari, but your leg sweeps behind both of their legs at once.","tags":["Judo","Ashi-Waza"],"objective":"Break their balance back and sweep both legs from behind with one leg.","mechanics":"Push them back onto their heels. Step in deep beside them and swing your leg behind both of their legs, at about knee height. Drive your upper body forward and down while your leg acts as a bar behind both of theirs. They fall back over it.","defense":"They step back out of the line or lean forward.","mistake":"Not stepping deep enough. The leg must reach behind both legs.","drill":"Uchikomi: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Large Outer Wheel"],"rel":["o_soto_gari","o_soto_otoshi"]}},{"id":"o_soto_otoshi","cat":"judo","name":"O-Soto-Otoshi","tagline":"Place your leg behind theirs and drop them back, rather than reaping.","tags":["Judo","Ashi-Waza"],"objective":"Block behind their leg and drive them back and down over it.","mechanics":"Push them back onto their heel. Step your leg behind theirs and plant it. Rather than reaping the leg up, drive your weight down and forward so they fall back over your planted leg.","defense":"They step back or keep their weight forward.","mistake":"Standing tall. Drive your weight down into them.","drill":"Uchikomi: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Large Outer Drop"],"rel":["o_soto_gari","o_soto_guruma"]}},{"id":"o_soto_gaeshi","cat":"judo","name":"O-Soto-Gaeshi","tagline":"They attack with o-soto-gari; you reap them back with your own.","tags":["Judo","Counter"],"objective":"Counter an o-soto-gari by reaping their supporting leg as they attack.","mechanics":"As they step in and swing their leg for o-soto-gari, drop your weight and keep your posture. Their reaping leg is off the mat. Pull them close and reap their standing leg with your own o-soto, driving them back.","defense":"They commit less, or chain to another throw.","mistake":"Reacting late, after their leg has reaped yours.","drill":"Counter drill: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Large Outer Counter"],"rel":["o_soto_gari","kaeshi_waza"]}},{"id":"o_uchi_gaeshi","cat":"judo","name":"O-Uchi-Gaeshi","tagline":"Pull your leg free from their o-uchi-gari and turn them over.","tags":["Judo","Counter"],"objective":"Counter o-uchi-gari by moving your reaped leg and twisting them to the mat.","mechanics":"As their leg hooks yours for o-uchi-gari, lift your leg out of the hook and step it around behind. At the same time, turn your upper body and pull them in the direction of their attack. They fall onto their side.","defense":"They hold the reap tight or chain into ko-uchi-gari.","mistake":"Trying to resist the reap with strength.","drill":"Counter drill: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Large Inner Counter"],"rel":["ouchi_gari","kaeshi_waza"]}},{"id":"ko_uchi_gaeshi","cat":"judo","name":"Ko-Uchi-Gaeshi","tagline":"Sweep their attacking foot along the path of their ko-uchi-gari.","tags":["Judo","Counter"],"objective":"Counter ko-uchi-gari by sweeping their attacking foot as it reaches for yours.","mechanics":"As they reach for your foot with ko-uchi-gari, lift your foot slightly so it doesn't get reaped. Sweep their attacking foot in the same direction it's moving, while turning them with your hands. They fall onto their side.","defense":"They keep the reap short and fast.","mistake":"Lifting your foot too high and losing balance.","drill":"Counter drill: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Small Inner Counter"],"rel":["ko_uchi_gari","kaeshi_waza"]}},{"id":"tsubame_gaeshi","cat":"judo","name":"Tsubame-Gaeshi","tagline":"Dodge their foot sweep and sweep them back with the same foot.","tags":["Judo","Counter","Foot Sweep"],"objective":"Avoid a foot sweep by lifting your foot, then use that same foot to sweep their leg.","mechanics":"As they sweep your foot with de-ashi-harai, lift your foot over their sweep like a swallow dipping. Bring the foot down and sweep their sweeping leg or their supporting foot.","defense":"They sweep fast and recover their foot.","mistake":"Lifting your foot late, after their sweep has already landed.","drill":"Partner sweeps slowly: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Swallow Counter"],"rel":["de_ashi_harai","kaeshi_waza"]}},{"id":"uchi_mata_gaeshi","cat":"judo","name":"Uchi-Mata-Gaeshi","tagline":"Lift them when they attack with uchi-mata, and turn them over.","tags":["Judo","Counter"],"objective":"Counter uchi-mata by lifting their sweeping leg and turning them backward.","mechanics":"As their leg sweeps between yours, drop your hips and catch them. Lift their sweeping leg with your leg or hip and turn your body, pulling them back. They fall onto their back.","defense":"They attack with uchi-mata faster or from a different angle.","mistake":"Standing tall as they attack.","drill":"Counter drill: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Inner Thigh Counter"],"rel":["uchi_mata","uchi_mata_sukashi","kaeshi_waza"]}},{"id":"uchi_mata_sukashi","cat":"judo","name":"Uchi-Mata-Sukashi","tagline":"Slide your leg away from their uchi-mata so they sweep air, then turn them over.","tags":["Judo","Counter","Evasion"],"objective":"Evade uchi-mata by moving your leg out of the way, then throw them with your hands.","mechanics":"As their leg comes up between yours, step your inside leg back out of the way. Their sweep misses and they are off balance. Turn your upper body and pull them in the direction they were throwing. They fall forward.","defense":"They attack with less commitment, or chain to another throw.","mistake":"Moving the leg too early.","drill":"Counter drill: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Inner Thigh Evasion"],"rel":["uchi_mata","uchi_mata_gaeshi"]}},{"id":"harai_goshi_gaeshi","cat":"judo","name":"Harai-Goshi-Gaeshi","tagline":"Counter harai-goshi by sweeping their supporting leg.","tags":["Judo","Counter"],"objective":"When they attack with harai-goshi, sweep their standing leg and throw them back.","mechanics":"As they turn in and sweep, drop your hips to stop the throw. Their weight is on their supporting leg. Sweep that leg with your own leg from behind while turning them backward.","defense":"They sweep faster or turn in deeper.","mistake":"Trying it without stopping their throw first.","drill":"Counter drill: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Sweeping Hip Counter"],"rel":["harai_goshi","kaeshi_waza"]}},{"id":"hane_goshi_gaeshi","cat":"judo","name":"Hane-Goshi-Gaeshi","tagline":"Block their hane-goshi and spring them back with your own.","tags":["Judo","Counter"],"objective":"Counter hane-goshi by blocking it and throwing with your own spring hip in the other direction.","mechanics":"As they attack with hane-goshi, drop your hips and stop their turn. Turn in yourself and spring your bent leg into their supporting leg, throwing them back.","defense":"They chain to another throw.","mistake":"Waiting too long after blocking.","drill":"Counter drill: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Spring Hip Counter"],"rel":["hane_goshi","kaeshi_waza"]}},{"id":"tawara_gaeshi","cat":"judo","name":"Tawara-Gaeshi","tagline":"They shoot a double leg; you wrap their back and roll them over you. Great against wrestlers.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Takedown Defence"],"objective":"Counter a low leg attack by wrapping over their back and rolling backward so they go over you.","mechanics":"As they shoot low, sprawl slightly and wrap both arms around their waist from above, locking your hands. Pull them tight to your chest. Fall back onto your back, lifting them with your arms and rolling backward. They go over your head. Roll with them to come out on top.","defense":"They keep their head up and drive forward, or switch to a single leg.","mistake":"Falling back without a tight lock.","drill":"Partner shoots slowly; tawara-gaeshi on a crash mat. 3 × 5.","groups":["judo","standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Rice Bag Reversal"],"rel":["sprawl","double_leg","morote_gari"]}},{"id":"daki_wakare","cat":"judo","name":"Daki-Wakare","tagline":"Lift a turtled or bent-over opponent from the front and throw them sideways.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Turtle"],"objective":"From in front of a bent-over or turtled opponent, wrap their waist and roll to the side, throwing them.","mechanics":"From the front of a bent-over opponent, reach over their back and wrap your arms around their waist. Lift them and fall to your side, rolling them over you sideways. Come out on top.","defense":"They drop their weight or come up to face you.","mistake":"A loose grip around the waist.","drill":"Crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo","headlock"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["High Separation"],"rel":["turtle_top","tawara_gaeshi"]}},{"id":"uki_waza","cat":"judo","name":"Uki-Waza","tagline":"Fall to your side with your leg extended as a block. They float over it.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Side"],"objective":"Pull them forward and to the side and throw by falling sideways with your leg blocking theirs.","mechanics":"As they step forward, pull them strongly to their front corner. Extend your leg across in front of their foot and fall to your side. They trip over your leg and roll over you.","defense":"They keep their weight back or step over your leg.","mistake":"Falling before you pull them forward.","drill":"Crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Floating Technique"],"rel":["yoko_otoshi","sumi_gaeshi"]}},{"id":"yoko_otoshi","cat":"judo","name":"Yoko-Otoshi","tagline":"Slide your leg to the outside of their foot and drop to your side.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Side"],"objective":"Throw them sideways by falling with your leg blocking the outside of their foot.","mechanics":"Pull them to the side so their weight is on one foot. Slide your leg to the outside of that foot and drop to your side, pulling them with you. They fall over your leg.","defense":"They keep their weight centred.","mistake":"Falling too far away from them.","drill":"Crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Side Drop"],"rel":["uki_waza","tani_otoshi"]}},{"id":"yoko_gake","cat":"judo","name":"Yoko-Gake","tagline":"Sweep their foot as you fall to your side, so they go down with you.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Side"],"objective":"Pull them to the side and sweep their foot as you drop.","mechanics":"Pull them to their side so their weight is on the outside foot. Sweep that foot with your foot, falling to your side at the same time. They fall onto their side.","defense":"They step their weight back to the other foot.","mistake":"Sweeping without the pull.","drill":"Crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Side Hook"],"rel":["de_ashi_harai","yoko_otoshi"]}},{"id":"yoko_guruma","cat":"judo","name":"Yoko-Guruma","tagline":"When they bend forward, slide between their legs and roll them over you.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Counter"],"objective":"Counter a forward-bent opponent by sliding your body between their legs and rolling.","mechanics":"When they bend forward or turn in for a throw, wrap one arm around their waist. Slide your leg and body between their legs and fall to your side. Roll them over you sideways.","defense":"They straighten up or step away.","mistake":"Sliding in without a waist grip.","drill":"Crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Side Wheel"],"rel":["ura_nage","tani_otoshi"]}},{"id":"yoko_wakare","cat":"judo","name":"Yoko-Wakare","tagline":"Throw yourself across in front of them so they fall over your body.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Side"],"objective":"Pull them forward and throw yourself sideways across their front so they fall over you.","mechanics":"Pull them forward and down. Throw your body across in front of their feet, landing on your side with your legs extended. They fall over your body.","defense":"They keep their weight back or step over you.","mistake":"Throwing yourself too early.","drill":"Crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Side Separation"],"rel":["uki_waza","yoko_otoshi"]}},{"id":"o_soto_makikomi","cat":"judo","name":"O-Soto-Makikomi","tagline":"An o-soto-gari that becomes a wrap and roll when they block it.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Wrap"],"objective":"Wrap their arm and roll into an o-soto when the standing reap is blocked.","mechanics":"Start o-soto-gari. As they block, wrap their arm under your armpit and keep reaping as you fall, turning so your body weight takes them down. Land on top.","defense":"They pull their arm free.","mistake":"Releasing the wrapped arm as you fall, so you land alone.","drill":"Crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Large Outer Wrap"],"rel":["o_soto_gari","soto_makikomi"]}},{"id":"uchi_makikomi","cat":"judo","name":"Uchi-Makikomi","tagline":"Wrap their arm and spin inward, falling forward so they roll over you.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Wrap"],"objective":"Wrap their arm inward against your body and fall forward, rolling them over you.","mechanics":"Hold their sleeve. Turn inward, trapping their arm under your armpit. Drop forward to the mat, rolling your whole body. They roll over your shoulder and back.","defense":"They pull the arm out or sprawl.","mistake":"Losing the arm wrap halfway through the roll.","drill":"Crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Inner Wrap"],"rel":["soto_makikomi","seoi_nage"]}},{"id":"harai_makikomi","cat":"judo","name":"Harai-Makikomi","tagline":"A harai-goshi that wraps and rolls when they resist the throw.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Wrap"],"objective":"Wrap their arm and continue the harai-goshi sweep into a rolling fall.","mechanics":"Start harai-goshi. Release your lapel grip and wrap their arm with your free arm. Keep sweeping and fall forward, rolling your body so they go over you.","defense":"They drop their hips and pull their arm out.","mistake":"Falling without sweeping.","drill":"Crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Sweeping Wrap"],"rel":["harai_goshi","soto_makikomi"]}},{"id":"hane_makikomi","cat":"judo","name":"Hane-Makikomi","tagline":"A hane-goshi that wraps and rolls.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Wrap"],"objective":"Wrap their arm and continue a hane-goshi into a rolling fall.","mechanics":"Start hane-goshi. Release your lapel grip, wrap their arm under your armpit and keep springing your leg into theirs as you fall forward and roll.","defense":"They pull the arm out and drop their hips.","mistake":"Losing the arm wrap, so they post and stop the roll.","drill":"Crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Springing Wrap"],"rel":["hane_goshi","harai_makikomi"]}},{"id":"uchi_mata_makikomi","cat":"judo","name":"Uchi-Mata-Makikomi","tagline":"An uchi-mata that wraps and rolls when they resist.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice","Wrap"],"objective":"Wrap their arm and continue uchi-mata into a rolling fall.","mechanics":"Start uchi-mata. Release your lapel grip, wrap their arm under your armpit and keep lifting with your leg between theirs as you fall forward and roll.","defense":"They drop their hips and pull the arm out.","mistake":"Falling with your leg not between theirs.","drill":"Crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Inner Thigh Wrap"],"rel":["uchi_mata","harai_makikomi"]}},{"id":"ko_uchi_makikomi","cat":"judo","name":"Ko-Uchi-Makikomi","tagline":"A ko-uchi-gari where you drop your weight and wrap, falling onto them.","tags":["Judo","Sacrifice"],"objective":"Reap their foot from inside while dropping your body weight onto them.","mechanics":"Grip their sleeve and wrap their arm. Reap their foot from inside with ko-uchi-gari, dropping your weight forward onto them as you go. They fall backward with you on top. Versions that grab the leg are banned in IJF competition.","defense":"They step their foot away.","mistake":"Reaping without dropping your weight.","drill":"Crash mat: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Small Inner Wrap"],"rel":["ko_uchi_gari"]}},{"id":"kani_basami","cat":"judo","name":"Kani-Basami","tagline":"A scissor throw with both legs. Banned in judo and many other sports because of serious knee injuries.","tags":["Judo","Banned","Safety"],"objective":"Know it, recognise it, and don't use it in training or competition.","mechanics":"The thrower jumps and scissors the opponent's legs from the side, one leg in front and one behind, and twists to the mat. The opponent's knee is easily trapped and injured when they fall. It is prohibited in IJF judo, IBJJF and most grappling rulesets.","defense":"Not applicable. It is banned for safety.","mistake":"Trying it. It has caused career-ending injuries.","drill":"None. This entry exists for reference only.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Flying Scissors"],"rel":["kawazu_gake"]}},{"id":"kawazu_gake","cat":"judo","name":"Kawazu-Gake","tagline":"Wrapping their leg and falling back. Banned in judo for safety.","tags":["Judo","Banned","Safety"],"objective":"Know it and recognise it, not use it.","mechanics":"The thrower wraps their leg around the opponent's leg from the outside and falls backward, pulling them down. The knee and ankle are twisted in the fall. It is prohibited in IJF judo.","defense":"Not applicable. It is banned for safety.","mistake":"Trying it in training. Knee and ankle injuries are common.","drill":"None. This entry exists for reference only.","groups":["judo"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Judo","aka":["One-Leg Entanglement"],"rel":["kani_basami"]}},{"id":"kata_gatame_pin","cat":"position","name":"Kata-Gatame (Shoulder Hold)","tagline":"A pin that traps their head and arm together. In BJJ the same shape becomes the arm triangle.","tags":["Judo","Pin"],"objective":"Pin them by trapping their head and one arm together.","mechanics":"From the side, push one of their arms across their face. Wrap your arm around their head and that arm, joining your hands. Press your head down against their arm, trapping it against their neck. Keep your body low and your legs wide.","defense":"They pull the arm out or turn toward you.","mistake":"Letting their arm slip out from under your head.","drill":"20-second holds: 5 rounds.","groups":["judo_ground","side"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Kata-Gatame Pin"],"rel":["arm_triangle","kesa_gatame","osaekomi_rules"]}},{"id":"uki_gatame","cat":"position","name":"Uki-Gatame","tagline":"A side hold with your knee on their body and their arm controlled — judo's take on knee on belly.","tags":["Judo","Pin"],"objective":"Pin them from the side with your knee on their body while you control their near arm.","mechanics":"From the side, place your knee across their stomach and post your other foot out for base. Control their near arm against your body and hold their collar or shoulder. Your weight goes through the knee.","defense":"They push your knee off and turn into you.","mistake":"Leaning your weight onto your hands instead of the knee.","drill":"20-second holds: 5 rounds.","groups":["judo_ground","side"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Judo","aka":["Floating Hold"],"rel":["knee_on_belly","yoko_shiho_gatame"]}},{"id":"gyaku_juji_jime","cat":"submission","name":"Gyaku-Juji-Jime","tagline":"The cross choke with both palms up, fingers inside the collar.","tags":["Gi","Choke","Judo"],"objective":"Choke them with a cross-collar grip where both palms face you.","mechanics":"Insert one hand deep into their collar, palm up, fingers inside. Insert the other hand into the other side of the collar, crossing over, palm up. Pull your elbows apart and down, bringing their head toward you. The nami version has both palms down; kata has one up and one down.","defense":"They push your elbows together or posture up.","mistake":"Shallow grips that sit on the lapels rather than behind the neck.","drill":"From guard and mount: 3 × 5.","groups":["judo_ground","closed","mount"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","aka":["Reverse Cross Choke"],"rel":["cross_collar_choke","kata_juji_jime"]}},{"id":"kata_juji_jime","cat":"submission","name":"Kata-Juji-Jime","tagline":"A cross choke with one palm up and one palm down. Very effective from mount.","tags":["Gi","Choke","Judo"],"objective":"Choke them with one hand palm up deep in the collar and the other palm down on the other side.","mechanics":"First hand palm up, deep into the collar. Second hand palm down (thumb inside) into the other side of the collar, crossing over the first. Drop your elbow toward the mat beside their head and pull. From mount, lean forward to the side of the second hand.","defense":"They push your elbows or bridge.","mistake":"Grips too shallow, so the collar never closes on the neck.","drill":"From mount: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo_ground","mount"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","aka":["Half Cross Choke"],"rel":["cross_collar_choke","gyaku_juji_jime"]}},{"id":"kata_te_jime","cat":"submission","name":"Kata-Te-Jime","tagline":"A one-hand collar choke. Your knuckles or forearm press into their neck.","tags":["Gi","Choke","Judo"],"objective":"Choke them with one deep collar grip, pressing the forearm or wrist across their neck.","mechanics":"Get one hand deep in their collar. Turn your wrist so your forearm or knuckles press against their neck. Pull and press with your body weight. Your other hand can push their head to tighten.","defense":"They turn their head toward the grip or push your elbow.","mistake":"No body weight behind it.","drill":"From guard or mount: 3 × 5.","groups":["judo_ground"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","aka":["One-Hand Choke"],"rel":["cross_collar_choke","ryo_te_jime"]}},{"id":"ryo_te_jime","cat":"submission","name":"Ryo-Te-Jime","tagline":"Both hands grip the collars from the front and pull together.","tags":["Gi","Choke","Judo"],"objective":"Choke them by pulling both sides of their collar together around the neck.","mechanics":"Grip each side of their collar with your thumbs inside, at the sides of their neck. Pull your hands together and toward you, closing the collar around their neck.","defense":"They break your grips or posture away.","mistake":"Gripping too low on the lapels.","drill":"From guard and mount: 3 × 5.","groups":["judo_ground"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","aka":["Two-Hand Choke"],"rel":["cross_collar_choke","kata_te_jime"]}},{"id":"tsukkomi_jime","cat":"submission","name":"Tsukkomi-Jime","tagline":"Push their own lapel across their throat.","tags":["Gi","Choke","Judo"],"objective":"Choke them by gripping their lapel and thrusting it into their throat.","mechanics":"Grip their lapel with one hand and pull it across. Push your fist and the lapel into their throat, while the other hand pulls the opposite lapel down to tighten.","defense":"They block your fist or turn away.","mistake":"Pushing on the chin instead of the throat.","drill":"From mount or guard: 3 × 5.","groups":["judo_ground"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi","aka":["Thrust Choke"],"rel":["ezekiel_choke","kata_te_jime"]}},{"id":"do_jime","cat":"submission","name":"Do-Jime","tagline":"Squeezing the body with your legs. Banned in judo; in BJJ the body triangle squeeze is legal.","tags":["Judo","Banned in Judo","Body Lock"],"objective":"Understand the squeeze: your legs compress their ribs and stomach.","mechanics":"Wrap your legs around their body and lock them, then squeeze. In judo it is prohibited. In BJJ and submission grappling, the body triangle from the back is legal and its squeeze can make opponents tap or tire.","defense":"They push your feet apart, breathe out and turn.","mistake":"Squeezing with crossed ankles — the attacker's ankles can be hurt by a counter.","drill":"Body triangle holds from the back: 5 rounds of 30 seconds.","groups":["judo_ground","back"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Trunk Squeeze","Body Triangle Squeeze"],"rel":["body_triangle","back_control"]}},{"id":"waki_gatame","cat":"submission","name":"Waki-Gatame","tagline":"Trap their straight arm under your armpit and turn. Falling into it is banned in judo competition.","tags":["Judo","Armlock","Standing"],"objective":"Lock their straight arm under your armpit and press against the elbow.","mechanics":"Grip their wrist. Trap their straight arm under your armpit, with the elbow pointing up. Lean your body weight down onto the elbow and turn slightly away. Do not fall to the mat with it — it injures the elbow and is prohibited in judo competition.","defense":"They bend the arm, turn into you or step around.","mistake":"Falling with the lock on.","drill":"From the knees, slowly: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo_ground","standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Armpit Armlock"],"rel":["ude_gatame","armbar"]}},{"id":"hara_gatame","cat":"submission","name":"Hara-Gatame","tagline":"Trap their arm against your stomach and press on the elbow.","tags":["Judo","Armlock"],"objective":"Trap their straight arm against your stomach and push your hips forward into the elbow.","mechanics":"Usually from the front of a turtled opponent. Trap their arm straight against your stomach, gripping the wrist. Press your hips forward into their elbow while pulling the wrist up.","defense":"They bend the arm or roll.","mistake":"Pressing with the arm bent.","drill":"Slowly from turtle: 3 × 5.","groups":["judo_ground","headlock"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Stomach Armlock"],"rel":["ude_gatame","waki_gatame"]}},{"id":"hiza_gatame","cat":"submission","name":"Hiza-Gatame","tagline":"Use your knee against their elbow to straighten the arm.","tags":["Judo","Armlock","Guard"],"objective":"Trap their straight arm and press your knee into the elbow.","mechanics":"From guard, trap their arm under your armpit, holding the wrist. Turn to the side and bring your knee against the outside of their elbow. Press the knee in while you pull the wrist.","defense":"They bend the arm or posture.","mistake":"Losing the wrist grip, so they bend the arm and pull it out.","drill":"From guard, slowly: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo_ground","closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Knee Armlock"],"rel":["ude_gatame","armbar"]}},{"id":"ashi_gatame","cat":"submission","name":"Ashi-Gatame","tagline":"Lock their arm straight using your leg over the elbow.","tags":["Judo","Armlock"],"objective":"Trap their straight arm and use your leg as the lever on the elbow.","mechanics":"From guard or the side, trap their wrist. Bring your leg over their arm so the back of your knee or thigh presses on the outside of their elbow. Extend your leg while holding the wrist.","defense":"They bend the arm or step over.","mistake":"Pressing on the forearm instead of the elbow.","drill":"Slowly from guard: 3 × 5 each side. Partner taps early.","groups":["judo_ground","closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Leg Armlock"],"rel":["ude_gatame","hiza_gatame"]}},{"id":"te_gatame","cat":"submission","name":"Te-Gatame","tagline":"Straighten their arm with your hands alone and twist the elbow.","tags":["Judo","Armlock"],"objective":"Lock the straight arm using your hands to hold the wrist and press the elbow.","mechanics":"Grip their wrist and hold it against your body. Press against the outside of their elbow with your other hand or forearm. Turn your body to apply pressure.","defense":"They bend the arm or turn their elbow down toward the mat.","mistake":"Pressure in the wrong direction — the elbow must be turned against its bend.","drill":"Slowly from standing or kneeling: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo_ground"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Hand Armlock"],"rel":["ude_gatame","waki_gatame"]}},{"id":"sankaku_gatame","cat":"submission","name":"Sankaku-Gatame","tagline":"From a triangle lock, straighten the trapped arm for an armlock.","tags":["Judo","Armlock","Triangle"],"objective":"From a triangle, pull their trapped arm straight and lock the elbow.","mechanics":"With the triangle locked around their head and arm, grip their trapped wrist. Pull the arm straight across your body and lift your hips into the elbow.","defense":"They keep the arm bent and posture.","mistake":"Letting the triangle loosen while you go for the arm.","drill":"From the triangle: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["judo_ground"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Triangle Armlock"],"rel":["triangle","judo_sankaku"]}},{"id":"inside_trip","cat":"takedown","name":"Inside Trip","tagline":"Hook inside their leg from the clinch and drive them back over it.","tags":["Takedown","Clinch","Body Lock"],"objective":"From a body lock or over-under, hook the inside of their leg and drive them backward.","mechanics":"From a clinch, step close so your hips are against theirs. Hook your leg around the inside of their leg, behind the knee or calf. Drive your chest and head forward into them while pulling the hooked leg toward you. They fall back. Follow them down chest to chest.","defense":"They step the leg away, widen their stance, or drive back into you.","mistake":"Hooking from too far. Your hips must be tight to theirs.","drill":"From over-under: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["ouchi_gari","body_lock_takedown","outside_trip"]}},{"id":"outside_trip","cat":"takedown","name":"Outside Trip","tagline":"Step behind their leg from the outside and drive them back over it.","tags":["Takedown","Clinch","Body Lock"],"objective":"From a clinch, step your leg behind theirs on the outside and push them back.","mechanics":"From a body lock or underhook, step to the outside of their leg and place your leg behind theirs. Turn your upper body and drive your chest into them, pushing them back over your leg. Follow them down.","defense":"They step back or circle away.","mistake":"Standing upright as you trip. Lean your weight into them.","drill":"From body lock: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["o_soto_gari","inside_trip","body_lock_takedown"]}},{"id":"back_body_lock_trip","cat":"takedown","name":"Back Body Lock Takedowns","tagline":"From behind, trip or lift them to the mat and land on their back.","tags":["Takedown","Back","Body Lock"],"objective":"From a standing rear body lock, take them down safely and keep the back.","mechanics":"Lock your hands around their waist from behind, head tight to their back. To trip, step your leg behind and outside theirs, and sit to the side, pulling them down over your leg. To mat-return, lift with your hips and drop them to the side. Insert hooks as you land. Never lift and drop someone on their head.","defense":"They peel your grip, sit down, or turn to face you.","mistake":"A loose lock around their waist.","drill":"Rear body lock trips: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["standing","back"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Rear Body Lock Trip","Mat Return"],"rel":["mat_return","spin_behind","back_control"]}},{"id":"suplex","cat":"takedown","name":"Suplex","tagline":"An arching throw from a body lock. Spectacular and dangerous — only with a trained partner and a crash mat.","tags":["Wrestling","Throw","Safety"],"objective":"Lift them off their feet from a body lock and arch backward to throw them over you.","mechanics":"Lock your hands around their waist (front or back). Drop your hips under theirs and lift them off the mat with your legs and hips. Arch your back and turn as you go over, so they land on their side or back — not their head. Many rulesets ban slamming or spiking an opponent.","defense":"They sprawl, sit down or post their legs wide.","mistake":"Throwing straight back over your head. That lands them on their neck. Turn the throw.","drill":"Only under a coach, with a crash mat: 3 × 3.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Wrestling","aka":["Belly-to-Belly","Back Arch Throw"],"rel":["lateral_drop","back_body_lock_trip","ura_nage"]}},{"id":"folding_pass","cat":"pass","name":"Folding Pass","tagline":"Fold their legs up toward their chest and walk around them.","tags":["Passing","Pressure"],"objective":"Compress their legs together and toward their chest so they can't move them, then pass.","mechanics":"Get both of their legs together. Push their knees toward their chest with your chest or shoulder. Their hips lift off the mat. Walk your feet around to the side and settle into side control as their legs drop.","defense":"They turn and push your head or recover a leg inside.","mistake":"Letting their hips stay on the mat.","drill":"Folding pass: 3 × 6 each side.","groups":["passing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["double_under","smash_pass","leg_weave_pass"]}},{"id":"single_under_pass","cat":"pass","name":"Single Under Pass","tagline":"One arm under a leg, stack it up, and pass to the other side.","tags":["Passing","Pressure"],"objective":"Lift one of their legs on your shoulder and pass to the opposite side.","mechanics":"Put one arm under their leg, lifting it toward their head. Your other arm controls their far hip or pants. Stack their weight onto their shoulders. Pass to the side opposite the lifted leg and settle in side control.","defense":"They triangle you, or turn and recover guard.","mistake":"Passing to the same side as the lifted leg — the triangle is waiting.","drill":"Single under pass: 3 × 6 each side.","groups":["passing"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["over_under","double_under"]}},{"id":"float_pass","cat":"pass","name":"Float Pass","tagline":"Float your hips over their legs from half guard while keeping chest pressure.","tags":["Passing","Half Guard","Pressure"],"objective":"From half guard top, keep your chest on them and float your hips over their legs to free your leg.","mechanics":"With an underhook and crossface, keep your chest heavy on theirs. Lift your hips and float them over their legs, using your hands for balance. As you float, free your trapped leg and settle into side control or mount.","defense":"They hold your leg tight or recover a knee shield.","mistake":"Lifting your chest along with your hips.","drill":"From half guard top: 3 × 6 each side.","groups":["passing","half"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["half_guard_top","smash_pass"]}},{"id":"lumberjack_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"Lumberjack Sweep","tagline":"When they stand up in your guard, grab both ankles and push them over.","tags":["Sweep","Standing Opponent"],"objective":"Sweep an opponent who stands up in your guard by grabbing both ankles and pushing their hips.","mechanics":"When they stand in your closed guard, open your legs and grab both of their ankles from behind. Pull the ankles toward you and push your hips and knees into their hips. They fall backward. Sit up and follow them to mount.","defense":"They keep their weight forward or step back.","mistake":"Grabbing the ankles without pushing the hips.","drill":"Partner stands in your guard: 3 × 8.","groups":["closed","gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Double Ankle Grab Sweep"],"rel":["guard_closed","standing_guard_break","double_ankle_sweep"]}},{"id":"double_ankle_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"Double Ankle Sweep","tagline":"Feet on their hips, hands on both ankles, push them over.","tags":["Open Guard","Sweep"],"objective":"From open guard, hold both ankles and push their hips back so they fall.","mechanics":"With your feet on their hips, grab both ankles. Pull the ankles toward you and extend your legs, pushing their hips back. They fall. Come up on top.","defense":"They step back or lean forward.","mistake":"Pushing without pulling the ankles.","drill":"Double ankle sweep: 3 × 8.","groups":["open"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["lumberjack_sweep","tripod_sweep"]}},{"id":"john_wayne_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"John Wayne Sweep","tagline":"Underhook their leg from half guard and roll them over the top of you.","tags":["Half Guard","Sweep"],"objective":"From half guard, underhook their far leg and roll them over your body to the far side.","mechanics":"From half guard with an underhook on their body, reach and underhook their far leg too. Roll toward your underhook side, lifting their leg and rolling them over you. Come out on top.","defense":"They base out wide or crossface you down.","mistake":"Rolling without the leg underhook.","drill":"John Wayne sweep: 3 × 6 each side.","groups":["half"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["half_guard_bottom","old_school"]}},{"id":"omoplata_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"Omoplata Sweep","tagline":"When they roll out of the omoplata, follow them and come up on top.","tags":["Sweep","Omoplata"],"objective":"Turn an omoplata they defend by rolling into a sweep to the top position.","mechanics":"From the omoplata, if they posture or roll forward, reach over their back to the far hip. Sit up and drive your weight forward, rolling them over their trapped shoulder. Land on top in side control.","defense":"They posture and step around before you sit up.","mistake":"Staying flat on your back.","drill":"From omoplata: 3 × 6 each side.","groups":["closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["omoplata","flower_sweep"]}},{"id":"knee_tap_sweep","cat":"sweep","name":"Knee Tap Sweep","tagline":"From seated guard, block their knee and pull them over it.","tags":["Seated Guard","Sweep"],"objective":"Sweep a standing opponent from seated guard by blocking their knee and pulling their upper body.","mechanics":"From seated guard, grip their collar, sleeve or behind the neck. Put your hand on the outside of their knee. Pull their upper body across while blocking the knee. They fall to the side. Come up on top.","defense":"They step the leg back or sprawl.","mistake":"Blocking the knee without pulling.","drill":"From seated guard: 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["open"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["seated_guard","wrestle_up","knee_tap"]}},{"id":"squid_guard","cat":"position","name":"Squid Guard","tagline":"Their lapel wrapped around their arm and held by your foot. A lapel guard for the spider game.","tags":["Gi","Lapel","Advanced"],"objective":"Control their arm with their own lapel to off-balance them and sweep.","mechanics":"Pull their lapel out and wrap it around their arm, then hook it with your foot. Your foot pushes on their bicep with the lapel locked. Use the control to off-balance them and sweep.","defense":"They keep their lapel tucked or break the grip early.","mistake":"A loose lapel wrap that slides off the arm.","drill":"Squid guard set-up: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["gi_guard"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi","rel":["worm_guard","lasso_guard"]}},{"id":"backside_fifty","cat":"position","name":"Backside 50/50","tagline":"A 50/50 where they've turned away. Their heel is exposed and their back may be too.","tags":["Leg Entanglement","Advanced"],"objective":"Control them when they turn away in 50/50, attacking the heel or the back.","mechanics":"When they turn their back in 50/50, keep the leg entanglement. Their heel is exposed. Grip it for a heel hook, or come up toward their back.","defense":"They turn back toward you or free their leg.","mistake":"Letting the entanglement loosen.","drill":"From 50/50, partner turns away: 3 × 5.","groups":["legs"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["fifty_fifty","heel_hook_inside"]}},{"id":"schultz_front_headlock","cat":"position","name":"Schultz Front Headlock","tagline":"A front headlock with your arm across their face and their arm controlled. Strong control, many attacks.","tags":["Front Headlock","Control"],"objective":"Control a turtled or bent-over opponent's head and arm tightly from the front.","mechanics":"From the front, wrap one arm around their head with the forearm across their face. Control their arm on that side with your other hand. Keep your chest heavy on their head. From here, attack chokes or go behind.","defense":"They post their head up or shoot for your legs.","mistake":"Light chest pressure, letting them posture.","drill":"From a front headlock: hold for 30 seconds, 5 rounds.","groups":["headlock"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["front_headlock_td","high_elbow_guillotine","darce"]}},{"id":"mir_lock","cat":"submission","name":"Mir Lock","tagline":"A figure-four shoulder lock with your grip on your own forearm, behind their arm.","tags":["Shoulder Lock","Kimura Variation"],"objective":"Lock their arm in a figure-four that rotates the shoulder, when the normal kimura grip isn't available.","mechanics":"From a top position, wrap your arm around their arm and grab your own forearm or bicep, forming a figure-four behind their elbow. Lift their elbow while their wrist stays down, rotating the shoulder.","defense":"They straighten their arm or turn into you.","mistake":"Applying it fast. Shoulder locks give little warning before damage.","drill":"From top: 3 × 3 each side, slowly.","groups":["mount","side","closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["kimura","americana"]}},{"id":"bulldog_choke","cat":"submission","name":"Bulldog Choke","tagline":"A headlock choke from the side, squeezing their head into your chest.","tags":["Choke","Headlock"],"objective":"Choke them with your arm around their neck from the side, compressing against your chest.","mechanics":"From the side of a turtled or kneeling opponent, wrap your arm around their neck. Grip your own hands. Pull their head into your chest and squeeze, pressing your forearm into the side of their neck.","defense":"They turn into you or put their hands between your arm and neck.","mistake":"Squeezing the jaw instead of the neck.","drill":"From the side of turtle: 3 × 5 each side.","groups":["headlock","side"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["front_headlock_td","guillotine"]}},{"id":"can_opener","cat":"submission","name":"Can Opener","tagline":"Pulling the head down in closed guard. A neck crank — illegal in IBJJF and most beginner rules.","tags":["Neck Crank","Illegal in Many Rulesets"],"objective":"Know what it is and why it's banned, and defend it.","mechanics":"The top player in closed guard puts both hands behind the bottom player's head and pulls it toward their chest, cranking the neck, to force the guard open. It is illegal in IBJJF and most rulesets. It is listed so you recognise it and protect your neck.","defense":"The bottom player opens their guard, frames on the top player's hips and gets their head back on the mat.","mistake":"Using it in training without permission. Neck injuries are serious.","drill":"Defence only: recognise the grip and open the guard. 3 × 5.","groups":["closed"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","aka":["Neck Crank from Guard"],"rel":["guard_closed","standing_guard_break"]}},{"id":"suloev_stretch","cat":"submission","name":"Suloev Stretch","tagline":"A hamstring and knee stretch from the back when they stand or tripod.","tags":["Leg Lock","Back","Advanced"],"objective":"From the back, trap their leg and stretch it when they try to stand.","mechanics":"From behind, as they stand or post a leg, hook your leg inside their leg. Push your hips forward and pull the leg up, stretching the hamstring and knee. Apply slowly.","defense":"They sit back down or free the leg.","mistake":"Applying it fast. The hamstring and knee tear before the pain warns them.","drill":"Slowly from back control: 3 × 3 each side.","groups":["back","legs"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"No-Gi","rel":["back_control","kneebar"]}},{"id":"flying_armbar","cat":"submission","name":"Flying Armbar","tagline":"Jump into an armbar from standing. Fast — and risky if it fails.","tags":["Armbar","Standing","Flying"],"objective":"From a grip on their arm, jump and lock an armbar before landing.","mechanics":"Grip their sleeve and collar or their wrist. Put one foot on their hip, jump and swing your other leg over their head. Lock your legs, lie back and finish the armbar. Land on your back, not your head. Banned in some beginner rulesets.","defense":"They pull the arm out, drop to their knees or stack you.","mistake":"Jumping without a strong grip on the arm.","drill":"With a coach, on a soft mat: 3 × 3 each side.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["armbar","flying_triangle"]}},{"id":"flying_triangle","cat":"submission","name":"Flying Triangle","tagline":"Jump into a triangle choke from standing. Catches people who stand upright.","tags":["Triangle","Standing","Flying"],"objective":"Jump and lock a triangle around their head and one arm.","mechanics":"Grip their collar or the back of their neck and one wrist. Jump, throwing one leg over their shoulder and around their neck while the other goes under their arm. Lock the triangle as you fall to guard. Finish from the bottom.","defense":"They pull the arm in and posture, or step back.","mistake":"Jumping without controlling one arm.","drill":"With a coach, on a soft mat: 3 × 3 each side.","groups":["standing"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Gi & No-Gi","rel":["triangle","flying_armbar"]}},{"id":"muay_thai_stance","cat":"concept","name":"Muay Thai Stance","tagline":"Tall and square, weight on the back leg. Built for kicking, checking kicks and the clinch.","tags":["Muay Thai","Stance","Foundation"],"objective":"Stand so your lead leg is light enough to check, teep or kick instantly, and your hands guard against punches and elbows.","mechanics":"Stand more upright and more square to your opponent than in boxing, feet about shoulder width. Most of your weight sits on your back leg, so your lead leg can lift quickly to check a kick or throw a teep. Hands are high, near your forehead, elbows in front of your body. Your chin stays down. Move with short steps and keep your hips square so both legs can kick.","defense":"Boxers punish an upright stance with straight punches and body shots; wrestlers shoot under it. Adjust your stance for the ruleset you fight under.","mistake":"Copying this stance straight into MMA. Its upright posture makes you easy to take down.","drill":"Shadowboxing in stance: 3 × 3 minutes. Lift the lead leg into a check every time a partner calls 'check'.","groups":["muay_thai"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Muay Thai","rel":["fighting_stance","checking_kicks","teep","long_guard"]}},{"id":"wai_kru","cat":"concept","name":"Wai Kru Ram Muay","tagline":"The pre-fight ritual: a bow of respect to your teachers, then a slow dance around the ring.","tags":["Muay Thai","Tradition","Ritual"],"objective":"Understand the tradition: showing respect to your teachers, your gym and the art before you fight.","mechanics":"Before a traditional fight, the fighter kneels and bows (the wai kru), paying respect to teachers and family. The ram muay is a slow, personal dance that often reflects the fighter's gym or teacher. Many fighters also wear a headband (mongkol) and armbands (prajiad) as part of the ritual. It's also a moment to focus, warm up and settle nerves.","defense":"Not applicable — this is tradition, not technique.","mistake":"Treating it as a performance to rush through. It is a sign of respect.","drill":"Learn your gym's version from your coach before your first fight.","groups":["muay_thai"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Muay Thai","aka":["Wai Kru","Ram Muay"],"rel":["muay_thai_stance","lethwei_ritual"]}},{"id":"muay_thai_scoring","cat":"concept","name":"How Muay Thai Is Scored","tagline":"Clean kicks, knees and balance win rounds. Punches that land matter less than in boxing.","tags":["Muay Thai","Rules","Strategy"],"objective":"Know what judges reward so you fight to win the scorecards, not just to land the most strikes.","mechanics":"Traditional fights are usually five rounds of three minutes. Judges reward clean, powerful strikes that have an effect — kicks and knees score well, especially when the opponent is off balance after them. Balance and composure matter: a fighter who looks unaffected and in control is seen as winning. Clinch dominance and sweeps that dump the opponent score. The early rounds are often slower; the later rounds usually decide the fight. Check the rules of each promotion — scoring varies.","defense":"Not applicable — this is about rules and strategy.","mistake":"Throwing lots of light punches. In Muay Thai, effective, clean strikes score; volume alone doesn't.","drill":"Watch a full traditional fight and score each round yourself before checking the result.","groups":["muay_thai"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Muay Thai","rel":["muay_thai_stance","teep","body_kick","clinch_fighting"]}},{"id":"long_guard","cat":"defence","name":"Long Guard","tagline":"Extend your lead arm into their face or shoulder to stop them coming forward.","tags":["Muay Thai","Defence","Distance"],"objective":"Keep them at a distance with an extended arm frame, so they can't throw elbows or hooks at close range.","mechanics":"Push your lead hand out toward their face, shoulder or chest, with the arm extended but not locked. Your rear hand stays high by your face. The extended arm blocks their line of sight and stops them stepping in. Use it to measure distance for your kicks, or to frame them away after a combination.","defense":"They hook around it, slap it down, or kick under it.","mistake":"Locking the elbow straight. A locked arm can be hyperextended and is easy to pull.","drill":"Partner walks forward; frame with the long guard and circle away. 3 × 2 minutes.","groups":["muay_thai"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Muay Thai","rel":["blocking_covering","muay_thai_stance","teep"]}},{"id":"switch_kick","cat":"strike","name":"Switch Kick","tagline":"Switch your feet quickly, then kick with the lead leg at full power.","tags":["Muay Thai","Kick","Lead Leg"],"objective":"Throw a powerful roundhouse with your lead leg by switching stance first.","mechanics":"Make a small, quick jump or step to swap your lead and rear feet. Your former lead leg is now behind, loaded to kick. Immediately turn your hips over and kick to the body or head with your shin. Keep your hands up during the switch. It's often aimed at the body on the open side when you're in opposite stances.","defense":"They time the switch and teep or punch while your feet are moving.","mistake":"A big, slow switch that tells them the kick is coming.","drill":"Switch kick on pads: 3 × 10 each side.","groups":["muay_thai","striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Muay Thai","rel":["body_kick","head_kick","teep"]}},{"id":"diagonal_knee","cat":"strike","name":"Diagonal Knee","tagline":"A knee driven up at an angle into the ribs. The main clinch weapon in Muay Thai.","tags":["Muay Thai","Knee","Clinch"],"objective":"Drive your knee diagonally into their side or ribs, from the clinch or at close range.","mechanics":"From the clinch, turn your hips slightly and drive your knee up and across at an angle into their ribs or stomach. Point your toes down and push your hips forward. Pull them into the knee with the clinch. Return your foot to the mat and keep your balance before throwing the next.","defense":"They block with their own knee, push your hip away, or turn you off balance.","mistake":"Kneeing with your hips back. Without the hip, the knee has no power.","drill":"Diagonal knees on a heavy bag: 3 × 20, alternating sides.","groups":["muay_thai","striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Muay Thai","aka":["Kao Chiang"],"rel":["straight_knee","clinch_fighting","thai_clinch"]}},{"id":"uppercut_elbow","cat":"strike","name":"Uppercut Elbow","tagline":"An elbow driven straight up through their guard to the chin.","tags":["Muay Thai","Elbow","Close Range"],"objective":"Strike up through the middle of their guard with the point of your elbow at very close range.","mechanics":"At close range, bend your arm fully and drive your elbow straight up, with the forearm vertical, through the gap between their hands to their chin. Bend your knees slightly and drive up with your legs. Keep your other hand up.","defense":"They lean back, cover tightly, or clinch.","mistake":"Throwing it from too far away. It only reaches at clinch range.","drill":"Pads held low and flat: 3 × 10 each side.","groups":["muay_thai","striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Muay Thai","aka":["Sok Ngat"],"rel":["horizontal_elbow","uppercut","chopping_elbow"]}},{"id":"chopping_elbow","cat":"strike","name":"Chopping Elbow","tagline":"An elbow brought down from above onto the head. It often cuts.","tags":["Muay Thai","Elbow","Cut"],"objective":"Strike down onto their head or brow with the point of your elbow when they lower their head.","mechanics":"Raise your elbow above shoulder height. Bring it down at an angle onto their forehead or brow, using your body weight and a slight drop of your knees. It is most effective when they duck or lean forward. Return to guard immediately.","defense":"They keep their head up, cover high, or tie up your arm.","mistake":"Lifting the elbow early so they see it coming.","drill":"Pads held flat at head height: 3 × 10 each side, dropping your knees slightly into each elbow.","groups":["muay_thai","striking"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Muay Thai","aka":["Downward Elbow (Standing)"],"rel":["horizontal_elbow","uppercut_elbow"]}},{"id":"clinch_fighting","cat":"position","name":"Clinch Fighting: Position, Knees and Turns","tagline":"In the Thai clinch you fight for inside position, land knees, and turn them off balance.","tags":["Muay Thai","Clinch"],"objective":"Win the inside position in the clinch so you can knee, turn and dump them while they can't do the same to you.","mechanics":"Pummel your hands inside theirs to get the double collar tie (plum) or an arm-and-neck tie. Keep your hips close and your posture upright. Pull their head down and to the side to break their posture. Land knees to the body. Turn them by stepping back and pulling one side of their neck while pushing the other. Break the clinch with a frame or elbow if you're losing it.","defense":"They swim inside, push your hips away, or knee first.","mistake":"Standing with your hips back. A hips-back clinch gives them the knees.","drill":"Clinch-only rounds: 3 × 2 minutes, score with knees and turns.","groups":["muay_thai"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Muay Thai","rel":["thai_clinch","diagonal_knee","clinch_dump","underhooks_pummel"]}},{"id":"clinch_dump","cat":"takedown","name":"Clinch Dump","tagline":"Turn them off balance in the clinch and dump them to the canvas.","tags":["Muay Thai","Clinch","Sweep"],"objective":"Use the clinch to move their weight onto one leg, then turn them so they fall.","mechanics":"From the clinch, step back and to the side, pulling their head and shoulder with you so their weight falls onto one foot. Place your knee or hip across their body as a block and keep turning. They lose balance and fall. In Muay Thai, judo-style hip throws are not allowed, but dumping an opponent by off-balancing is.","defense":"They keep a wide base, follow your steps, or knee as you turn.","mistake":"Pulling with your arms only. The turn comes from stepping and turning your body.","drill":"Clinch dump drill: 3 × 8 each side, slowly.","groups":["muay_thai","lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Muay Thai","aka":["Clinch Sweep","Off-Balance"],"rel":["clinch_fighting","catch_and_sweep","thai_clinch"]}},{"id":"catch_and_sweep","cat":"takedown","name":"Catch and Sweep","tagline":"Catch their body kick, then sweep the leg they're standing on.","tags":["Muay Thai","Counter","Sweep"],"objective":"Trap a kick against your body and sweep their standing leg so they fall.","mechanics":"As their kick lands on your body, wrap your arm around their leg and trap it against your side. Step to the outside of their standing leg. Sweep it with your leg or kick the standing leg while you push their upper body or lift the caught leg. They fall. You can also punch or kick while holding the leg, depending on the rules.","defense":"They pull the kick back quickly, or turn into a spinning back fist or elbow as you catch.","mistake":"Catching the kick with your hands out in front. Let it land, then trap it with your arm.","drill":"Partner throws slow body kicks: catch and sweep, 3 × 8 each side.","groups":["muay_thai","lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Muay Thai","aka":["Kick Catch"],"rel":["body_kick","checking_kicks","clinch_dump"]}},{"id":"counter_kick","cat":"strike","name":"Check and Counter Kick","tagline":"Check their kick, then kick back straight away on the same side.","tags":["Muay Thai","Counter","Kick"],"objective":"Turn their kick into your scoring chance by checking it and kicking back before they reset.","mechanics":"Lift your shin to check their low kick. As you put the leg down, plant it and throw your own kick straight back — usually a body kick or low kick with the other leg. Their leg is still returning and their guard is low on that side. Speed matters more than power.","defense":"They kick and step back out of range, or feint the kick to draw your counter.","mistake":"Pausing after the check. The counter must come immediately.","drill":"Partner kicks low; check and counter. 3 × 10 each side.","groups":["muay_thai"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Muay Thai","rel":["checking_kicks","body_kick","counterstriking"]}},{"id":"thai_pads","cat":"concept","name":"Training on Thai Pads","tagline":"The pad holder plays the opponent: they feed strikes, check and counter so you learn rhythm and timing.","tags":["Muay Thai","Training"],"objective":"Use pad rounds to build combinations, power, conditioning and reactions.","mechanics":"A good pad holder holds Thai pads on the forearms and a belly pad, calls combinations, and throws light kicks and punches back so you have to defend. Rounds are usually three minutes. Combine punches into kicks, knees and elbows, and finish each combination by resetting your stance. Pad holding is a skill too — it protects the kicker's shins and the holder's arms.","defense":"Not applicable — this is a training method.","mistake":"Hitting pads with no defence. If the pad holder never swings back, you build bad habits.","drill":"5 rounds of 3 minutes on Thai pads, 1 minute rest.","groups":["muay_thai"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Muay Thai","rel":["training_methods","muay_thai_stance"]}},{"id":"muay_thai_conditioning","cat":"concept","name":"Conditioning for Striking","tagline":"Running, bag rounds and gradual shin conditioning. Build it slowly, over months.","tags":["Muay Thai","Lethwei","Conditioning"],"objective":"Build the fitness and toughness to fight five rounds, without injuring yourself in training.","mechanics":"Traditional fighters run, skip rope and do many rounds on bags and pads. Shins toughen gradually through repeated, controlled kicking on heavy bags and pads — not by hitting hard objects. Core and neck strength protect against body shots and the clinch. Rest and recovery are part of conditioning.","defense":"Not applicable — this is a training method.","mistake":"Kicking trees, poles or other hard objects. It causes injuries, not toughness.","drill":"Three times a week: 5 rounds of bag work, 20 minutes of running or rope.","groups":["muay_thai","lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Muay Thai","rel":["thai_pads","checking_kicks"]}},{"id":"lethwei_rules","cat":"concept","name":"Lethwei: Rules and Nine Limbs","tagline":"Myanmar's bare-knuckle fighting art. Fists, elbows, knees, feet and the head are all weapons.","tags":["Lethwei","Myanmar","Rules"],"objective":"Understand what makes Lethwei unique: no gloves, headbutts allowed, and a tradition of winning only by knockout.","mechanics":"Lethwei is called the art of nine limbs: two fists, two elbows, two knees, two feet and the head. Fighters wrap their hands in gauze and tape instead of wearing gloves. Clinching, throws and sweeps are allowed. Under traditional rules, a fight is won only by knockout or when one fighter can't continue; if both are still standing, it's a draw. Traditional rules also allow an injury time-out so a hurt fighter can recover once. Some modern international promotions add judges' decisions — check the rules of each event.","defense":"Not applicable — this is about the art and its rules.","mistake":"Treating it as Muay Thai without gloves. Headbutts and bare knuckles change stance, defence and distance.","drill":"Watch traditional and modern Lethwei bouts and note how the rules change the fighting.","groups":["lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Lethwei","aka":["Burmese Boxing","Myanmar Traditional Boxing"],"rel":["lethwei_ritual","headbutt","bare_knuckle_punching","bando"]}},{"id":"lethwei_ritual","cat":"concept","name":"Lekkha Moun and Lethwei Yay","tagline":"The challenge and the dance. Lethwei fighters open each bout with traditional gestures of respect and challenge.","tags":["Lethwei","Myanmar","Tradition"],"objective":"Understand the tradition behind a Lethwei bout.","mechanics":"Before the fight, fighters perform the Lethwei Yay, a traditional dance. The Lekkha Moun is a gesture of challenge — the fighter slaps their arm or chest, inviting the opponent to fight. It can also be used during the bout to show the fighter is still ready and to encourage a passive opponent. Like the wai kru in Muay Thai, these rituals show respect for the art and its history.","defense":"Not applicable — this is tradition, not technique.","mistake":"Copying the gestures without understanding them. Learn them from a Lethwei teacher.","drill":"Learn the ritual from your coach before your first bout.","groups":["lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Lethwei","aka":["Lethwei Ritual"],"rel":["lethwei_rules","wai_kru"]}},{"id":"lethwei_stance","cat":"concept","name":"Lethwei Stance & Guard","tagline":"A tight guard and a controlled head. In Lethwei, the head is both a target and a weapon.","tags":["Lethwei","Stance","Headbutt Defence"],"objective":"Stand so you can strike with all nine limbs while protecting your face from bare fists, elbows and headbutts.","mechanics":"The stance is similar to Muay Thai — fairly upright, weight able to shift to the back leg for kicks and checks. Hands are high with forearms in front of your face, because without gloves a cover-up protects less. Keep your chin down and your forehead forward slightly, so if heads meet, your forehead meets their face rather than your face meeting their forehead. Avoid leaning your head forward into range carelessly.","defense":"Opponents use headbutts and clinch entries to break a stance that leans forward.","mistake":"Ducking your head low at close range. In Lethwei, that walks your face into knees and headbutts.","drill":"Shadowboxing in stance: 3 × 3 minutes, with head position checks from a partner.","groups":["lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Lethwei","rel":["muay_thai_stance","headbutt_defence","bare_knuckle_defence"]}},{"id":"bare_knuckle_punching","cat":"strike","name":"Bare-Knuckle Punching","tagline":"Without gloves, where you hit matters as much as how hard. Protect your hands.","tags":["Lethwei","Punching","Hand Safety"],"objective":"Punch effectively with bare, wrapped hands without breaking them.","mechanics":"Make a tight fist with your wrist straight, striking with the first two knuckles. Target soft and breakable areas: the jaw, nose, body and liver. Avoid punching the top of the skull and the forehead with your knuckles — it breaks hands; use elbows or hammer-type strikes for hard targets. Shorter, straighter punches are safer for the hands than wide swings. Hands are wrapped in gauze and tape, which supports the wrist and knuckles but doesn't pad them like a glove.","defense":"Opponents tuck their chin and present their forehead to make you punch hard bone.","mistake":"Throwing wide, looping punches at the head. They often land on the skull and break the hand.","drill":"Bag work with wraps only, light power: 3 × 2 minutes. Focus on knuckle alignment.","groups":["lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Lethwei","rel":["jab","cross","hook_punch","lethwei_rules"]}},{"id":"headbutt","cat":"strike","name":"Headbutt","tagline":"The ninth limb. A strike with the top of the forehead to the opponent's face, legal in Lethwei.","tags":["Lethwei","Head Strike","Close Range"],"objective":"Strike with the hard part of your forehead, close to the hairline, against their face when you're at close range.","mechanics":"At close range or as you step in, drive forward from your legs and hips, keeping your neck firm. Strike with the top of the forehead near the hairline, aiming at their nose, cheekbone or brow. Keep your hands up as you go in. Headbutts are often thrown as a surprise after a punch or as you enter the clinch. Train them on pads only — never full contact in training.","defense":"They tuck their chin, frame your head, or meet you forehead to forehead.","mistake":"Leading with your face or nose instead of the forehead. Also: training them on partners at speed.","drill":"Pads held at face height: 3 × 10, controlled. Never practise on a partner's head.","groups":["lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Lethwei","rel":["clinch_headbutt","headbutt_defence","lethwei_rules"]}},{"id":"clinch_headbutt","cat":"strike","name":"Clinch Headbutt","tagline":"Pull their head toward you in the clinch and meet it with your forehead.","tags":["Lethwei","Clinch","Head Strike"],"objective":"Use the clinch to control their head and land headbutts at the closest range.","mechanics":"From a collar tie or plum, pull their head toward you while you drive your forehead into their face. Keep your neck stiff and your chin tucked. Combine with knees to the body: when they bend to defend the knee, their face comes into range. Release and reset the clinch quickly.","defense":"They keep their head beside yours, pressing cheek to cheek, so there's no space for the headbutt.","mistake":"Pulling them in without tucking your own chin.","drill":"With a pad held at face height, from the clinch: 3 × 8, controlled.","groups":["lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"A","fmt":"Lethwei","rel":["headbutt","lethwei_clinch","thai_clinch"]}},{"id":"headbutt_defence","cat":"defence","name":"Headbutt Defence","tagline":"Keep your head beside theirs, chin tucked, and frame on their head when they lean in.","tags":["Lethwei","Defence","Clinch"],"objective":"Avoid taking headbutts at close range and in the clinch.","mechanics":"In the clinch, press the side of your head against the side of theirs, so there is no space to headbutt. Keep your chin tucked and your forehead forward. At close range, put a hand or forearm on their forehead or shoulder to stop them leaning in. Don't duck straight forward into the clinch.","defense":"They pull your head away to make space, then headbutt.","mistake":"Leaving space between your heads in the clinch.","drill":"Clinch rounds where the only goal is to keep your head beside theirs: 3 × 1 minute.","groups":["lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Lethwei","rel":["headbutt","clinch_headbutt","lethwei_stance"]}},{"id":"lethwei_clinch","cat":"position","name":"Lethwei Clinch","tagline":"A clinch with knees, elbows, headbutts and throws. More dangerous than in Muay Thai.","tags":["Lethwei","Clinch","Throws"],"objective":"Control the clinch so you can knee, headbutt and throw, while protecting yourself from the same.","mechanics":"Fight for inside position with your arms, like the Thai clinch. Keep your head beside theirs to stop headbutts. Land knees, short elbows and headbutts. Use your legs and hips to trip and throw — Lethwei allows throws and sweeps. Referees separate a stalled clinch quickly, so stay active.","defense":"They do the same: headbutt, knee and throw.","mistake":"Holding the clinch passively. It gets broken up and you've wasted energy.","drill":"Clinch rounds with pads for headbutts: 3 × 2 minutes.","groups":["lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Lethwei","rel":["clinch_headbutt","lethwei_throws","thai_clinch","diagonal_knee"]}},{"id":"lethwei_throws","cat":"takedown","name":"Throws and Sweeps in Lethwei","tagline":"Lethwei allows throws from the clinch. A fighter who can throw controls the clinch.","tags":["Lethwei","Throws","Clinch"],"objective":"Put them on the floor from the clinch to score dominance, tire them and reset the fight on your terms.","mechanics":"From the clinch, use trips and throws: an outside reap (like o-soto-gari), an inside trip, a hip turn, or a catch-and-sweep against a kick. Break their balance first by pulling their head and shoulder, then take the leg. There is no ground fighting, so the referee restarts the bout standing.","defense":"They keep a wide base, knee you as you set up, or headbutt as you pull.","mistake":"Throwing without breaking their balance first.","drill":"Clinch throws: 3 × 6 each side, on a soft mat.","groups":["lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Lethwei","rel":["lethwei_clinch","clinch_dump","o_soto_gari","inside_trip"]}},{"id":"bare_knuckle_defence","cat":"defence","name":"Defence Without Gloves","tagline":"Without gloves, covering up doesn't stop much. Parry, move and control distance.","tags":["Lethwei","Defence"],"objective":"Defend against bare-knuckle punches and elbows, which slip through a cover that would stop a gloved punch.","mechanics":"Parry punches with your hands rather than relying on covering. Block with your forearms and elbows. Move your head and control the distance with your feet and teeps. Covering up with both arms still protects briefly, but bare fists find gaps easily, so don't stay covered — move out or clinch.","defense":"Opponents use feints and combinations to get through your parries.","mistake":"Covering up and standing still, like you would with gloves.","drill":"Partner throws light punches with open hands; parry and move. 3 × 2 minutes.","groups":["lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"I","fmt":"Lethwei","rel":["blocking_covering","head_movement","lethwei_stance"]}},{"id":"bando","cat":"concept","name":"Bando and Banshay: Burmese Martial Roots","tagline":"Lethwei is one part of Myanmar's martial heritage, alongside the self-defence art Bando and the weapons art Banshay.","tags":["Myanmar","Tradition","History"],"objective":"Know where Lethwei sits in Myanmar's martial traditions.","mechanics":"Myanmar has several traditional martial arts. Lethwei is the competitive striking art. Bando is an unarmed self-defence system, often taught with animal-inspired styles. Banshay covers weapons such as the sword, staff and spear. Lethwei bouts were traditionally held at festivals and celebrations. CHINTHE, the guardian lion, comes from the same heritage.","defense":"Not applicable — this is history and context.","mistake":"Assuming all Burmese martial arts are the same. Each has its own purpose and methods.","drill":"Not a drill: read about and, if you can, visit a traditional Lethwei or Bando school.","groups":["lethwei"],"meta":{"lvl":"F","fmt":"Lethwei","rel":["lethwei_rules","lethwei_ritual"]}}]};
